\c 1
\s1 Alexandros' conquests and divided kingdom
\p
\v 1 After¦62193 Alexandros \add !(Alexander)\add* the¦62194 person from Makedonia, the¦62197 son of Filippos \add !(Philip)\add*, who¦62199 came out of the¦62204 land¦62205 of Kitim, and¦62207 struck¦62208 Dareyavesh \add !(Darius)\add* king¦62211 of the Persians and Madim \add !(Medes)\add*, it happened, after he'd¦62218 struck him, that¦62221 he reigned¦62216 in his place, in former time, over\f + \fr 1:1 \ft That is, the Greek Empire. Compare 1 Maccabees 1:10 and 1 Maccabees 6:2.\f* Yavan \add !(Greece)\add*.
\v 2 He fought¦62225 many battles, won many strongholds¦62229, killed the kings¦62233 of the¦62234 earth¦62235,
