\v 8 Her temple¦63354 has become like a man¦63357 who¦63353 was glorious.
\v 9 Her vessels¦63360 of glory¦63362 are carried away into¦63366 captivity. Her infants are slain in¦63370 her streets. Her young¦63374 men¦63374 are slain with the enemy's¦63378 sword¦63377.
\v 10 What¦63379 nation¦63380 hasn't inherited her palaces and¦63385 taken¦63387 possession of her spoils?
\v 11 Her adornment has all¦63391 been¦63398 taken away. Instead of a free woman, she's¦63394 become a slave.
\v 12 Listen, our holy¦63404 things, our beauty¦63408, and¦63410 our glory¦63412 are laid¦63414 waste¦63414. The¦63418 Gentiles have profaned them.
\v 13 Why¦63420 should we¦63421 live¦63423 any longer?”
\p
\v 14 Matityah \add !(Mattathias)\add* and his sons¦63428 tore¦63425 their clothes¦63431, put on sackcloth¦63435, and¦63436 mourned greatly.
\s1 Matityah refuses to obey the king
\p
