\v 17 The¦63473 king's¦63474 officers answered¦63470 and¦63475 spoke¦63479 to¦63476 Matityah, saying¦63476, “You're a ruler¦63480 and¦63481 an honourable¦63482 and¦63483 great¦63484 man in¦63486 this¦63487 city¦63488, and¦63490 strengthened with sons¦63493 and¦63494 kindred.
\v 18 Now¦63496 therefore¦63497 come¦63498 first¦63499 and¦63500 do¦63501 the¦63504 king's¦63505 commandment, as all¦63508 the¦63509 nations¦63510 have done, including¦63511 the¦63512 men¦63513 of Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add* and¦63515 those who¦63516 remain in¦63518 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*. You¦63522 and¦63523 your house¦63525 will be numbered among the¦63529 king's¦63530\f + \fr 2:18 \ft See 1 Maccabees 3:38; 10:10, etc.; Compare 1 Maccabees 10:65; 11:27; 2 Maccabees 8:9.\f* friends¦63528, and¦63531 you¦63532 and¦63533 your sons¦63535 will be honoured with silver and¦63539 gold¦63540 and¦63541 many gifts.”
\p
\v 19 And¦63544 Matityah replied¦63548 with a loud voice¦63549, “If¦63551 all¦63552 the¦63553 nations¦63554 that¦63555 are in¦63556 the house¦63557 of¦63560 the¦63560 king's¦63561 dominion listen¦63562 to¦63562 him, to¦63564 fall away¦63566 each¦63565 one from¦63566 the worship of his fathers¦63568, and¦63570 have made choice to follow his commandments¦63574,
\v 20 yet I¦63577 and¦63578 my sons¦63580 and¦63582 my kindred will walk in¦63587 the covenant¦63588 of our fathers¦63589.
\v 21 Far be it from us that we¦63592 should forsake the law¦63594 and¦63595 the ordinances.
\v 22 We won't listen¦63602 to the¦63599 king's¦63600 words¦63598, to turn aside from our worship, to¦63604 the¦63605 right¦63608 hand, or¦63609 to the left.”
