\v 23 When¦63611 he'd finished speaking¦63614 these words¦63616, a Yehudi \add !(Jew)\add* came¦63618 in¦63621 the sight of all¦63623 to sacrifice on the altar which¦63612 was at Modi'in, according¦63631 to¦63631 the¦63634 king's¦63635 commandment.
\v 24 Matityah saw it, so¦63636 his zeal was kindled, and¦63639 his guts trembled, and¦63641 he¦63645 vented his anger¦63648 according¦63649 to¦63649 judgement¦63651, and¦63652 ran¦63653 and killed him on¦63656 the¦63657 altar¦63658.
\v 25 He killed¦63667 the¦63662 king's¦63663 officer, who¦63664 compelled men¦63661 to¦63666 sacrifice¦63666, at the¦63669 same time¦63670, and¦63672 pulled down¦63675 the¦63673 altar¦63674.
