\s1 The decision to fight on the Sabbath
\p
\v 29 Then¦63724 many who sought¦63727 justice and¦63729 judgement¦63730 went¦63725 down¦63725 into¦63727 the¦63732 wilderness to¦63734 live there¦63735—
\v 30 they, their children¦63739, their wives, and their livestock—because¦63749 evils¦63754 were multiplied¦63750 on¦63751 them.
\v 31 It was told the¦63759 king's¦63760 officers and¦63761 the¦63762 forces that¦63764 were¦63765 in¦63766 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, the city¦63768 of David, that¦63770 certain men¦63772 who'd¦63773 broken the¦63775 king's commandment¦63776 had gone¦63771 down¦63771 into the secret places in¦63782 the¦63783 wilderness;
\v 32 and¦63785 many pursued after¦63787 them, and¦63790 having overtaken them, they encamped against¦63794 them and¦63796 set the battle¦63800 in array against them on the¦63804 Sabbath¦63805 day¦63803.
\v 33 They said¦63807 to¦63808 them, “Enough of¦63811 this! Come¦63814 out¦63814 and¦63815 do¦63816 according¦63817 to¦63817 the¦63820 king's¦63821 word¦63819, and¦63822 you'll all live¦63823!”
\p
\v 34 They said¦63825, “We won't come out. We won't do¦63829 the¦63832 king's¦63833 word¦63831, to¦63835 profane¦63835 the Sabbath¦63839 day¦63837.”
\p
\v 35 Then¦63840 the enemy hurried to¦63842 attack them.
\p
\v 36 They didn't answer¦63847 them. They didn't throw a stone¦63850 at them, or block their secret places,
\v 37 saying, “Let's all¦63859 die¦63858 in¦63860 our innocence. Heaven¦63868 and¦63869 earth¦63871 testify¦63864 for us, that¦63872 you put us to death unjustly.”
\p
\v 38 So¦63876 they attacked them on¦63880 the¦63883 Sabbath¦63884, and¦63885 they died¦63886—they, their wives, their children¦63894, and¦63896 their livestock—in number a thousand¦63901 souls¦63902 of men.
\p
\v 39 When¦63904 Matityah \add !(Mattathias)\add* and¦63907 his friends¦63909 found out about it¦63910, and¦63911 they mourned over them greatly.
\v 40 One said¦63918 to¦63918 another, “If¦63923 we all¦63924 do¦63925 as our kindred have done¦63930, and¦63931 don't¦63932 fight against the¦63935 Gentiles for¦63937 our lives and¦63941 our ordinances, they'll quickly¦63946 destroy us from¦63949 off the¦63950 earth¦63951.”
\v 41 So¦63952 they decided that¦63956 day¦63955, saying, “Anyone who comes¦63962 against us to¦63963 battle¦63966 on the¦63969 Sabbath¦63970 day, let's fight against him, and¦63974 we'll in no¦63975 way all die, as¦63979 our kindred died¦63980 in¦63984 the¦63985 secret places.”
\p
\v 42 Then¦63987 a company of the Hasidim,\f + \fr 2:42 \ft That is, \fqa Chasidim.\f* mighty¦63993 men of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*, everyone¦63997 who¦63998 offered himself willingly for the¦64000 law¦64001, were gathered together to them.
\v 43 All¦64003 those who¦64004 fled from¦64006 the¦64007 evils¦64008 were added¦64009 to¦64009 them, and¦64011 supported them.
\v 44 They mustered an army, and struck sinners in¦64022 their anger, and¦64025 lawless¦64027 men¦64026 in¦64028 their anger¦64023. The¦64032 rest fled¦64034 to¦64034 the¦64036 Gentiles for safety.
\v 45 And¦64039 Matityah and¦64042 his friends¦64044 went around and¦64046 pulled down the¦64048 altars.
\v 46 They forcibly circumcised the¦64052 boys who¦64054 were uncircumcised, as many as they found¦64057 in the coasts of Yisrael.
\v 47 They pursued¦64064 the arrogant, and¦64069 the¦64071 work¦64072 prospered in¦64073 their hand¦64074.
\v 48 They rescued the¦64078 law¦64079 out¦64080 of the hand¦64081 of the¦64082 Gentiles and¦64084 out¦64085 of the hand¦64086 of the¦64087 kings¦64088. They never allowed the sinner to¦64091 triumph.
\s1 Matityah's final advice to his sons
\p
\v 49 The¦64097 days¦64098 of¦64099 Matityah drew near¦64096 that he should die¦64101, and¦64102 he said¦64103 to¦64103 his sons¦64105, “Now¦64107 pride¦64109 and scorn have gained strength. It's a season¦64113 of overthrow and¦64115 indignant anger.
\v 50 Now¦64119, my children¦64120, be zealous for the¦64122 law¦64123, and¦64124 give¦64125 your lives for the covenant¦64130 of your fathers¦64131.
\v 51 Call to¦64133 remembrance¦64133 the¦64134 actions¦64138 of our fathers¦64135 which¦64139 they did¦64140 in¦64141 their generations¦64143; and¦64145 receive¦64146 great¦64148 glory¦64147 and¦64149 an eternal¦64151 name¦64150.
\v 52 Wasn't Avraham found¦64156 faithful¦64157 in¦64154 temptation¦64155,\x + \xo 2:52: \xt Gen 22:1-12.\x* and¦64158 it¦64160 was reckoned to him for righteousness¦64162?\x + \xo 2:52: \xt Gen 15:6.\x*
\v 53 Yosef \add !(Joseph)\add* in¦64164 the time¦64165 of his distress kept¦64168 the commandment¦64169,\x + \xo 2:53: \xt Gen 39:7-9.\x* and¦64170 became lord¦64172 of Mitsrayim \add !(Egypt)\add*.\x + \xo 2:53: \xt Gen 41:39-43.\x*
\v 54 Pinhas our father¦64176, because he was extremely zealous, obtained the¦64179 covenant¦64183 of an eternal priesthood¦64184.\x + \xo 2:54: \xt Num 25:10-13.\x*
\v 55 Yeshua \add !(Jesus)\add* became a judge¦64192 in¦64187 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*\x + \xo 2:55: \xt Num 27:18-23.\x* for fulfilling¦64189 the¦64188 word¦64190.
\v 56 Kalev \add !(Caleb)\add* obtained a heritage¦64204 in¦64196 the¦64197 land¦64203 for testifying in¦64199 the¦64200 congregation¦64201.\x + \xo 2:56: \xt Josh 14:6-14.\x*
\v 57 David inherited the¦64207 throne¦64211 of a kingdom¦64212 forever and ever\x + \xo 2:57: \xt 2Sam 7:12-16.\x* for being merciful.
\v 58 Eliyah \add !(Elijah)\add* was taken¦64222 up¦64222 into heaven¦64226\x + \xo 2:58: \xt 2Ki 2:11.\x* because he was extremely zealous for the law¦64221.
\v 59 Hananyah, Azaryah, and Mishael\x + \xo 2:59: \xt Dan 1:6-7.\x* believed, and were saved out¦64232 of the flame.\x + \xo 2:59: \xt Dan 3:26-27.\x*
\v 60 Daniyel was delivered from¦64240 the¦64236 mouth¦64241 of lions¦64242 for his innocence.\x + \xo 2:60: \xt Dan 6:21-23.\x*
\p
\v 61 “Thus consider throughout the generations that¦64250 no¦64256 one who put their trust in him will lack for strength.
\v 62 Don't¦64263 be afraid¦64264 of the¦64266 words¦64260 of a sinful man¦64261; for his glory¦64267 will be dung and¦64271 worms.
\v 63 Today¦64274 he'll be lifted up, and¦64276 tomorrow¦64277 he'll in no¦64278 way be found¦64280, because¦64281 he's returned to¦64282 dust¦64285, and¦64287 his thought has perished.
\v 64 You¦64293, my children¦64294, be¦64295 strong¦64295, and¦64296 show yourselves men¦64297 on¦64298 behalf of the¦64299 law¦64300; for in¦64302 it¦64303 you'll obtain glory.
\v 65 Listen, Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* your brother¦64309, whom I know to¦64311 be a man¦64313 of counsel. Always listen to him. He'll be¦64323 a father¦64325 to you.
\v 66 Yehudah \add !(Judas)\add* Makabi \add !(Maccabaeus)\add* has been strong¦64329 and¦64326 mighty from¦64331 his youth¦64332. He'll be¦64336 your captain and¦64339 will fight\f + \fr 2:66 \ft Some ancient authorities read \fqa you shall fight.\f* the battle of the people¦64342.
\v 67 Rally around all¦64348 the¦64349 doers of¦64351 the¦64351 law¦64352, and¦64353 avenge the¦64356 wrong done to your people¦64357.
\v 68 Repay¦64360 the¦64361 Gentiles, and¦64363 obey the¦64366 commandments of¦64368 the¦64368 law¦64369.”
\p
\v 69 He¦64372 blessed¦64371 them, and¦64373 was gathered to his ancestors.
\v 70 He died¦64380 in¦64381\f + \fr 2:70 \ft circa B.C. 167.\f* the¦64382 one hundred and forty sixth¦64383 year¦64388, and¦64389 his sons¦64393 buried¦64390 him in the tombs of his ancestors at Modi'in. All¦64404 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* made great¦64407 lamentation¦64406 for him.
\c 3
\s1 Yehudah Makabi leads the resistance
\p
\v 1 His son¦64414 Yehudah, who¦64411 was called¦64412 Makabi, rose up in his place.
\v 2 All¦64421 his kindred helped him, and¦64425 so did all¦64426 those who joined¦64428 with his father¦64430, and¦64432 they fought¦64435 with¦64437 gladness¦64438 the battle of Yisrael.
\v 3 He got his people great glory¦64441, and¦64445 put¦64446 on¦64446 a breastplate¦64447 like a¦64449 giant¦64449, and¦64450 bound his warlike harness around him, and¦64457 set battles in¦64462 array, protecting the army with his sword¦64463.
\v 4 He was like a lion¦64466 in¦64467 his actions¦64469, and¦64471 like a lion's cub¦64473 roaring for prey.
\v 5 He hunted and¦64477 pursued¦64478 the lawless¦64479, and¦64481 he burnt up those who troubled his people¦64485.
\v 6 The lawless shrunk back for fear¦64494 of him, and¦64496 all¦64497 the¦64498 workers¦64499 of lawlessness¦64501 were very troubled, and¦64503 deliverance prospered in¦64506 his hand¦64507.
\v 7 He angered many kings¦64511 and¦64513 made¦64519 Ya'akov \add !(Jacob)\add* glad with his acts. His memory¦64526 is blessed forever.
\v 8 He went through¦64531 the cities¦64533 of Yehudah, destroyed the ungodly¦64537\f + \fr 3:8 \ft Grk. \fqa out of it.\f* out¦64538 of the land, and¦64540 turned away¦64543 anger¦64542 from¦64543 Yisrael.
\v 9 He was renowned to¦64546 the utmost part of the¦64549 earth¦64550. He gathered together those who were ready to¦64552 perish.
\s1 Yehudah's first victories
\p
\v 10 Apolonios gathered the Gentiles together with a great¦64562 army from Shomron \add !(Samaria)\add* to¦64564 fight¦64564 against Yisrael.
\v 11 Yehudah learnt of it, and he went¦64571 out¦64571 to¦64576 meet him, struck¦64576 him, and¦64578 killed¦64579 him. Many fell wounded to¦64582 death, and¦64585 the¦64586 rest fled¦64588.
\v 12 They took their spoils, and Yehudah took Apolonios' sword¦64596, and¦64600 he fought¦64602 with it¦64604 all¦64605 his days¦64607.
\p
\v 13 Seron, the¦64611 commander of Aram's \add !(Syria)\add* army, heard¦64609 that¦64616 Yehudah had gathered¦64619 a large company, including¦64620 a body of faithful¦64622 men who stayed with¦64623 him, went out to¦64625 war¦64627.
\v 14 He said¦64629, “I'll make¦64630 myself¦64631 a name¦64632 and¦64633 get myself glory in¦64635 the¦64636 kingdom¦64637. I'll fight¦64639 against Yehudah and¦64642 those who¦64643 are with¦64644 him, who despise the¦64650 king's¦64651 command.
\v 15 A mighty¦64662 army of¦64654 the¦64654 ungodly¦64661 went up with him to¦64663 help¦64663 him, to¦64666 take vengeance¦64668 on¦64669 the children¦64670 of Yisrael.
\p
\v 16 He came¦64673 near¦64673 to the ascent of Beyt-Horon, and Yehudah went¦64678 out¦64678 to meet him with a small company.
\v 17 But¦64685 when they saw the¦64687 army coming¦64689 to¦64693 meet them, they said¦64693 to Yehudah, “How can our small group fight¦64700 against such a large¦64703, strong¦64704 army? We're¦64706 exhausted, and we haven't eaten anything today¦64709.”
\p
\v 18 Yehudah said¦64711, “It's¦64714 an easy thing for many to be¦64722 hemmed in¦64724 by the¦64725 hands¦64718 of¦64727 a few. With\f + \fr 3:18 \ft Some ancient authorities read \fqa the god of heaven.\f* heaven¦64728 it's all one, to¦64729 save¦64729 by many or¦64732 by few¦64734;
\v 19 for victory¦64740 in battle stands not in the multitude¦64738 of¦64746 an army, but¦64743 strength¦64749 is from¦64745 heaven¦64747.
\v 20 They come¦64751 to¦64752 us in¦64754 fullness of insolence and¦64757 lawlessness¦64758, to destroy us and¦64762 our wives and¦64766 our children¦64768, and to plunder us,
\v 21 but¦64774 we¦64779 fight for our lives and¦64780 our laws.
\v 22 He himself will crush them before¦64788 our face¦64789; but¦64792 as for you¦64791, don't¦64793 be afraid¦64794 of them.
\p
\v 23 Now when¦64798 he'd finished speaking¦64800, he¦64803 rushed suddenly¦64804 against Seron and¦64805 his army, and¦64808 they were defeated before¦64812 him.
\v 24 They pursued¦64815 them down the¦64818 descent¦64819 of¦64822 Beyt-Horon to the¦64822 plain, and¦64824 about eight hundred men¦64829 of them fell; but the rest fled¦64834 into the land¦64836 of the Pelishtim.
\p
\v 25 The¦64840 fear¦64841 of Yehudah and¦64843 his kindred, and¦64847 the¦64848 dread of them, began to¦64850 fall¦64850 on the¦64852 nations¦64853 around them.
\v 26 His fame reached¦64858 the¦64860 king¦64861, and¦64865 every¦64871 nation¦64872 told¦64870 of the battles of Yehudah.
\s1 The king sends an army against Yehudah
\p
\v 27 But¦64874 when King¦64878 Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* heard¦64875 these words¦64880, he¦64881 was full of indignation; and¦64884 he sent¦64885 and¦64886 gathered together all¦64890 the¦64891 forces of his realm, an extremely strong¦64895 army.
\v 28 He opened¦64898 his treasury¦64900 and¦64902 gave¦64903 his forces pay for a year¦64909, and¦64910 commanded them to be¦64912 ready¦64914 for every¦64916 need¦64917.
\v 29 He saw that¦64920 the¦64922 money¦64923 was gone from¦64924 his treasures¦64926, and¦64927 that the¦64928 tributes of the¦64930 country¦64931 were small¦64932, because¦64933 of¦64933 the¦64934 dissension¦64935 and¦64936 disaster¦64937 which¦64938 he'd brought on¦64940 the¦64941 land¦64942, to the end that he might take¦64944 away the¦64945 laws which¦64947 had been¦64948 from¦64949 the¦64951 first¦64952 days¦64950.
\v 30 He was afraid that¦64958 he wouldn't have enough as at other times for the¦64963 charges and¦64965 the¦64966 gifts¦64967 which¦64968 he used to¦64969 give¦64969 with a liberal hand¦64972, more abundantly than the¦64976 kings¦64977 who¦64978 were before¦64979 him.
\v 31 And¦64980 he¦64984 was extremely perplexed in his mind, and¦64986 he determined to¦64989 go into Paras \add !(Persia)\add*, and¦64993 to¦64994 take¦64994 the¦64995 tributes of those countries, and¦64999 to¦65000 gather¦65000 much¦65002 money¦65001.
\v 32 He left¦65004 Lusias, an honourable¦65007 man¦65006, and¦65008 one of royal lineage, to¦65013 be over the¦65014 affairs of¦65016 the¦65016 king¦65017 from¦65018 the¦65019 river¦65020 Perat \add !(Euphrates)\add* to the¦65023 borders of Mitsrayim \add !(Egypt)\add*,
\v 33 and¦65026 to bring up his son¦65030 Antiokos, until¦65032 he¦65035 came again.
\v 34 He delivered¦65037 to Lusias half of his forces and¦65043 the¦65044 elephants, and¦65046 gave him charge of all¦65050 the things that¦65051 he'd have done, and¦65053 about¦65054 those who¦65055 lived¦65056 in Yehudah and¦65059 in Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*,
\v 35 that he should send¦65061 an army against them to root out and¦65067 destroy the¦65069 strength¦65070 of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* and¦65072 the¦65073 remnant¦65074 of Yerushalem, and¦65076 to¦65077 take¦65077 away¦65081 their memory¦65079 from¦65081 the¦65082 place¦65083,
\v 36 and¦65084 that he should make foreigners live¦65085 in¦65088 all¦65089 their territory¦65091, and¦65093 should divide their land¦65096 to them by lot.
\v 37 The¦65099 king¦65100 took¦65101 the¦65102 half that¦65104 remained of the¦65106 forces, and¦65108 left Antiokeia, his royal city¦65113, in the one hundred and forty seventh¦65117 year;\f + \fr 3:37 \ft circa B.C. 166.\f* and he passed over the¦65124 river¦65126 Perat, and¦65127 went through¦65128 the¦65129 upper countries¦65131.
\p
\v 38 Lusias¦65134 chose Ptolemaios \add !(Ptolemy)\add* the¦65136 son of Dorumenes, Nikanor, and Gorgias, mighty men¦65142 of¦65146 the¦65146 king's¦65147 friends¦65145;\f + \fr 3:38 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f*
\v 39 and¦65148 with¦65150 them, he¦65151 sent¦65149 forty¦65152 thousand infantry and¦65155 seven thousand cavalry to¦65159 go¦65159 into the land¦65161 of Yehudah and¦65163 to destroy it¦65165, according¦65166 to¦65166 the¦65169 king's¦65170 word¦65168.
\v 40 They set out with¦65173 all¦65174 their army, and¦65178 came¦65179 and¦65180 encamped near¦65182 Emmaous in¦65184 the plain country.
\v 41 The¦65191 merchants¦65192 of the¦65193 country¦65194 heard¦65190 of their fame, and¦65198 took¦65199 silver and¦65201 gold¦65202 in large quantities, and¦65205 fetters,\f + \fr 3:41 \ft Most of the authorities read \fqa servants.\f* and¦65207 came¦65208 into the camp to¦65213 take¦65213 the¦65214 children¦65218 of Yisrael for slaves. Forces of Aram \add !(Syria)\add* and¦65219 of the land¦65226 of the Pelishtim\f + \fr 3:41 \ft Grk. \fqa foreigners.\f* joined with¦65221 them.
\s1 The people pray and prepare for battle
\p
\v 42 Yehudah and his kindred saw that¦65235 evils¦65238 were multiplied¦65236, and¦65239 that the¦65240 forces were encamping in¦65243 their borders. They learnt about the king's¦65252 words¦65250 which¦65253 he'd commanded, to¦65254 destroy¦65259 the¦65256 people¦65257 and¦65260 make¦65255 an end of them.
\v 43 Then¦65262 they each¦65264 said¦65263 to¦65265 his neighbour¦65267, “Let's repair the¦65270 ruins of¦65272 our people¦65273. Let's fight for our people¦65279 and¦65281 the¦65282 holy¦65283 place.”
\v 44 The congregation was gathered together, that they might be¦65289 ready¦65290 for battle¦65292, and¦65293 that they might pray¦65295 and¦65296 ask¦65297 for mercy¦65298 and¦65299 compassion.
\v 45 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* was¦65303 without inhabitant like a wilderness. There was¦65308 none of her offspring who¦65309 went in or went out¦65313. The sanctuary was trampled down. Children¦65322 of foreigners were in¦65324 the¦65325 citadel. The¦65328 Gentiles lived there. Joy was taken away from¦65333 Ya'akov \add !(Jacob)\add*, and¦65335 the pipe and¦65338 the harp ceased.
\v 46 They gathered themselves together, and¦65340 came to Mitspah, near Yerushalem; for in Mitspah there used to be a place¦65349 of prayer¦65350 for Yisrael.
\v 47 They fasted that¦65361 day¦65360, put on sackcloth¦65364, put ashes on¦65367 their heads¦65369, tore their clothes¦65374,
\v 48 and¦65376 opened the¦65378 book¦65379 of¦65380 the¦65380 law¦65381, to learn about¦65382 the things for which¦65383 the Gentiles consulted the images of their idols¦65390.
\v 49 They brought the priests¦65397’ clothes¦65395, the first fruits, and the tithes. They stirred up the Nazarites, who'd accomplished their days¦65411.
\v 50 They cried aloud towards¦65415 heaven¦65417, saying, “What should we do¦65420 with these men? Where¦65423 should we carry them away?
\v 51 Your holy¦65428 place is trampled down and profaned. Your priests¦65435 mourn in¦65437 humiliation.
\v 52 Listen, the¦65443 Gentiles are assembled together against us to destroy us. You¦65451 know what things they imagine against¦65455 us.
\v 53 How¦65457 will we be¦65458 able¦65458 to¦65460 stand against them, unless you¦65465 help us?”
\v 54 They sounded¦65474 with the¦65470 trumpets, and¦65472 gave a loud shout.
\p
\v 55 And¦65476 after¦65477 this¦65478 Yehudah \add !(Judas)\add* appointed¦65479 leaders of¦65482 the¦65482 people¦65483: captains of thousands, captains of hundreds, captains of fifties, and captains of tens.
\v 56 He said¦65492 to¦65492 those who¦65493 were building houses, were betrothing wives, were planting vineyards, and were fearful, that they should return¦65504, each¦65505 man to his own house¦65508, according¦65510 to¦65510 the¦65511 law¦65512.
\v 57 The army marched out and encamped on the south¦65520 side of Emmaous.
\v 58 Yehudah said¦65523, “Arm yourselves and¦65526 be¦65527 valiant men! Be¦65532 ready¦65533 in the¦65536 morning to¦65537 fight¦65537 with these Gentiles who are assembled together against us to destroy us and¦65548 our holy¦65550 place.
\v 59 Because¦65552 it's better for us to¦65555 die¦65555 in¦65556 battle¦65558 than¦65559 to¦65561 see the¦65562 calamities of¦65564 our nation¦65565 and¦65567 the¦65568 holy¦65569 place.
\v 60 Nevertheless, as may be¦65573 the will¦65574 in¦65575 heaven¦65576, so¦65571 will he do¦65578.
\c 4
\s1 Yehudah defeats Gorgias' army
\p
\v 1 Gorgias¦65581 took¦65580 five¦65582 thousand infantry, a thousand chosen cavalry, and the¦65590 army moved out at night¦65592,
\v 2 that it might fall onto the¦65596 army of the¦65598 Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add* and¦65600 strike¦65601 them suddenly¦65603. The¦65605 men of the¦65607 citadel were¦65609 his guides¦65611.
\v 3 Yehudah heard¦65613 of this, and¦65615 he¦65617 and¦65618 the¦65619 valiant men moved, that he might strike¦65621 the king's¦65625 army which was at Emmaous
\v 4 while the¦65631 forces were¦65634 still¦65630 dispersed from¦65635 the¦65636 camp.
\v 5 Gorgias¦65640 came¦65639 into the¦65642 camp of Yehudah at night¦65645 and¦65646 found¦65648 no man. He¦65651 sought¦65650 them in¦65652 the¦65653 mountains¦65654; for he¦65658 said¦65656, “These men are running away¦65659 from¦65659 us.”
\p
\v 6 As soon as it was day¦65664, Yehudah appeared in¦65667 the¦65668 plain with three thousand men¦65672. However¦65673 they didn't have the armour and¦65675 swords¦65676 they desired.
\v 7 They saw the camp of the Gentiles strong¦65685 and¦65687 fortified, with cavalry all around it¦65690; and¦65691 these were expert in war.
\v 8 Yehudah said¦65696 to¦65696 the¦65698 men¦65699 who were with¦65701 him, “Don't¦65703 be afraid¦65704 of their numbers, or when¦65708 they charge.
\v 9 Remember¦65714 how¦65715 our fathers¦65718 were saved in¦65720 the Red¦65722 sea¦65721, when¦65723 Par'oh \add !(Pharaoh)\add* pursued¦65724 them with an army.
\v 10 Now¦65730 let's cry to heaven¦65734, if¦65735 he'll have us, and¦65738 will remember the covenant¦65740 of our fathers¦65741, and¦65743 destroy¦65744 this army before our face¦65749 today¦65751.
\v 11 Then¦65752 all¦65754 the¦65755 Gentiles will know¦65753 that¦65757 there's¦65758 one who¦65759 redeems and¦65761 saves Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*.
\p
\v 12 The foreigners lifted up¦65766 their eyes¦65770, and¦65772 saw them coming¦65775 near them.
\v 13 They went¦65778 out of the¦65780 camp to battle¦65783. Those who¦65786 were with¦65787 Yehudah sounded their trumpets
\v 14 and joined battle. The¦65793 Gentiles were defeated, and¦65795 fled¦65796 into the¦65798 plain¦65799.
\v 15 But¦65801 all¦65803 those in¦65805 the rear fell by the sword¦65806. They pursued¦65808 them to\f + \fr 4:15 \ft Grk. \fqa Gazera.\f* Gezer, and¦65812 to the plains of Edom, Azotos, and Yavneh. About three thousand of those men¦65827 fell.
\v 16 Then¦65829 Yehudah and¦65832 his army returned from¦65835 pursuing them;
\v 17 and¦65840 he said¦65841 to¦65842 the¦65843 people¦65844, “Don't¦65845 be greedy for the¦65847 spoils, because¦65849 there's a battle¦65850 before us.
\v 18 Gorgias¦65854 and¦65855 his army are near¦65861 us on¦65858 the¦65859 mountain¦65860. But¦65863 stand¦65864 now¦65865 against¦65866 our enemies¦65868 and¦65870 fight against them, and¦65873 afterwards¦65874 take the¦65877 spoils with¦65879 boldness¦65880.”
\v 19 While Yehudah was finishing this¦65884 speech, a part¦65886 of them appeared looking out¦65889 from¦65889 the¦65890 mountain¦65891.
\v 20 They saw that their army had been put to flight, and that the¦65898 Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add* were burning the¦65900 camp; for¦65901 the smoke¦65902 that was seen declared what was done.
\v 21 But¦65908 when they perceived these things, they were very¦65912 afraid. Perceiving also Yehudah's army in¦65919 the¦65920 plain ready¦65922 for battle,
\v 22 they all¦65926 fled¦65925 into the land¦65928 of the\f + \fr 4:22 \ft Grk. \fqa foreigners.\f* Pelishtim.
\v 23 Yehudah returned to¦65933 plunder the camp, and¦65938 they took¦65939 much¦65941 gold¦65940, silver, blue, sea purple¦65947, and¦65949 great¦65951 riches¦65950.
\v 24 Then they returned home, and sang a song of thanksgiving, and gave praise¦65954 to heaven¦65958, because¦65961 he's¦65969 good¦65962, because¦65963 his mercy¦65968 endures forever.
\v 25 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* had a great¦65973 deliverance that¦65979 day¦65978.
\s1 Yehudah defeats Lusias
\p
\v 26 The¦65982 foreigners who'd¦65987 escaped came and told Lusias all¦65989 the¦65990 things that'd happened.
\v 27 When¦65993 he heard¦65994 of it, he was confounded¦65995 and¦65996 discouraged, because¦65998 the things he desired¦66001 hadn't been done to¦66003 Yisrael, nor had such¦66008 things happened as¦66008 the¦66011 king¦66012 commanded him.
\p
\v 28 In¦66016 the next year, he gathered together sixty¦66025 thousand chosen infantry and¦66027 five thousand cavalry, that he¦66032 might subdue them.
\v 29 They came¦66034 into¦66040 Edom and¦66042 encamped at Beyt-Tsur. Yehudah met¦66043 them with ten¦66047 thousand¦66048 men¦66049.
\v 30 He saw that the¦66052 army was strong¦66054, and¦66055 he prayed¦66056 and¦66057 said¦66058, “Blessed are¦66060 you, Oh Saviour¦66062 of¦66063 Yisrael, who¦66065 defeated the¦66067 attack of¦66069 the mighty warrior by the hand¦66072 of¦66073 your servant¦66074 David, and¦66077 delivered¦66078 the army of the\f + \fr 4:30 \ft Grk. \fqa foreigners.\f* Pelishtim into the hands¦66084 of Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* the son¦66086 of Sha'ul \add !(Saul)\add*, and¦66088 of¦66089 his armour bearer.
\v 31 Hem in this army in¦66098 the hand¦66099 of your people¦66100 Yisrael, and¦66103 let them be ashamed for their army and¦66108 their cavalry.
\v 32 Give¦66112 them faintness of heart. Cause the boldness¦66117 of their strength¦66118 to melt away, and¦66120 let them quake at their destruction.
\v 33 Strike them down with the sword¦66127 of those who love¦66128 you¦66129, and¦66130 let all¦66133 who know your name¦66137 praise you¦66138 with thanksgiving.”
\p
\v 34 They joined in battle; and about five¦66151 thousand¦66151 men¦66152 of Lusias' army fell. They fell down near them.
\v 35 But¦66159 when Lusias¦66160 saw that¦66161 his troops were put to¦66162 flight, and the¦66164 boldness that'd¦66167 come on those who¦66170 were¦66171 with Yehudah, and¦66173 how¦66174 they were ready¦66175 either to¦66178 live¦66178 or¦66179 to die nobly, he withdrew to Antiokeia, and gathered together hired soldiers, that¦66189 he might come again¦66193 into Yehudah with an even greater army.
\s1 The temple is cleansed and rededicated
\p
\v 36 But¦66199 Yehudah and¦66201 his kindred said¦66198, “Listen, our enemies¦66208 are defeated. Let's go up to¦66211 cleanse¦66211 the¦66212 holy¦66213 place and¦66214 to rededicate it.”
\v 37 All¦66220 the army was gathered together, and¦66221 they went up to¦66222 Mt¦66224. Tsiyon \add !(Zion)\add*.
\v 38 They saw the¦66228 sanctuary laid desolate, the¦66232 altar¦66233 profaned, the¦66236 gates¦66237 burnt up, shrubs growing in¦66240 the¦66241 courtyards as in¦66246 a forest or¦66248 as on¦66250 one¦66251 of the¦66252 mountains¦66253, and¦66254 the¦66255 priests’ chambers pulled down;
\v 39 and¦66258 they tore their clothes¦66261, made great¦66266 lamentation¦66265, put¦66268 ashes on¦66270 their heads¦66272,
\v 40 fell on¦66276 their faces¦66277 to¦66278 the¦66279 ground¦66280,\f + \fr 4:40 \ft Compare Numbers 31:6.\f* blew with the solemn trumpets,\f + \fr 4:40 \ft Grk. \fqa trumpets of signals.\f* and¦66287 cried towards¦66289 heaven¦66291.
\v 41 Then¦66292 Yehudah appointed certain men¦66295 to¦66293 fight against those who¦66297 were in¦66298 the¦66299 citadel until¦66301 he'd cleansed¦66303 the¦66304 holy¦66305 place.
\p
\v 42 He chose blameless¦66309 priests¦66308 who were devoted to the law¦66311;
\v 43 and¦66312 they cleansed the¦66314 holy¦66315 place and¦66316 carried the¦66318 defiled stones¦66319 out to an unclean¦66324 place.
\v 44 They deliberated what to¦66326 do with the¦66328 altar¦66329 of¦66332 burnt offerings, which¦66334 had been profaned.
\v 45 A good plan¦66340 came into¦66342 their mind, that¦66349 they should pull it down, so that it wouldn't bring¦66342 disgrace¦66348 on them, because the¦66351 Gentiles had defiled it¦66353. So¦66354 they pulled down the¦66356 altar¦66357
\v 46 and¦66358 laid¦66359 up the¦66360 stones¦66361 on¦66362 the temple¦66366 hill¦66364 in¦66367 a convenient place¦66368, until¦66370 a prophet¦66373 would come to¦66375 give an answer¦66375 about¦66376 them.
\v 47 They took¦66379 whole stones¦66380 according¦66382 to¦66382 the¦66383 law¦66384, and¦66385 built a new¦66389 altar¦66388 like the¦66391 former.
\v 48 They built the¦66395 holy¦66396 place and¦66397 the¦66398 inner parts of¦66400 the¦66400 house¦66401; and¦66402 they consecrated the¦66403 courtyards.
\v 49 They made¦66407 new¦66410 holy¦66409 vessels¦66408, and¦66411 they brought the¦66413 lampstand¦66414, the¦66416 altar¦66417 of incense¦66419, and¦66420 the¦66421 table¦66422 into the¦66424 temple¦66425.
\v 50 They burnt incense on¦66428 the¦66429 altar¦66430, and¦66431 they lit the¦66433 lamps that¦66435 were on¦66436 the¦66437 lampstand¦66438, and¦66439 they gave light in¦66441 the¦66442 temple¦66443.
\v 51 They set¦66445 loaves on¦66446 the¦66447 table¦66448, hung up the¦66452 curtains, and¦66454 finished¦66455 all¦66456 the¦66457 work¦66458 which¦66459 they'd done¦66460.
\p
\v 52 They rose up early in the¦66464 morning, on the¦66468 twenty-fifth day of¦66470 the¦66470 ninth month, which is the¦66473 month¦66474 Kislev, in\f + \fr 4:52 \ft circa B.C. 165.\f* the¦66476 one hundred and forty eighth year,
\v 53 and¦66483 offered sacrifice¦66485 according¦66486 to¦66486 the¦66487 law¦66488 on¦66489 the¦66490 new¦66495 altar¦66491 of burnt¦66493 offerings¦66493 which¦66496 they'd made¦66497.
\v 54 At the¦66499 time¦66500 and¦66501 day¦66504 the Gentiles had profaned it, even then it was dedicated with songs¦66515, harps¦66517, lutes, and with cymbals.
\v 55 All¦66525 the¦66526 people¦66527 fell on¦66528 their faces¦66529, worshipped¦66531, and¦66532 gave praise towards¦66534 heaven¦66535, which had given them good success.
\v 56 They celebrated the¦66541 dedication of¦66543 the¦66543 altar¦66544 eight¦66546 days¦66545, and¦66547 offered burnt¦66549 offerings¦66549 with¦66550 gladness¦66551, and¦66552 sacrificed a sacrifice¦66554 of deliverance and¦66556 praise¦66557.
\v 57 They decorated the¦66560 front¦66562 of¦66563 the¦66563 temple¦66564 with crowns of gold and small shields. They dedicated the¦66571 gates¦66572 and¦66573 the¦66574 priests’ chambers, and¦66576 made doors for them.
\v 58 There was¦66580 very¦66586 great¦66582 gladness¦66581 among¦66583 the¦66584 people¦66585, and¦66587 the reproach of the Gentiles was turned away.
\p
\v 59 Yehudah \add !(Judas)\add* and¦66591 his kindred and¦66594 the¦66595 whole¦66599 congregation¦66601 of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* ordained that¦66603 the¦66605 days¦66606 of the dedication of the¦66608 altar¦66609 should be kept in¦66610 their seasons from year¦66614 to¦66615 year¦66616 for eight¦66618 days, from¦66619 the¦66620 twenty-fifth day of¦66624 the¦66624 month Kislev, with¦66627 gladness¦66628 and¦66629 joy¦66630.
\p
\v 60 At that¦66636 time¦66635, they fortified Mt¦66638. Tsiyon \add !(Zion)\add* with high¦66642 walls¦66641 and¦66643 strong towers around¦66640 it, so that the¦66648 Gentiles wouldn't come and trample them down, as they'd done¦66653 before.
\v 61 Yehudah stationed a garrison to guard¦66659 it. They fortified Beyt-Tsur to¦66664 keep¦66664 it, that¦66665 the¦66667 people¦66670 might have¦66668 a stronghold¦66671 near Edom.
\c 5
\s1 The surrounding nations attack Yisrael
\p
\v 1 When¦66678 the¦66680 Gentiles all around¦66682 heard¦66679 that¦66683 the¦66685 altar¦66686 had been rebuilt and¦66687 the¦66689 sanctuary dedicated as before, they were extremely angry¦66694.
\v 2 They took¦66699 counsel to destroy the¦66700 race of Ya'akov \add !(Jacob)\add* that¦66703 was¦66704 among¦66705 them, and they began to kill and destroy among¦66712 the¦66713 people¦66714.
\v 3 Yehudah fought against the¦66721 children¦66722 of Esav \add !(Esau)\add* in¦66724 Edom at Akrabattine, because¦66729 they besieged Yisrael. He¦66735 struck¦66734 them with a great¦66737 slaughter, humbled them, and took¦66742 their spoils.
\v 4 He remembered¦66747 the¦66748 wickedness¦66749 of the children¦66750 of\f + \fr 5:4 \ft Compare 2 Maccabees 10:18-23.\f* Baean, who¦66752 were¦66753 a¦66755 snare and¦66758 a stumbling¦66760 block¦66760 to the people, lying in wait for them on the¦66766 highways.
\v 5 They were shut up by¦66770 him in¦66772 the¦66773 towers. He encamped against¦66777 them, and¦66779 destroyed them utterly, and¦66782 burnt with fire¦66788 the towers of the place with¦66789 all¦66790 who¦66791 were in them.
\v 6 He passed over to the¦66796 children¦66797 of Amon, and¦66799 found¦66800 a mighty¦66802 band and¦66803 many people¦66804, with Timotheos for their leader.
\v 7 He¦66813 fought¦66814 many battles with them, and¦66816 they were defeated before¦66818 his face¦66819. He¦66820 struck¦66822 them,
\v 8 and¦66824 took possession of Yazer and¦66828 its villages,\f + \fr 5:8 \ft Grk. \fqa daughters. \ft Compare Numbers 21:25.\f* and¦66832 returned again into Yehudah.
\s1 Calls for help from Gilead and Galil
\p
\v 9 The¦66839 Gentiles who¦66841 were in¦66842 Gilead gathered themselves together against¦66845 the¦66846 Israelis who¦66848 were¦66849 on¦66850 their borders, to¦66858 destroy them. They fled¦66858 to the¦66861 stronghold¦66862 of Dathema¦66860,
\v 10 and¦66863 sent¦66864 letters to¦66866 Yehudah and¦66868 his kindred, saying, “The Gentiles who are around us are gathered together against us to destroy us.
\v 11 They're preparing to¦66887 come¦66887 and¦66888 get possession of the¦66890 stronghold¦66891 where we fled for refuge, and¦66895 Timotheos¦66896 is the¦66898 leader of their army.
\v 12 Now¦66901 therefore¦66902 come¦66903 and deliver us from¦66906 their hand¦66907, for many of us have fallen.
\v 13 All¦66915 our kindred who were¦66920 in¦66921 the land of Toviyah \add !(Tobias)\add*\f + \fr 5:13 \ft Compare 2 Maccabees 12:17.\f* have been put to¦66920 death. They've carried their wives, their children¦66932, and their stuff into captivity. They destroyed about a thousand men¦66943 there¦66939.”
\p
\v 14 While the letters were still¦66944 being read, look¦66949, other¦66951 messengers came¦66952 from¦66953 Galil with their clothes¦66958 torn, bringing a similar report,
\v 15 saying, “People of Ptolemais, of Tsor \add !(Tyre)\add*, of Tsidon \add !(Sidon)\add*, and all¦66975 Galil of¦66978 the¦66978\f + \fr 5:15 \ft Grk. \fqa foreigners.\f* Gentiles have gathered together to destroy us.”
\p
\v 16 Now when¦66982 Yehudah and¦66985 the¦66986 people heard¦66983 these words¦66989, a great¦66993 congregation assembled together to¦66996 determine what they should do¦66996 for their kindred who were¦67001 in¦67002 distress and¦67004 under¦67006 attack.
\v 17 Yehudah said¦67009 to¦67009 Shim'on his brother¦67013, “Choose men¦67017 and go deliver¦67021 your kindred who are in¦67026 Galil, but¦67030 Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* my brother and I'll¦67035 go into¦67036 the¦67038 land of Gilead.”
\v 18 He left¦67041 Yosef \add !(Joseph)\add* the¦67043 son of¦67044 Zekaryah \add !(Zechariah)\add*, and¦67046 Azaryah, as leaders of¦67049 the¦67049 people¦67050, with¦67051 the¦67052 remnant of the¦67054 army, in¦67056 Yehudah, to guard it.
\v 19 He¦67063 commanded them, saying, “Take charge of¦67066 this people¦67067, and¦67069 fight no battle with¦67073 the¦67074 Gentiles until¦67076 we¦67079 return¦67078.”
\v 20 Then¦67080 three¦67084 thousand¦67084 men were assigned to¦67086 go into Galil with Shim'on, but¦67091 eight¦67093 thousand¦67093 men were assigned to Yehudah to go into the¦67095 land of Gilead.
\s1 Shim'on rescues the people in Galil
\p
\v 21 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* went into¦67098 Galil and¦67103 fought¦67105 many battles with¦67107 the¦67108 Gentiles, and¦67110 the¦67112 Gentiles were defeated before him.
\v 22 He pursued¦67118 them to Ptolemais' gate¦67122. About three thousand men¦67131 of the¦67127 Gentiles fell, and¦67132 he¦67136 took¦67133 their spoils.
\v 23 They took¦67138 to¦67138 them those who¦67139 were in¦67140 Galil and¦67143 in¦67144 Arbatta, with¦67146 their wives, their children¦67151, and¦67152 all¦67153 that they had, and¦67157 brought¦67158 them into Yehudah with¦67162 great¦67164 gladness¦67163.
\s1 Yehudah rescues the people in Gilead
\p
\v 24 Yehudah Makabi \add !(Maccabaeus)\add* and his brother¦67172 Yonatan passed over the¦67175 Yarden \add !(Jordan)\add*, and¦67177 went three¦67180 days¦67181’ journey in¦67182 the¦67183 wilderness.
\v 25 They met with the¦67187 Nabataeans, and¦67189 these met¦67190 them in a peaceful manner and¦67193 told them all¦67196 things that'd happened to their kindred in¦67202 the¦67203 land of Gilead,
\v 26 and¦67205 how many of them were¦67211 shut up in Bosora, Bosor¦67215, Alema,\f + \fr 5:26 \ft Compare 2 Maccabees 12:13.\f* Kasfor, Maked¦67219, and¦67220\f + \fr 5:26 \ft compare 2 Maccabees 12:21.\f* Karnayim—all¦67222 these cities¦67224 are strong and¦67227 large¦67228—
\v 27 and¦67229 how they were shut up in¦67230 the rest of the cities¦67233 of the¦67234 land of Gilead, and¦67238 that tomorrow¦67240 they planned to encamp against the¦67244 strongholds, and¦67246 to¦67247 take them, and¦67248 to destroy all¦67250 these men in¦67252 one day¦67253.
\p
\v 28 Yehudah and his army turned suddenly¦67268 by the¦67259 way of the¦67264 wilderness to Bosora; and¦67269 he took the¦67271 city¦67272, and¦67273 killed¦67274 all¦67275 the males with the edge of the sword, took¦67281 all¦67282 their spoils, and¦67286 burnt¦67287 the city with fire¦67289.
\v 29 He left there¦67292 at night¦67293, and¦67294 went until¦67296 he came to¦67297 the¦67298 stronghold¦67299.
\v 30 When the morning came, they lifted up¦67304 their eyes¦67306 and¦67308 saw many people¦67310 who couldn't be¦67314 counted¦67315, bearing ladders and¦67318 engines of war, to¦67320 take¦67304 the¦67321 stronghold¦67322; and¦67323 they were fighting against them.
\v 31 Yehudah saw that¦67329 the¦67331 battle¦67332 had begun, and¦67333 that the¦67334 cry of the¦67336 city¦67337 went up to¦67338 heaven¦67341, with trumpets and¦67343 a great¦67345 sound¦67344,
\v 32 and¦67346 he said¦67347 to¦67347 the¦67348 men¦67349 of his army, “Fight today¦67353 for¦67354 your kindred!”
\v 33 Then¦67358 he went¦67359 out¦67359 behind them in¦67360 three¦67361 companies. They sounded with their trumpets and cried out in¦67372 prayer¦67373.
\v 34 And¦67374 Timotheos' army perceived that¦67379 it was¦67381 Makabi \add !(Maccabaeus)\add*, and¦67382 they fled¦67383 from¦67384 before him. He¦67386 struck¦67388 them with a great¦67391 slaughter. About eight thousand men¦67402 of them fell on¦67396 that¦67397 day¦67399.
\p
\v 35 He turned away to Mitspah and fought¦67408 against it¦67409, took it¦67412, killed¦67414 all¦67415 its males, took¦67419 its spoils, and¦67423 burnt¦67424 it¦67425 with fire¦67426.
\v 36 From¦67427 there¦67427 he marched and¦67429 took\f + \fr 5:36 \ft See 1 Maccabees 5:26\f* Kasfor, Maked¦67433, Bosor¦67434, and¦67435 the¦67436 other cities¦67438 of the¦67439 land of Gilead.
\p
\v 37 Now after¦67441 these things, Timotheos¦67447 gathered another¦67449 army and¦67450 encamped near Rafon beyond the¦67457 brook¦67458.
\v 38 Yehudah sent¦67460 men to¦67460 spy on the¦67463 army; and¦67465 they brought him word, saying, “All¦67473 the¦67474 Gentiles who¦67476 are around us are gathered together to them, a very¦67481 great army.
\v 39 They've hired Aravim to help¦67486 them, and¦67488 are encamped beyond the¦67491 brook¦67492, ready¦67493 to¦67495 come¦67495 against¦67496 you¦67497 to battle¦67499.” So¦67500 Yehudah went to¦67501 meet them.
\p
\v 40 Timotheos¦67508 said¦67507 to the captains of his army when Yehudah and his army drew near¦67516 to¦67522 the¦67523 brook of¦67525 water¦67526, “If¦67527 he crosses over to¦67529 us first, we¦67530 won't be able to¦67539 withstand him, for he'll certainly defeat us;
\v 41 but if¦67541 he's afraid, and encamps beyond the¦67547 river¦67548, we'll cross over to¦67550 him, and¦67552 defeat him.”
\v 42 Now when¦67557 Yehudah came near¦67558 to¦67560 the¦67563 water¦67564 brook, he caused the¦67566 scribes¦67567 of¦67568 the¦67568 people¦67569 to¦67570 remain by the¦67571 brook¦67572, and¦67573 commanded them, saying, “Allow no man¦67580 to encamp, but¦67582 let all¦67584 come¦67558 to the¦67586 battle¦67587.”
\v 43 Then¦67588 he crossed¦67589 over the first against¦67590 them, and¦67593 all¦67594 the¦67595 people¦67596 after¦67597 him; and¦67599 all the Gentiles were defeated before¦67601 his face¦67602, and¦67607 threw¦67608 away their weapons¦67610, and¦67612 fled¦67613 to¦67613 the¦67615 temple at Karnayim.\f + \fr 5:43 \ft See 1 Maccabees 5:26.\f*
\v 44 They took the¦67621 city¦67622 and¦67623 burnt the¦67624 temple with fire¦67628, together with¦67629 all¦67630 who¦67631 were in¦67632 it¦67633. Karnayim was subdued. They couldn't stand any longer before Yehudah's face¦67644.
\s1 Yehudah brings the people home
\p
\v 45 Yehudah gathered together all¦67649 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*, those who¦67651 were in¦67652 the¦67653 land of Gilead, from¦67655 the¦67660 least to the¦67664 greatest, with their wives, their children¦67665, and¦67667 their stuff, a very¦67672 great¦67671 army, that they might come¦67673 into the land¦67675 of Yehudah.
\v 46 They came¦67678 as far as Efron¦67680, and¦67681 this same city¦67684 was large¦67685 and very¦67690 strong. It was on¦67686 the¦67687 road where they were¦67692 going. They couldn't turn away¦67694 from¦67694 it¦67695 on the right¦67696 hand or¦67697 on the left, but¦67699 needed to pass through¦67701 the middle¦67702 of¦67701 it¦67703.
\v 47 The¦67708 people of the¦67710 city¦67711 shut them out¦67709 and¦67712 blocked the¦67714 gates¦67715 with stones¦67716.
\v 48 Yehudah sent¦67718 to¦67718 them with¦67719 words¦67722 of peace, saying, “We'll pass through¦67726 your land¦67728 to¦67731 go¦67731 into our own land¦67734, and¦67736 no¦67745 one will harm you¦67739. We'll only pass by on our feet¦67742.” But they wouldn't open¦67747 to him.
\v 49 Then¦67749 Yehudah commanded¦67750 an announcement to¦67752 be made in¦67753 the army, that each¦67758 man should encamp in¦67759 the place¦67762 where he was.
\v 50 So¦67763 the¦67765 men¦67766 of the¦67767 army encamped, and¦67769 fought against the¦67771 city¦67772 all¦67773 that¦67774 day¦67775 and¦67777 all¦67778 that¦67779 night¦67780, and¦67781 the¦67783 city¦67784 was delivered¦67782 into¦67785 his hands¦67786.
\v 51 He destroyed¦67789 all¦67790 the males with the edge of the sword, razed the city, took¦67799 its plunder¦67801, and¦67803 passed¦67804 through the¦67806 city¦67807 over those who¦67809 were slain.
\v 52 They went over the Yarden \add !(Jordan)\add* into the¦67818 great¦67819 plain¦67817 near Beyt-Shean.
\v 53 And¦67823 Yehudah gathered together those who¦67827 lagged behind and¦67829 encouraged the¦67831 people¦67832 all¦67834 the¦67835 way through, until¦67837 he came¦67839 into the land¦67841 of Yehudah.
\v 54 They went up to¦67844 Mt¦67847. Tsiyon \add !(Zion)\add* with gladness¦67850 and¦67851 joy¦67852, and¦67853 offered whole burnt¦67855 offerings¦67855, because¦67856 not so much as one of them was slain until¦67862 they returned in¦67865 peace¦67866.
\s1 Yosef and Azaryah's failed attack
\p
\v 55 In¦67868 the¦67869 days¦67870 when Yehudah and¦67874 Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* were¦67872 in¦67876 the¦67877 land of Gilead, and¦67879 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* his brother¦67882 in¦67884 Galil before Ptolemais,
\v 56 Yosef \add !(Joseph)\add* the¦67892 son of¦67893 Zekaryah \add !(Zechariah)\add*, and¦67895 Azaryah, rulers¦67897 of the army, heard¦67890 of their exploits and¦67902 of¦67903 the¦67903 war, and what things they'd done¦67906.
\v 57 They said¦67908, “Let's also¦67910 get us a name¦67913, and¦67914 let's go fight¦67916 against the¦67918 Gentiles who¦67920 are around us.”
\v 58 So¦67923 they gave orders¦67924 to¦67924 the¦67925 men of the¦67927 army that¦67929 was with¦67930 them, and¦67932 went towards¦67934 Yavneh.
\v 59 Gorgias¦67938 and¦67942 his men¦67944 came out of the¦67940 city¦67941 to meet them in battle¦67950.
\v 60 Yosef and Azaryah were put to flight, and were pursued to¦67964 the¦67966 borders of¦67970 Yehudah. About two thousand men¦67976 of¦67972 Yisrael fell on that¦67968 day¦67967.
\v 61 There¦67992 was¦67978 a great¦67980 overthrow among¦67981 the¦67982 people¦67983, because¦67985 they didn't listen¦67987 to¦67987 Yehudah and¦67989 his kindred, thinking to do some exploit.
\v 62 But¦67996 they weren't¦67998 of¦68000 the family of¦68009 those men¦68003 by whose hand¦68010 deliverance was given¦68006 to Yisrael.
\p
\v 63 The¦68013 man¦68014 Yehudah and¦68016 his kindred were glorified greatly in¦68022 the sight of¦68022 all¦68023 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*, and¦68025 of all¦68028 the¦68031 Gentiles, wherever their name¦68032 was heard of.
\v 64 Men gathered together to¦68036 them, acclaiming them.
\s1 Yehudah's victories in the south
\p
\v 65 Yehudah and¦68039 his kindred went¦68040 out¦68040 and fought against the children¦68049 of Esav \add !(Esau)\add* in¦68051 the¦68052 land¦68053 towards the south¦68055. He¦68063 struck¦68057 Hevron and¦68064 its villages,\f + \fr 5:65 \ft Grk. \fqa daughters. \ft Compare Numbers 21:25.\f* pulled down¦68065 its strongholds¦68067, and¦68069 burnt¦68073 its towers all around¦68074.
\v 66 He marched to¦68078 go into the land¦68080 of¦68077 the¦68077\f + \fr 5:66 \ft Grk. \fqa foreigners.\f* Pelishtim, and¦68082 he went through¦68083\f + \fr 5:66 \ft Or, \fqa Marisa \ft See Josephus, Antiquities 12:8. 6, and 2 Maccabees 12:35.\f* Shomron \add !(Samaria)\add*.
\v 67 In¦68086 that¦68089 day¦68088 certain priests¦68091, desiring to¦68094 do exploits there, were slain in¦68096 battle, when they went¦68099 out¦68099 to battle unadvisedly.
\v 68 But¦68103 Yehudah turned¦68130 towards¦68106 Azotos, to¦68111 the¦68112 land of the¦68116\f + \fr 5:68 \ft Grk. \fqa foreigners.\f* Pelishtim, pulled down¦68111 their altars, burnt the¦68118 carved images of their gods with fire¦68122, took¦68111 the¦68125 plunder¦68126 of their cities¦68128, and¦68129 returned into the¦68132 land¦68133 of Yehudah.
\c 6
\s1 The death of King Antiokos
\p
\v 1 King¦68137 Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* was travelling¦68139 through¦68139 the¦68140 upper countries¦68142; and¦68143 he heard¦68144 that¦68145 in Elymais in Paras \add !(Persia)\add* there was a city¦68151 renowned for riches, for silver and gold¦68157,
\v 2 and¦68158 that the¦68159 temple¦68160 which was in¦68162 it¦68163 was extremely rich¦68164, and¦68166 that in it were golden¦68169 shields, breastplates, and weapons¦68173 which¦68174 Alexandros¦68177 \add !(Alexander)\add*, son of Filippos \add !(Philip)\add*, the¦68178 Makedonian king¦68180, who reigned¦68184 first¦68185 among¦68186 the¦68187 Hellains \add !(Greeks)\add*, left¦68175 behind¦68175 there¦68176.
\v 3 So¦68189 he came¦68190 and¦68191 tried¦68192 to¦68193 take the¦68194 city¦68195 and¦68196 to pillage it¦68198; and¦68199 he wasn't¦68201 able¦68201, because¦68202 his plan was known¦68203 to¦68203 them of the¦68208 city¦68209,
\v 4 and¦68210 they rose up against him in battle¦68214. He¦68212 fled¦68216 and¦68215 returned to¦68216 Bavel \add !(Babylon)\add* with¦68220 great¦68222 disappointment.
\p
\v 5 Then¦68226 someone¦68229 came¦68227 into¦68228 Paras bringing him news that¦68234 the armies which went against the land¦68241 of Yehudah had been put to¦68239 flight,
\v 6 and¦68243 that Lusias¦68245 went first¦68249 with a strong army and was put to shame before them, and that they'd grown strong because of weapons, power¦68259, and¦68260 a supply of plunder which¦68263 they took¦68264 from¦68265 the¦68266 armies that they'd cut off,
\v 7 and¦68270 that they'd pulled down the¦68272 abomination¦68273 which¦68274 he'd built¦68275 on¦68276 the¦68277 altar¦68278 that¦68279 was in¦68280 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, and¦68282 that they'd surrounded¦68288 the¦68283 sanctuary with high¦68290 walls, as¦68285 before¦68287, and¦68291 also¦68291 Beyt-Tsur, his city¦68294.
\p
\v 8 When¦68296 the¦68300 king¦68301 heard¦68299 these words¦68303, he¦68304 was astonished and moved greatly. He laid himself down on¦68311 his bed¦68313, and¦68314 fell sick for grief¦68320, because¦68321 it¦68324 hadn't turned out for him as¦68325 he'd planned.
\v 9 He was¦68328 there¦68329 many days¦68330, because¦68332 great¦68337 grief¦68336 continually gripped him, and¦68338 he realised that¦68340 he'd die¦68341.
\v 10 He called¦68343 for all¦68344 his\f + \fr 6:10 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* friends¦68346, and¦68348 said¦68349 to¦68350 them, “Sleep¦68354 departs from¦68355 my eyes¦68357, and¦68359 my heart¦68362 fails because of worry.
\v 11 I said¦68367 in my heart¦68369, ‘To¦68374 what suffering I've come¦68374! How great¦68377 a flood it's that¦68382 I'm in¦68378, now¦68380! Because I was¦68381 gracious and¦68384 loved in¦68387 my power.’
\v 12 But now¦68391 I remember the¦68394 evils¦68395 which¦68396 I did¦68397 at Yerushalem, and¦68400 that I took¦68401 all¦68402 the¦68403 vessels¦68404 of silver and¦68407 gold that were in¦68411 it¦68412, and¦68413 sent out to destroy the inhabitants¦68417 of Yehudah without a cause.
\v 13 I perceive that¦68422 it's because¦68423 of¦68423 this¦68424 that¦68427 these evils¦68428 have come on me. Listen, I'm perishing through great¦68434 grief¦68433 in¦68435 a strange land¦68436.”
\p
\v 14 Then¦68438 he called¦68439 for Filippos \add !(Philip)\add*, one¦68441 of his\f + \fr 6:14 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* friends¦68443, and¦68445 set him over all¦68449 his kingdom¦68451.
\v 15 He¦68455 gave¦68454 him his crown, his robe¦68460, and¦68462 his signet ring¦68464, so that he could guide Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* his son¦68469, and¦68471 nourish him up that he¦68473 might be king.
\v 16 Then¦68476 King¦68481 Antiokos died¦68477 there¦68478 in the¦68480 one hundred and forty-ninth year.\f + \fr 6:16 \ft Circa B.C. 164.\f*
\v 17 When¦68488 Lusias¦68490 learnt that¦68491 the¦68493 king¦68494 was dead¦68492, he set up Antiokos his son¦68500 to¦68497 reign¦68497, whom¦68499 he'd nourished up being young, and he called¦68508 his name¦68510 Eupator.
\s1 The siege of the citadel brings another invasion
\p
\v 18 Those who were¦68518 in the¦68520 citadel kept hemming Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* in around the¦68523 sanctuary¦68524, and¦68525 always sought¦68526 to¦68526 harm¦68528 them and¦68531 to strengthen the¦68533 Gentiles.
\v 19 Yehudah planned to destroy them, and called all¦68542 the¦68543 people¦68544 together to¦68547 besiege them.
\v 20 They were gathered together¦68551, and besieged them in\f + \fr 6:20 \ft circa B.C. 163.\f* the one hundred fiftieth year, and he made¦68561 mounds to¦68562 shoot from, and¦68565 engines of war.
\v 21 Some of those who were hemmed in came out, and some of the¦68578 ungodly¦68579 men of Yisrael were joined¦68575 to them.
\v 22 They went to the¦68585 king¦68586, and¦68587 said¦68588, “How much longer will you wait to¦68592 bring justice¦68593, and¦68594 avenge our kindred?
\v 23 We¦68599 were willing to¦68600 serve your father¦68603 and¦68605 to¦68606 live by¦68608 his words, and to follow his commandments.
\v 24 Because¦68625 of¦68625 this, the children¦68621 of¦68622 our people¦68623 besieged the citadel\f + \fr 6:24 \ft Grk. \fqa it.\f* and¦68627 were alienated from¦68629 us; but¦68631 as many of us as they could catch, they killed, and¦68637 plundered our inheritances.
\v 25 Not against¦68644 us only¦68646 did they stretch out their hand¦68648, but¦68649 also¦68650 against¦68651 all¦68652 their borders.
\v 26 Listen, they're encamped this day against the citadel at Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* to¦68666 take it¦68667. They've fortified the¦68669 sanctuary and¦68671 Beyt-Tsur.
\v 27 If¦68676 you don't¦68677 quickly prevent them, they'll do¦68683 greater¦68681 things than these, and¦68684 you won't be¦68686 able¦68686 to control them.
\p
\v 28 When¦68694 the¦68692 king¦68693 heard¦68695 this¦68699, he¦68701 was angry¦68691, and¦68702 gathered together all¦68698 his\f + \fr 6:28 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* friends¦68700, the¦68703 rulers¦68704 of his army, and¦68708 those who¦68709 were over the¦68711 cavalry.
\v 29 Bands of hired soldiers came¦68721 to him from¦68714 other¦68716 kingdoms and¦68717 from¦68718 islands of the sea.
\v 30 The¦68728 number¦68729 of his forces was one hundred¦68733 thousand¦68734 infantry, and¦68737 twenty¦68738 thousand¦68739 cavalry, and thirty-two elephants trained for war¦68747.
\v 31 They went¦68765 through¦68750 Edom, and¦68753 encamped against¦68755 Beyt-Tsur, and¦68757 fought against it many days¦68759, and¦68761 made¦68762 engines of war. The Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add* came out¦68765 and¦68766 burnt them with fire¦68770, and¦68771 fought valiantly.
\s1 The battle at Beyt-Zekaryah
\p
\v 32 Yehudah \add !(Judas)\add* marched away¦68777 from¦68777 the¦68778 citadel and¦68780 encamped at Beyt-Zekaryah, near the¦68787 king's¦68788 camp.
\v 33 The¦68791 king¦68792 rose early in¦68798 the¦68802 morning, and¦68805 marched his army\f + \fr 6:33 \ft Or, \fqa itself eager for the fight\f* at full speed along the road¦68803 to Beyt-Zekaryah. His forces made themselves ready to battle¦68811 and¦68812 sounded their trumpets.
\v 34 They offered the elephants the juice of¦68824 grapes and mulberries, that they might prepare them for the battle¦68829.
\v 35 They distributed the¦68832 animals¦68833 among the¦68835 phalanxes. They set by¦68838 each¦68839 elephant a thousand men¦68842 armed with coats of mail and¦68846 helmets of brass on¦68844 their heads¦68851. Five¦68854 hundred¦68854 chosen cavalry were appointed for each¦68857 elephant.
\v 36 These were¦68865 ready beforehand, wherever the¦68866 elephant was¦68868. Wherever the elephant went, they went with it. They didn't leave it.
\v 37 Strong, covered wooden towers were on¦68882 them, one on¦68886 each¦68887 elephant, fastened on¦68890 it¦68891 with secure harnesses. On¦68894 each¦68895 were four valiant men¦68896 who¦68901 fought on¦68903 them, beside his Indian driver.
\v 38 The rest of the cavalry he set on this side and¦68914 that side on¦68917 the¦68918 two¦68919 flanks of the army, striking terror into the enemy, and¦68924 protected by the¦68927 phalanxes.
\v 39 Now when¦68930 the¦68932 sun¦68933 shone on¦68934 the¦68935 shields of gold¦68936 and¦68937 brass, the¦68941 mountains¦68942 lit up, and¦68945 blazed like flaming torches.
\p
\v 40 A part¦68952 of¦68956 the¦68956 king's¦68957 army was spread on¦68958 the¦68959 high¦68960 hills¦68961 and¦68962 some on the low ground, and¦68966 they went¦68967 on firmly and¦68969 in order.
\v 41 All¦68973 who¦68974 heard¦68975 the noise¦68976 of their multitude¦68977, the marching of¦68981 the¦68981 multitude¦68982, and¦68983 the rattling of the weapons¦68986 trembled; for¦68988 the¦68989 army was¦68987 very¦68992 great¦68991 and¦68993 strong¦68994.
\v 42 Yehudah and¦68995 his army drew near¦68996 for battle, and six¦69011 hundred¦69011 men¦69012 of¦69009 the¦69009 king's¦69010 army fell.
\v 43 Eleazar¦69015, who¦69016 was called Avaran, saw¦69031 one of the¦69019 animals¦69020 armed with royal breastplates, and¦69024 it was¦69025 taller than all¦69027 the¦69028 animals¦69029, and¦69030 the¦69036 king¦69037 seemed to be on¦69033 it¦69034.
\v 44 He gave¦69039 his life to¦69042 deliver his people¦69044, and¦69046 to get himself¦69048 an eternal¦69050 name¦69049.
\v 45 He¦69053 ran on him courageously into the middle¦69056 of the¦69057 phalanx, and¦69059 killed on the right¦69061 hand and¦69062 on the left, and¦69064 they parted away¦69066 from¦69066 him on this side and¦69069 on that.
\v 46 He crept under¦69073 the¦69074 elephant, and¦69076 stabbed it¦69078 from beneath, and¦69079 killed it¦69081. The elephant fell to the¦69085 earth¦69086 on him, and he died¦69090 there¦69091.
\v 47 They saw the¦69094 strength¦69095 of the¦69096 kingdom¦69097 and¦69098 the¦69099 fierce attack of the¦69101 army, and¦69103 turned¦69104 away¦69105 from¦69105 them.
\s1 The temple is besieged
\p
\v 48 But¦69108 the¦69110 soldiers of¦69112 the¦69112 king's¦69113 army went up to Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* to meet them, and¦69120 the¦69122 king¦69123 encamped towards¦69124 Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add* and¦69127 towards¦69128 Mt¦69130. Tsiyon \add !(Zion)\add*.
\v 49 He made¦69133 peace¦69134 with¦69135 the¦69136 people of Beyt-Tsur. He came out of the¦69142 city¦69143 because¦69144 they had no¦69145 food¦69149 there¦69148 to endure the¦69150 siege, because it¦69153 was a Sabbath¦69155 to¦69156 the¦69157 land¦69158.
\v 50 The king¦69161 took Beyt-Tsur, and¦69164 appointed a garrison there¦69166 to¦69168 keep¦69168 it¦69169.
\v 51 He encamped against¦69172 the¦69173 sanctuary many days¦69175; and¦69177 set there¦69179 mounds to shoot from, and¦69181 engines of war, and¦69183 machines for throwing fire and¦69185 stones, and¦69187 weapons to throw darts, and¦69193 slings.
\v 52 The Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add* also¦69195 made¦69196 engines of war against their engines, and fought for many days¦69206.
\v 53 But¦69209 there was no¦69210 food¦69208 in¦69212 the¦69213 sanctuary, because¦69215 it was the¦69216 seventh year¦69218, and¦69220 those who fled for safety into Yehudah from¦69226 among the¦69227 Gentiles had eaten up the¦69230 rest of the¦69232 stores.
\v 54 There¦69252 were only a few¦69240 people left in¦69236 the¦69237 sanctuary¦69238, because¦69241 the¦69244 famine prevailed against them, and¦69246 they were scattered, each¦69248 man¦69239 to his own place¦69251.
\s1 The king agrees to peace
\p
\v 55 Lusias¦69255 heard¦69254 that¦69256 Filippos¦69257 \add !(Philip)\add*, whom Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* the¦69260 king¦69261, while he was yet alive¦69264, appointed¦69259 to raise his son¦69268 Antiokos to¦69272 be king,
\v 56 had returned from¦69275 Paras \add !(Persia)\add* and¦69278 Maday \add !(Media)\add*, and¦69280 with him the¦69281 forces that¦69283 went with the¦69285 king¦69286, and¦69289 that¦69290 he was seeking¦69291 to¦69292 take¦69292 control of the¦69293 government.
\v 57 He hurried, and gave orders to depart. He said¦69300 to¦69301 the¦69302 king¦69303 and¦69304 the¦69305 leaders of the¦69307 army and¦69309 to¦69313 the¦69316 men¦69311, “We get weaker daily, our food¦69317 is scant, the¦69321 place¦69322 where we encamp is¦69325 strong, and¦69327 the¦69330 affairs of the¦69331 kingdom¦69332 lie¦69328 on¦69328 us.
\v 58 Now¦69333 therefore¦69334 let's negotiate with these men, and¦69340 make¦69341 peace¦69344 with them and¦69345 with¦69346 all¦69347 their nation¦69348,
\v 59 and¦69350 covenant with them, that they may walk after their own laws, as before; for because¦69360 of¦69360 their laws which¦69365 we abolished they were angered¦69367, and¦69368 did¦69369 all¦69371 these things.”
\p
\v 60 The¦69374 speech pleased¦69373 the¦69377 king¦69378 and¦69379 the¦69380 princes, and¦69382 he sent¦69383 to¦69383 them to¦69384 make peace; and they accepted it.
\v 61 The¦69392 king¦69393 and¦69394 the¦69395 princes swore¦69390 to them. On these conditions, they came out from¦69400 the¦69401 stronghold.
\v 62 Then¦69403 the¦69405 king¦69406 entered¦69404 into¦69412 Mt¦69409. Tsiyon \add !(Zion)\add*. He saw the¦69413 strength of¦69415 the¦69415 place¦69416, and¦69417 broke the¦69419 oath which¦69421 he'd sworn¦69422, and¦69423 gave orders¦69424 to¦69425 pull down¦69425 the¦69426 wall¦69427 all around¦69428.
\v 63 Then he left in haste and¦69429 returned to¦69431 Antiokeia, and found¦69438 Filippos master of the¦69441 city¦69442. He¦69446 fought¦69444 against him, and¦69447 took the¦69449 city¦69450 by force¦69451.
\c 7
\s1 Demetrios sends Bakides and Alkimos
\p
\v 1 In the one¦69453 hundred and fifty first year,\f + \fr 7:1 \ft circa B.C. 162.\f* Demetrios the¦69460 son of¦69461 Seleukos \add !(Seleucus)\add* came out¦69463 of Romai, and¦69465 went¦69458 up with¦69467 a few¦69469 men¦69468 to a city¦69471 by the sea, and¦69473 reigned¦69474 there¦69475.
\v 2 When¦69476 he'd go into¦69479 the house¦69481 of the kingdom¦69482 of his fathers¦69483, that¦69486 the¦69488 army laid hands on Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* and¦69490 Lusias, to¦69493 bring¦69493 them to him.
\v 3 The¦69499 thing became known¦69497 to him, and he said¦69502, “Don't¦69503 show me their faces¦69507!”
\v 4 So¦69509 the¦69512 army killed¦69510 them. Then¦69514 Demetrios sat on¦69517 the throne¦69518 of his kingdom¦69519.
\p
\v 5 All¦69525 the lawless and¦69528 ungodly¦69529 men¦69526 of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* came¦69522 to¦69523 him. Alkimos¦69533 was their leader, desiring to be high priest¦69537.
\v 6 They accused the¦69540 people¦69541 to¦69542 the¦69543 king¦69544, saying, “Yehudah and¦69548 his kindred have destroyed¦69546 all your¦69551 friends¦69553, and¦69555 have scattered us from¦69558 our own land¦69560.
\v 7 Now¦69562 therefore¦69563 send¦69564 a man¦69565 whom you trust¦69567, and let him go and see all the destruction which¦69574 he's brought on us and¦69577 the¦69580 king's¦69581 country¦69579, and¦69582 how he's¦69584 punished them and¦69585 all¦69586 who¦69587 helped them.”
\v 8 So¦69590 the¦69592 king¦69593 chose Bakides, one of¦69598 the¦69598 king's¦69599\f + \fr 7:8 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* friends¦69597, who was ruler in¦69601 the¦69602 country beyond the¦69604 river¦69605, and¦69606 was a great¦69607 man in¦69608 the¦69609 kingdom¦69610, and¦69611 faithful¦69612 to the¦69613 king¦69614.
\v 9 He¦69617 sent¦69616 him and¦69618 that¦69620 ungodly¦69621 Alkimos, whom he¦69624 made¦69630 the¦69625 high priest¦69626; and¦69627 he¦69629 commanded him to take vengeance¦69632 on¦69633 the¦69634 children¦69635 of Yisrael.
\p
\v 10 They marched away and came¦69640 with¦69641 a great army into the land¦69645 of Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add*. He sent¦69648 messengers to¦69650 Yehudah and¦69652 his kindred with¦69658 words¦69656 of peace deceitfully¦69659.
\v 11 They paid no¦69661 attention to their words¦69664; for¦69667 they saw that¦69668 they'd come¦69669 with¦69670 a great army.
\v 12 A group of scribes¦69680 gathered together to Alkimos and Bakides to seek just¦69682 terms.
\v 13 The¦69685\f + \fr 7:13 \ft That is, Chasidim.\f* Hasidim were¦69687 the first¦69684 among¦69688 the children¦69689 of Yisrael who sought¦69692 peace¦69695 from them,
\v 14 for¦69697 they said¦69696, “One who's a¦69698 priest¦69699 of¦69701 the¦69701 seed¦69702 of Aharon \add !(Aaron)\add* has come¦69704 with the¦69706 army, and¦69708 he'll do us no¦69709 wrong.”
\v 15 He spoke¦69713 with¦69714 them words¦69716 of peace, and¦69718 swore¦69719 to¦69719 them, saying, “We won't seek to¦69721 harm¦69725 you¦69729 or your friends¦69728.”
\v 16 They trusted him. Then¦69730 he¦69732 seized¦69734 sixty¦69737 men¦69738 of them, and¦69739 killed¦69740 them in¦69742 one day¦69743, according¦69745 to¦69745 the¦69746 word¦69747 which¦69748 was written¦69749,
\q1
\v 17 The flesh¦69750 of your saints\f + \fr 7:17 \ft Psalms 79:2, 3.\f*
\q2 and¦69753 their blood was shed all around Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*,
\q2 and¦69759 there was no¦69760 one to¦69761 bury them.
\p
\v 18 The¦69768 fear¦69769 and¦69770 the¦69771 dread of them fell¦69766 onto all¦69774 the¦69775 people¦69776, for they said¦69778, “There's¦69780 neither truth¦69783 nor justice¦69785 in them; for¦69787 they've broken the¦69788 covenant and¦69790 the¦69791 oath¦69792 which¦69793 they swore.”
\v 19 Bakides withdrew from¦69798 Yerushalem, and¦69800 encamped in¦69802 Bezeth. He sent¦69805 and¦69806 seized¦69807 many of the deserters who were with him, and¦69815 some of¦69817 the¦69817 people¦69818, and¦69819 he¦69821 killed them, throwing them into a large¦69826 pit.
\v 20 He placed Alkimos in charge¦69828 of the¦69829 country¦69830 and¦69833 left with¦69835 him a force to¦69842 aid him. Then Bakides went¦69842 away¦69842 to¦69844 the¦69845 king¦69846.
\p
\v 21 Alkimos¦69849 struggled to maintain his high priesthood.
\v 22 All¦69857 those who¦69858 troubled¦69859 their people¦69861 joined him, and¦69863 they took control of the land¦69865 of Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add*, and¦69867 did¦69868 great¦69870 damage in¦69871 Yisrael.
\v 23 Yehudah saw all¦69876 the¦69877 wrongs that¦69879 Alkimos¦69881 and¦69882 his company had done¦69880 among¦69886 the¦69883 children¦69887 of Yisrael, even more than the¦69890 Gentiles.
\v 24 He went¦69893 out¦69893 into all¦69895 the borders of Yehudah and¦69901 took vengeance¦69903 on¦69904 the¦69905 men¦69906 who'd¦69907 deserted from him, and¦69909 they were restrained from going out into the¦69914 country¦69915.
\v 25 But¦69917 when Alkimos¦69919 saw that¦69920 Yehudah and¦69923 his company had grown strong, and¦69927 knew¦69928 that¦69929 he wasn't¦69931 able¦69931 to withstand them, he returned to the¦69937 king¦69938, and¦69939 brought evil¦69942 accusations against them.
\s1 Nikanor attacks Yehudah
\p
\v 26 Then¦69943\f + \fr 7:26 \ft See 2 Maccabees 14:12.\f* the¦69945 king¦69946 sent¦69944 Nikanor, one¦69948 of his honourable princes, a man who hated Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* and was their enemy, and commanded him to¦69961 destroy the¦69964 people¦69965.
\v 27 Nikanor¦69968 came¦69967 to¦69974 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* with a great army. He sent¦69974 to¦69975 Yehudah and¦69977 his kindred deceitfully¦69982 with¦69981 words¦69983 of peace, saying,
\v 28 “Let there be¦69987 no battle between me and¦69991 you¦69992; I'll come¦69993 with a few¦69996 men¦69995, that¦69997 I may see your faces¦70001 in peace¦70003.”
\v 29 He came¦70005 to¦70006 Yehudah, and¦70008 they saluted one¦70010 another¦70010 peaceably. The¦70013 enemies were¦70015 ready¦70016 to seize Yehudah by violence.
\v 30 This was known¦70021 to Yehudah, that¦70026 he came¦70029 to him with¦70027 deceit¦70028, and¦70032 he¦70035 was very afraid of him, and¦70036 would see his face¦70042 no¦70037 more.
\v 31 Nikanor¦70046 found out that¦70047 his plan¦70050 was disclosed; and he¦70051 went¦70053 out¦70053 to meet Yehudah in¦70058 battle¦70059 beside Kefar-Shalama.
\v 32 About¦70067 five¦70068 hundred men¦70069 of Nikanor's army fell, and¦70070 the rest fled¦70071 into the¦70073 city¦70074 of David.
\s1 Nikanor threatens the temple
\p
\v 33 After¦70077 these things, Nikanor¦70082 went¦70088 up to¦70088 Mt¦70085. Tsiyon \add !(Zion)\add*. Some of the¦70090 priests¦70091 came out¦70092 of the¦70093 sanctuary¦70094, with some of¦70099 the¦70099 people's¦70100 elders¦70098, to salute him peaceably, and¦70104 to¦70105 show¦70105 him the¦70107 whole burnt sacrifice that¦70109 was being offered for¦70111 the¦70112 king¦70113.
\v 34 He mocked them, laughed at them, derided them shamefully,\f + \fr 7:34 \ft Grk. \fqa polluted them.\f* spoke¦70124 arrogantly,
\v 35 and¦70126 swore¦70127 in a rage, saying, “Unless Yehudah and¦70135 his army are now¦70143 delivered into my¦70138 hands¦70140, it'll be¦70145 that, if¦70146 I return¦70147 safely, I'll burn up this¦70151 house¦70152!” And he went¦70155 out¦70155 in a great¦70158 rage.
\v 36 The¦70161 priests¦70162 entered¦70160 in, and¦70163 stood¦70164 before the¦70167 altar¦70168 and¦70169 the¦70170 temple¦70171; and¦70172 they wept, and¦70174 said¦70175,
\v 37 “You¦70176 chose this¦70179 house¦70180 to be called by your name¦70184, to be¦70188 a house¦70189 of prayer¦70190 and¦70191 supplication for your people¦70194.
\v 38 Take vengeance¦70197 on¦70198 this¦70199 man¦70200 and his army, and let them fall by the sword¦70210. Remember¦70211 their blasphemies, and¦70215 don't¦70216 allow them to¦70217 live any longer.”
\s1 Yehudah defeats Nikanor
\p
\v 39 Then¦70220 Nikanor¦70222 went¦70221 out¦70223 from¦70223 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* and¦70225 encamped in¦70227 Beyt-Horon, and¦70229 there the Arami \add !(Syrian)\add* army met¦70230 him.
\v 40 Yehudah encamped in¦70237 Adasa¦70238 with three thousand men¦70241. Yehudah prayed¦70243 and¦70245 said¦70246,
\v 41 “When¦70252 those who¦70247 came from¦70248 the¦70249 king¦70250 blasphemed, your angel¦70256 went¦70254 out¦70254, and¦70259 struck¦70260 among¦70261 them one hundred¦70263 and eighty-five¦70264 thousand.
\v 42 Even so, crush this army before¦70271 us today¦70273, and¦70274 let all the¦70276 rest know that¦70278 he's spoken¦70280 wickedly against¦70281 your sanctuary¦70283. Judge him according¦70288 to¦70288 his wickedness¦70290.”
\v 43 On the thirteenth day of¦70300 the¦70300 month Adar¦70302, the¦70305 armies met in battle. Nikanor's army was defeated, and¦70308 he¦70310 himself was the first¦70311 to fall in¦70312 the¦70313 battle¦70314.
\v 44 Now when his army saw that¦70321 Nikanor¦70323 had fallen, they threw¦70324 away their weapons¦70326 and fled¦70328.
\v 45 They pursued them a day's¦70333 journey from¦70335 Adasa¦70336 until¦70337 you come¦70339 to\f + \fr 7:45 \ft Grk. \fqa Gazera.\f* Gezer, and¦70342 they sounded an alarm after¦70344 them with the signal trumpets.
\v 46 Men came out of all¦70353 the¦70354 surrounding¦70358 villages of Yehudah, and outflanked them. These turned them back on those, and they all¦70369 fell by the sword¦70370. There wasn't one of them left¦70373.
\v 47 The Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add* took¦70379 the¦70380 spoils and¦70382 the¦70383 booty, and¦70385 they cut off Nikanor's head¦70387 and¦70390 his right¦70392 hand, which¦70394 he'd stretched¦70395 out¦70395 so arrogantly, and¦70397 brought them, and¦70399 hung them up beside Yerushalem.
\v 48 The people¦70407 were extremely glad, and¦70409 they kept that¦70413 day¦70412 as a day¦70414 of great¦70416 gladness¦70415.
\v 49 They\f + \fr 7:49 \ft See 2 Maccabees 15:36.\f* ordained to keep this day year by year on the thirteenth day of¦70428 Adar¦70429.
\v 50 So¦70430 the¦70432 land¦70433 of Yehudah had rest a few¦70436 days¦70435.
\c 8
\s1 Yehudah hears about the Romaios
\p
\v 1 Yehudah heard¦70438 of the¦70440 fame of the¦70442 Romaios, that¦70444 they're¦70445 valiant men, and¦70448 have pleasure in¦70451 all¦70452 who¦70453 join themselves to them, and make friends with all who¦70465 come to¦70466 them,
\v 2 and¦70469 that¦70484 they're valiant men. They told him of their wars¦70473 and¦70475 exploits which¦70478 they do¦70479 among¦70480 the¦70481 Gauls, and¦70483 how they conquered them, and¦70487 forced them to¦70488 pay tribute;
\v 3 and¦70492 what things they did¦70494 in¦70495 the¦70498 land of Spania, that¦70500 they might take control of¦70502 the¦70502 silver and¦70504 gold¦70506 mines which were there¦70508;
\v 4 and how by their policy and persistence they conquered all¦70513 the¦70514 place (and the¦70521 place¦70522 was¦70523 extremely far from¦70526 them), and¦70529 the¦70530 kings¦70531 who¦70532 came against¦70534 them from¦70536 the uttermost part of the¦70538 earth¦70539, until¦70540 they'd defeated them, and¦70543 struck them severely; and¦70549 how the¦70550 rest give¦70552 them tribute year by year.
\v 5 Filippos \add !(Philip)\add*, and Perseus, king¦70564 of Kitim, and¦70565 those who¦70566 lifted up themselves against¦70568 them, they defeated in¦70572 battle¦70573, and¦70574 conquered them.
\v 6 Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* also¦70577, the¦70579 great¦70580 king¦70581 of Asia, came against¦70586 them to¦70590 battle¦70589, having¦70590 one hundred¦70591 and twenty¦70592 elephants, with cavalry, chariots, and a very¦70601 great army, and¦70602 he¦70605 was defeated by them.
\v 7 They took¦70607 him alive¦70609, and¦70610 decreed that both he and those who¦70617 reigned after¦70619 him should give them a great¦70622 tribute, and should give¦70623 hostages, and¦70625 a parcel of land from the best of their provinces:
\v 8 the¦70629 countries¦70628 of Hodu, Maday \add !(Media)\add*, and Ludia. They took¦70642 them from¦70636 him, and¦70641 gave¦70646 them to King¦70650 Eumenes.
\v 9 Yehudah heard how the Hellains \add !(Greeks)\add* planned¦70657 to¦70658 come¦70658 and¦70659 destroy them,
\v 10 but¦70662 this became known¦70663 to them, and they sent¦70668 against them a general who fought against them, and many of them fell down wounded to death, and they made captive their wives and their children¦70690, and¦70692 plundered them, and¦70695 conquered their land¦70698, and pulled down their strongholds, and plundered them, and brought them into bondage to this¦70709 day¦70710.
\v 11 The¦70713 remaining kingdoms¦70715 and¦70716 islands, as many as rose up against them at any time, they destroyed and made them to¦70721 be their servants;
\v 12 but with their friends and¦70738 those who¦70740 relied on them they stayed friends. They conquered the¦70742 kingdoms that were near¦70743 and¦70744 those that were far off, and¦70747 all that heard¦70749 of their fame were afraid¦70753 of them.
\v 13 What's more, whoever they desired to help and to make kings, these they make kings; and whoever they desired, they depose. They're exalted greatly.
\v 14 Because all¦70774 this¦70775, none¦70778 of them ever put on a crown, neither did they clothe themselves with purple¦70784, as a display of grandeur.
\v 15 Yehudah heard how they'd made¦70791 for themselves a senate house, and¦70793 day by day, three¦70797 hundred¦70797 and¦70798 twenty¦70799 men sat in council, consulting always¦70801 for the¦70803 people¦70804, to the¦70805 end they might be well governed,
\v 16 and¦70808 how they commit their government to¦70809 one¦70810 man¦70810 year by year, that he¦70814 should rule over them, and¦70817 control all¦70819 their country, and¦70823 all¦70824 are obedient to¦70825 that one¦70827, and¦70828 there's¦70830 neither envy¦70831 nor emulation among¦70834 them.
\s1 An alliance with Romai
\p
\v 17 So¦70836 Yehudah chose Eupolemos the¦70839 son¦70841 of¦70843 Yohan \add !(John)\add*, the¦70843 son of Hakots, and¦70845 Yason the son¦70847 of Eleazar, and¦70849 sent¦70850 them to¦70850 Romai, to¦70854 establish friendship and¦70857 alliance with them,
\v 18 and¦70859 that they should free the¦70862 yoke¦70863 from¦70864 themselves; for they saw that¦70866 the¦70868 kingdom¦70869 of the Hellains \add !(Greeks)\add* kept Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* in bondage.
\v 19 Then¦70876 they went to¦70877 Romai, a very¦70884 long journey, and¦70885 they entered¦70886 into the¦70888 senate house, and said¦70893,
\v 20 “Yehudah, who's¦70895 also called Makabi \add !(Maccabaeus)\add*, and¦70897 his kindred, and¦70901 the¦70902 people¦70903 of the¦70904 Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add*, have sent¦70906 us to¦70908 you¦70909, to¦70910 make an alliance and¦70914 peace¦70915 with you, and¦70916 that we¦70918 might be registered as your allies and¦70920 friends¦70921.”
\p
\v 21 This¦70925 thing was pleasing¦70924 to them.
\v 22 This¦70930 is the¦70931 copy of the¦70933 writing which¦70935 they wrote back again on¦70937 tables of brass, and¦70940 sent¦70941 to¦70944 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, that it might be¦70944 with¦70945 them there¦70947 for a memorial¦70948 of peace¦70949 and¦70950 alliance:
\p
\v 23 “Good success be to the Romaios, and¦70955 to the¦70956 nation¦70957 of the¦70960 Yehudim, by sea¦70961 and¦70962 by land forever. May the sword¦70970 and¦70971 the enemy¦70972 be far from¦70974 them.
\v 24 But if¦70976 war¦70979 arises for Romai first, or¦70983 any of their allies in¦70988 all¦70989 their dominion,
\v 25 the¦70993 nation¦70994 of the¦70995 Yehudim must help them as allies, as the¦70999 occasion will indicate to them, with all their heart¦71003.
\v 26 To those who make war on them, they mustn't give¦71009 supplies, food, weapons¦71013, money¦71014, or ships, as it's¦71023 seemed good to¦71025 Romai, and they must keep their ordinances without taking¦71025 anything in return.
\v 27 In the¦71027 same way¦71041, moreover, if¦71030 war¦71035 comes first on the nation¦71031 of the Yehudim, the Romaios must willingly help them as allies, as the occasion will indicate to them;
\v 28 and¦71047 to those who are fighting with them, there mustn't be given¦71051 food, weapons¦71053, money¦71054, or ships, as it's¦71063 seemed good to¦71057 Romai. They must keep these ordinances, and¦71059 that¦71061 without deceit¦71067.
\v 29 According¦71068 to¦71068 these terms, the Romaios made a treaty with the¦71076 Jewish¦71077 people.
\v 30 But if in the future the one party and the other decide to¦71088 add¦71088 or¦71089 diminish anything, they may do so by mutual agreement, and¦71095 whatever they add or¦71099 take¦71090 away will be¦71101 ratified.
\p
\v 31 About¦71104 the¦71105 evils¦71106 which¦71107 King¦71109 Demetrios is doing to¦71116 them, we've¦71125 written to him, saying, ‘Why¦71117 have you made your yoke¦71120 heavy on¦71122 our friends¦71124 and allies the¦71126 Yehudim?
\v 32 If¦71129 therefore¦71130 they plead any more against you¦71134, we'll do¦71135 them justice¦71138, and¦71139 fight with you¦71141 on sea¦71144 and¦71145 on land.’ ”
\c 9
\s1 Yehudah's last battle
\p
\v 1 Demetrios heard¦71150 that¦71152 Nikanor¦71154 had fallen with his forces in¦71159 battle¦71160, and¦71155 he¦71158 sent¦71170 Bakides and¦71161 Alkimos again into¦71162 the land¦71172 of Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add* a second time, and¦71174 the¦71175 right¦71176 wing of his army with¦71178 them.
\v 2 They went by the way that leads to Gilgal, and¦71186 encamped against¦71188 Mesaloth, which is in¦71191 Arbela, and¦71193 took possession of it¦71195, and¦71196 killed many people.
\v 3 The¦71204 first¦71205 month of¦71207 the¦71207 one hundred and fifty-second year,\f + \fr 9:3 \ft circa B.C. 161.\f* they encamped against¦71214 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*.
\v 4 Then¦71216 they marched away and¦71218 went to¦71219 Beroia with twenty¦71223 thousand¦71224 infantry and¦71226 two thousand cavalry.
\v 5 Yehudah was¦71231 encamped at Elasa with three¦71236 thousand¦71236 chosen men¦71237.
\v 6 They saw the¦71243 multitude¦71244 of the¦71245 forces, that¦71247 they were¦71249 many, and they were terrified. Many slipped away¦71256 out¦71261 of the army. There weren't left of them more than¦71264 eight¦71265 hundred¦71265 men¦71266.
\p
\v 7 Yehudah saw that his army slipped away and¦71267 that¦71270 the¦71272 battle¦71277 pressed on him, and¦71275 he¦71279 was very troubled in spirit¦71283, because¦71284 he had no¦71285 time¦71287 to¦71288 gather¦71288 them together, and he¦71289 became faint.
\v 8 He said¦71293 to¦71293 those who¦71294 were left, “Let's arise and¦71297 go up against¦71299 our adversaries, if¦71303 perhaps we may be able to¦71306 fight¦71306 with them.”
\p
\v 9 They tried to¦71311 dissuade him, saying, “There's no¦71312 way we're able; but¦71315 let's rather save our lives now¦71322. Let's return again with¦71325 our kindred, and¦71329 fight against them; but¦71334 we're too few¦71335.”
\p
\v 10 Yehudah said¦71337, “Let it not¦71339 be¦71341 so that I should do¦71342 this¦71343 thing¦71344, to¦71346 flee¦71346 from¦71347 them. If¦71350 our time¦71353 has come¦71351, let's die¦71356 in¦71357 a manly way for¦71359 our kindred's sake, and¦71363 not¦71364 leave a cause¦71366 of reproach against our honour¦71368.”
\p
\v 11 The army marched out from the camp, and stood to encounter them. The cavalry was divided into two companies, and the slingers and the archers went before the army, and all the mighty men that fought in the front of the battle.
\v 12 Bakides was in the right wing. The phalanx advanced on the two parts, and they blew with their trumpets.
\v 13 The men by Yehudah’ side sounded¦71438 with their trumpets, and¦71432 the¦71434 earth¦71435 shook¦71433 with the¦71437 shout of the¦71439 armies, and¦71441 the¦71443 battle¦71444 was joined, and continued from¦71447 morning¦71447 until¦71448 evening¦71449.
\p
\v 14 Yehudah saw that¦71453 Bakides and¦71455 the¦71456 strength¦71457 of his army were on¦71460 the¦71461 right¦71462 side, and¦71463 all¦71466 that were brave in heart¦71470 went with him,
\v 15 and¦71471 the¦71473 right¦71474 wing was defeated by them, and he pursued¦71479 after¦71480 them to the mount¦71484 Azotos.
\v 16 Those who¦71486 were on the¦71488 left wing saw that¦71492 the¦71494 right¦71495 wing was defeated, and¦71497 they turned¦71498 and followed in the footsteps of Yehudah and of those who were with¦71504 him.
\v 17 The¦71511 battle¦71512 became desperate, and¦71513 many on both sides fell wounded to¦71514 death.
\v 18 Yehudah fell, and the¦71526 rest fled¦71528.
\p
\v 19 Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* and¦71529 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* took¦71530 Yehudah their brother¦71536, and¦71538 buried¦71539 him in¦71541 the tomb of his ancestors at Modi'in.
\v 20 They wept for him. All¦71555 Yisrael made great¦71558 lamentation¦71557 for him, and¦71559 mourned many days¦71561, and¦71563 said¦71564,
\v 21 “How¦71565 is the mighty fallen, the saviour of Yisrael!”
\v 22 The¦71572 rest of the¦71574 acts of Yehudah, and¦71577 his wars¦71579, and¦71580 the¦71581 valiant actions which¦71583 he¦71588 did¦71584, and¦71585 his greatness, aren't written; for¦71592 they were¦71593 very¦71594 many.
\s1 Yonatan takes over the leadership
\p
\v 23 After¦71597 Yehudah's death, the¦71602 lawless emerged within all¦71605 the¦71606 borders of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*. All¦71611 those who did iniquity rose up.
\v 24 In¦71616 those days¦71618 there was¦71620 a very¦71623 great¦71622 famine, and¦71624 the¦71626 country¦71627 went over to their side.
\v 25 Bakides chose the¦71633 ungodly¦71634 men¦71635 and¦71636 made them rulers of the¦71640 country¦71641.
\v 26 They enquired and searched for Yehudah's friends¦71647, and¦71649 brought them to¦71652 Bakides, and¦71654 he took vengeance on¦71656 them and¦71658 used them despitefully.
\v 27 There was¦71662 great¦71664 suffering in¦71665 Yisrael, such as wasn't since the¦71666 time¦71673 prophets¦71676 stopped appearing to¦71675 them.
\p
\v 28 All¦71681 Yehudah's friends¦71683 were gathered together, and¦71685 they said¦71686 to¦71686 Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add*,
\v 29 “Since your brother¦71692 Yehudah has died, we have no¦71700 man¦71697 like¦71698 him to¦71702 go¦71702 out¦71702 against our enemies¦71705 and¦71706 Bakides, and¦71708 among¦71709 those of¦71712 our nation¦71713 who hate us.
\v 30 Now¦71715 therefore¦71716 we've chosen you¦71717 this¦71731 day to¦71721 be¦71721 our prince and¦71727 leader¦71726 in his place, that you may fight¦71730 our battles.”
\v 31 So¦71734 Yonatan took the¦71738 governance on him at that¦71740 time¦71739, and rose up in the place of¦71747 his brother¦71748 Yehudah.
\p
\v 32 When Bakides found out, he¦71755 tried¦71754 to¦71756 kill¦71756 him.
\v 33 Yonatan, and Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* his brother¦71763, and¦71765 all¦71766 who were with¦71768 him, knew¦71758 it¦71769; and¦71770 they fled¦71771 into the¦71773 wilderness of Tekoa, and¦71776 encamped by the¦71779 water¦71780 of the pool of Asphar.
\v 34 Bakides found this¦71786 out on the¦71788 Sabbath¦71789 day¦71787, and¦71790 came¦71791—he¦71792 and¦71793 all¦71794 his army—over the Yarden \add !(Jordan)\add*.
\s1 Yonatan and Shim'on avenge their brother
\p
\v 35 Yonatan sent¦71802 his brother¦71805, a leader of¦71808 the¦71808 multitude, and¦71810 implored his friends¦71814 the¦71818 Nabataeans, that¦71821 they might store their baggage, which was much¦71822, with them.
\v 36 The children¦71825 of Jambri came out¦71827 of Meydeva, and¦71829 seized¦71830 Yohan \add !(John)\add* and¦71832 all¦71833 that he had¦71835, and¦71836 went¦71837 their way¦71834 with it.
\p
\v 37 But after these things, they brought word¦71842 to¦71844 Yonatan and¦71847 Shim'on his brother¦71850 that¦71852 the¦71853 children¦71854 of Jambri were celebrating a great wedding¦71857, and¦71859 were bringing¦71860 the¦71861 bride¦71862, a daughter¦71865 of one¦71866 of the¦71867 great¦71869 nobles of Kena'an \add !(Canaan)\add*, from¦71863 Nadabath¦71864 with¦71872 a large¦71874 escort.
\v 38 They remembered¦71876 Yohan their brother¦71879, and¦71881 went up, and¦71883 hid themselves under¦71885 the¦71886 cover of¦71888 the¦71888 mountain¦71889.
\v 39 They lifted up¦71891 their eyes¦71893 and looked¦71898, and¦71900 saw a great procession with much¦71902 baggage. The¦71904 bridegroom¦71905 came out¦71906 with his friends¦71909 and¦71911 his kindred to meet them with¦71918 timbrels, musicians¦71921, and¦71922 many weapons¦71923.
\v 40 They rose up¦71926 against¦71927 them from¦71929 their ambush and¦71936 killed¦71937 them, and¦71939 many fell wounded to¦71940 death. The¦71944 remnant fled¦71946 into the¦71948 mountain¦71949, and¦71950 the Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add* took¦71951 all¦71952 their spoils.
\v 41 So¦71956 the¦71958 wedding¦71959 was turned into mourning, and¦71962 the¦71963 voice¦71964 of their musicians¦71965 into lamentation.
\v 42 They avenged fully their brother's¦71974 blood¦71973, and¦71976 turned back to the¦71979 marshes¦71980 of¦71981 the¦71981 Yarden.
\s1 Yonatan escapes across the Yarden
\p
\v 43 Bakides heard¦71984 it, and¦71986 he came¦71987 on the¦71990 Sabbath¦71991 day¦71989 to the¦71993 banks of¦71995 Yarden \add !(Jordan)\add* with a great army.
\v 44 Yonatan said¦72001 to¦72001 his company, “Let's stand up now¦72007 and¦72008 fight for¦72010 our lives, for¦72015 things are¦72016 different today¦72017 than they were yesterday¦72019 and¦72020 the day¦72022 before.
\v 45 Because¦72024 the¦72025 battle¦72026 is before us and¦72029 behind us. Moreover the¦72032 water¦72034 of¦72035 the¦72035 Yarden is on this side and¦72038 on that side, and¦72040 marsh¦72041 and¦72042 thicket. There's no¦72044 place¦72046 to escape.
\v 46 Now¦72049 therefore¦72050 cry to heaven¦72053, that¦72054 you may be delivered out¦72056 of your enemies'¦72058 hand¦72057.”
\v 47 So¦72060 the¦72062 battle¦72063 was joined, and¦72064 Yonatan stretched¦72065 out¦72065 his hand¦72068 to¦72070 strike¦72070 Bakides, and¦72073 he turned away¦72075 back from¦72075 him.
\v 48 Yonatan and those who¦72084 were with¦72085 him leapt into the¦72088 Yarden, and¦72090 swam over to the¦72093 other¦72094 side¦72094. The enemy didn't pass over the Yarden against them.
\v 49 About a thousand men¦72111 of Bakides’ company fell that¦72108 day¦72107;
\v 50 and he returned to Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*. They built¦72117 strong cities¦72118 in¦72120 Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add*, the¦72123 stronghold¦72124 that¦72125 was in¦72126 Yeriho \add !(Jericho)\add*, and Emmaous, Beyt-Horon, Beyt-El \add !(Bethel)\add*, Timnah, Pireaton, and Tephon, with high¦72146 walls and¦72147 gates and¦72149 bars.
\v 51 He¦72155 set garrisons in¦72154 them to¦72152 harass Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*.
\v 52 He fortified the¦72162 city¦72163 Beyt-Tsur, Gezer, and the citadel, and put troops and stores of food¦72180 in them.
\v 53 He took¦72182 the¦72183 sons¦72184 of the¦72185 chief men of the¦72187 country¦72188 for hostages, and¦72190 put them under guard in¦72193 the¦72194 citadel at Yerushalem.
\s1 The death of Alkimos
\p
\v 54 And¦72200 in¦72201 the one hundred and fifty-third year¦72202,\f + \fr 9:54 \ft circa B.C. 160.\f* in the¦72209 second¦72210 month¦72208, Alkimos¦72212 gave orders to pull down the¦72214 wall¦72215 of the¦72216 inner courtyard¦72217 of the¦72218 sanctuary¦72219. He also¦72222 pulled down¦72223 the¦72224 works¦72225 of¦72230 the¦72230 prophets¦72227.
\v 55 He began to pull down. At that¦72235 time¦72234 was Alkimos¦72237 stricken¦72236, and¦72238 his works¦72241 were hindered; and¦72243 his mouth¦72246 was stopped, and he was taken with a palsy, and he could no¦72251 more speak¦72254 anything and¦72256 give orders about¦72258 his house¦72260.
\v 56 Alkimos¦72264 died¦72263 at that¦72268 time¦72267 with¦72269 great¦72271 torment¦72270.
\v 57 Bakides saw that¦72275 Alkimos¦72277 was dead, and¦72278 he returned to¦72280 the¦72281 king¦72282. Then¦72283 the¦72285 land¦72286 of Yehudah had rest for two¦72289 years¦72288.
\s1 Yonatan defeats Bakides and makes peace
\p
\v 58 Then¦72290 all¦72292 the¦72293 lawless men took counsel, saying, “Listen, Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* and his men are dwelling at ease and in¦72302 security. Now¦72306 therefore¦72307 we'll bring Bakides, and¦72311 he'll¦72313 capture them all¦72314 in¦72315 one night¦72316.
\v 59 They went and¦72318 consulted¦72320 with him.
\v 60 He marched out and¦72322 came¦72325 with¦72326 a great army, and¦72329 sent¦72330 letters secretly to¦72330 all¦72333 his allies who were in¦72338 Yehudah, that¦72341 they should seize Yonatan and¦72345 those who¦72346 were with¦72347 him; but¦72349 they couldn't, because¦72352 their plan¦72356 was known¦72353 to them.
\v 61 Yonatan's men seized about fifty¦72370 of the¦72361 men¦72362 of the¦72363 country¦72364 who¦72365 were authors of the¦72367 wickedness¦72368, and¦72372 he¦72374 killed¦72373 them.
\v 62 Yonatan, Shim'on, and those who¦72381 were with¦72382 him, went away to¦72391 Beyt-Basi, which is in¦72387 the¦72388 wilderness, and¦72390 he built¦72391 up that¦72392 which had been pulled down, and¦72395 they made it¦72397 strong.
\v 63 Bakides found out¦72409 about it, and he gathered together all¦72403 his multitude¦72405, and¦72407 sent orders¦72412 to those who were of Yehudah.
\v 64 He went¦72414 and¦72413 encamped against¦72416 Beyt-Basi and¦72418 fought¦72419 against it¦72420 many days¦72421, and¦72423 made¦72424 engines of war.
\p
\v 65 Yonatan left his brother¦72431 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* in¦72433 the¦72434 city¦72435, and¦72436 went¦72437 out¦72437 into the¦72439 country¦72440, and¦72441 he went¦72442 with a few men.
\v 66 He struck¦72446 Odomera and¦72448 his kindred, and¦72452 the¦72453 children¦72454 of Phasiron in¦72456 their tents¦72458.
\v 67 They began to strike them, and¦72467 to¦72473 go¦72473 up with their forces. Then Shim'on and¦72469 those who¦72470 were with¦72471 him went out of the¦72475 city¦72476, and¦72477 set the¦72479 engines of war on fire,
\v 68 and¦72481 fought against Bakides, and¦72486 he was defeated by¦72488 them. They afflicted him severely; for his counsel and¦72490 expedition was¦72495 in vain.
\v 69 They were very¦72521 angry with the¦72508 lawless¦72509 men¦72507 who¦72510 gave him counsel to¦72513 come¦72513 into the¦72515 country¦72516, and¦72517 they killed¦72518 many of¦72524 them. Then he decided to¦72525 depart into his own land¦72528.
\p
\v 70 Yonatan learnt of this and sent¦72534 ambassadors to¦72534 him, to¦72535 the¦72538 end that they should make peace¦72542 with him, and¦72543 that he should restore to them the¦72546 captives¦72547.
\v 71 He accepted the thing, and did¦72551 according¦72552 to¦72552 his words¦72554, and¦72556 swore¦72557 to¦72557 him that he¦72558 wouldn't¦72559 seek his harm¦72562 all¦72563 the¦72564 days¦72565 of his life¦72567.
\v 72 He restored to him the¦72572 captives¦72575 which¦72574 he'd taken¦72575 before out¦72577 of the land of Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add*, and he¦72586 returned and¦72587 departed into his own land, and didn't come¦72591 any more into their borders.
\v 73 Thus the sword¦72598 ceased from¦72599 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*. Yonatan lived at Mikmas. Yonatan began to¦72609 judge¦72609 the¦72610 people¦72611; and¦72612 he destroyed the¦72614 ungodly¦72615 out¦72616 of Yisrael.
\c 10
\s1 Rival kings seek Yonatan's support
\p
\v 1 In¦72619 the one hundred sixtieth year¦72620,\f + \fr 10:1 \ft circa B.C. 153.\f* Alexandros¦72625 \add !(Alexander)\add* Epifanes \add !(Epiphanes)\add*, the¦72626 son of¦72627 Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add*, went up and¦72631 took possession of Ptolemais. They received him, and¦72634 he¦72636 reigned¦72638 there¦72639.
\v 2 King¦72644 Demetrios heard¦72641 about this¦72643, and¦72645 he gathered together very¦72649 great forces, and¦72650 went¦72651 out¦72651 to meet him in battle¦72656.
\p
\v 3 Demetrios sent¦72658 a letter to¦72658 Yonatan with¦72660 words¦72663 of peace, so¦72665 as to honour him.
\v 4 Because he said¦72668, “Let's go beforehand to¦72668 make peace¦72672 with¦72674 them, before he makes peace with¦72679 Alexandros against us;
\v 5 for¦72684 he'll remember all¦72685 the¦72686 evils¦72687 that¦72688 we've done against him, and to his kindred and to his nation¦72700.”
\v 6 So¦72702 he¦72704 gave¦72703 him authority¦72705 to¦72706 gather¦72706 together forces, and¦72708 to provide weapons¦72710, and¦72711 that he should be¦72712 his ally. He also¦72716 commanded that they should release the hostages that were in¦72720 the¦72721 citadel to him.
\p
\v 7 Yonatan came¦72727 to¦72727 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, and¦72731 read the¦72733 letter in the¦72736 hearing of all¦72738 the¦72739 people¦72740, and¦72741 of those who¦72742 were in the¦72744 citadel.
\v 8 They were very afraid¦72748 when¦72750 they heard¦72751 that¦72752 the¦72755 king¦72756 had given¦72753 him authority¦72757 to¦72758 gather¦72758 together an army.
\v 9 Those in the citadel released the hostages to Yonatan, and he restored them to their parents¦72773.
\p
\v 10 Yonatan lived in¦72778 Yerushalem and¦72780 began to¦72782 build¦72782 and¦72783 renew the¦72785 city¦72786.
\v 11 He commanded those who did¦72791 the¦72792 work¦72793 to¦72794 build¦72794 the¦72795 walls¦72796 and¦72797 encircle Mt¦72799. Tsiyon \add !(Zion)\add* with\f + \fr 10:11 \ft So the versions and Josephus. Grk. \fqa four-foot stones.\f* square stones¦72803 for defence; and¦72807 they did¦72808 so.
\v 12 The¦72812 foreigners who¦72814 were¦72815 in¦72816 the¦72817 strongholds which¦72819 Bakides had built¦72820 fled¦72811 away.
\v 13 Each¦72824 man left¦72823 his place¦72826 and¦72828 departed into¦72829 his own land¦72832.
\v 14 Only at Beyt-Tsur, there were left some of those who'd¦72839 forsaken the¦72841 law¦72842 and¦72843 the¦72844 commandments, for¦72847 it¦72848 was a¦72849 place¦72849 of¦72849 refuge¦72849 to them.
\s1 Alexandros appoints Yonatan as high priest
\p
\v 15 King¦72854 Alexandros¦72852 \add !(Alexander)\add* heard¦72851 all the promises¦72856 which Demetrios had sent¦72858 to¦72863 Yonatan. They told him of the¦72865 battles and¦72867 the¦72868 valiant actions which¦72870 he¦72872 and¦72873 his kindred had done¦72871, and¦72877 of the¦72878 troubles which¦72880 they'd¦72881 endured.
\v 16 So¦72882 he said¦72883, “Could we find¦72885 another man¦72886 like¦72887 him? Now¦72890 we'll make¦72891 him our\f + \fr 10:16 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18. Compare 1 Maccabees 10:65.\f* friend¦72893 and¦72894 ally.”
\v 17 He wrote¦72898 a letter and¦72900 sent¦72901 it¦72902 to¦72903 him, in these words¦72905, saying,
\v 18 “King¦72908 Alexandros¦72909 to his brother¦72911 Yonatan, greetings.
\v 19 We've¦72926 heard¦72914 of you¦72916, that¦72917 you're a mighty man¦72918 of valour, and¦72921 worthy to be our\f + \fr 10:19 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18. Compare 1 Maccabees 10:65.\f* friend¦72927.
\v 20 Now¦72929 we've appointed you¦72931 this day to be high priest of¦72934 your nation¦72935, and¦72937 to¦72940 be called¦72940 the king's¦72939\f + \fr 10:20 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18. Compare 1 Maccabees 10:65.\f* friend¦72938, and to take our side, and¦72941 to¦72942 keep friendship with us.” He¦72943 also sent¦72942 to him a purple¦72944 robe¦72944 and¦72945 a golden¦72947 crown¦72946.
\p
\v 21 And¦72957 Yonatan put¦72958 on¦72958 the¦72960 holy¦72961 clothes in the¦72963 seventh month¦72965 of the one hundred sixtieth year,\f + \fr 10:21 \ft circa B.C. 153.\f* at the feast of tabernacles; and he gathered together forces and provided weapons¦72978 in abundance.
\s1 Demetrios offers more concessions
\p
\v 22 When¦72980 Demetrios heard¦72981 these things, he¦72985 was grieved¦72987 and¦72988 said¦72989,
\v 23 “What's this¦72991 that¦72993 we've¦72995 done¦72992, that¦72996 Alexandros¦72997 has gotten ahead of¦72998 us in establishing friendship with the¦72998 Yehudim to¦73000 strengthen himself?
\v 24 I also will write¦73005 to them words¦73008 of encouragement¦73009 and¦73010 of honour and¦73012 of gifts, that¦73014 they may be¦73015 with¦73016 me to aid me.”
\v 25 So¦73020 he¦73022 sent¦73021 to¦73023 them this¦73024 message¦73025:
\p “King¦73027 Demetrios to the¦73029 nation¦73030 of the¦73031 Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add*, greetings.
\v 26 Since¦73034 as you've kept your covenants with¦73037 us, and¦73040 continued in our friendship¦73043, and¦73045 haven't joined yourselves to¦73051 our enemies, we've heard¦73051 of this, and¦73052 are glad¦73053.
\v 27 Now¦73055 continue still¦73057 to¦73060 keep faith¦73062 with us, and¦73063 we'll repay you¦73065 with good in return for¦73067 your dealings with¦73070 us.
\v 28 We'll grant you¦73074 many immunities and¦73077 give¦73078 you¦73079 gifts¦73080.
\p
\v 29 “Now¦73082 I free¦73083 you¦73084 and¦73085 release¦73086 all¦73087 the¦73088 Yehudim from¦73090 the tributes, from the salt tax, and¦73098 from¦73099 the¦73100 crown levies.
\v 30 Instead of¦73104 the¦73104 third¦73105 part of the¦73106 seed¦73107, and¦73108 instead of¦73110 half¦73111 of¦73112 the¦73112 fruit¦73113 of¦73114 the trees, which falls to¦73119 me to¦73120 receive, I release¦73120 it from¦73121 this¦73122 day and¦73124 from now on, so that I won't take¦73127 it from¦73128 the¦73129 land¦73130 of Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add*, and¦73132 from¦73133 the¦73134 three¦73135 districts which are added to it¦73139 from¦73140 the¦73141 country of Shomron \add !(Samaria)\add* and Galil, from¦73146 this¦73147 day¦73149 forth and¦73150 for all time¦73154.
\v 31 Let Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* be¦73157 holy¦73158 and free, with her borders, tithes, and taxes¦73169.
\v 32 I yield up also¦73171 my authority¦73173 over the citadel which¦73189 is at Yerushalem, and¦73179 give¦73180 it to the¦73181 high priest, that¦73183 he may appoint in¦73186 it¦73187 men¦73188 whom he¦73192 chooses to¦73194 keep¦73194 it¦73195.
\v 33 Every¦73197 soul¦73220 of the Yehudim who's been carried captive from¦73202 the land¦73203 of Yehudah into any part of my kingdom¦73207, I¦73208 set at liberty without payment. Let all¦73213 officials also cancel the¦73215 taxes¦73216 on their livestock.
\p
\v 34 “All¦73222 the¦73223 feasts, the¦73226 Sabbaths¦73227, new moons, appointed days¦73231, three¦73234 days¦73235 before¦73236 a feast, and¦73238 three¦73239 days¦73240 after¦73241 a feast, let them all be days¦73246 of immunity and¦73248 release for all¦73250 the¦73251 Yehudim who are¦73254 in¦73255 my kingdom¦73257.
\v 35 No¦73260 one has¦73261 authority¦73262 to¦73264 exact anything from any of them, or to¦73266 trouble¦73266 them about¦73269 any matter.
\p
\v 36 “Let there be enrolled among the¦73279 king's¦73280 forces about thirty¦73282 thousand men¦73284 of the Yehudim, and¦73285 pay will be given¦73286 to them, as is due to all¦73291 the king's¦73295 forces.
\v 37 Of them, some will be placed in the king's great strongholds, and some of them will be placed over the affairs of the¦73313 kingdom¦73314, which are positions of trust. Let those who are over them and their rulers¦73325 be¦73326 of themselves, and¦73329 let them walk after their own laws, even as¦73334 the¦73337 king¦73338 has commanded in¦73339 the land¦73340 of Yehudah.
\p
\v 38 “The¦73343 three¦73344 districts that have been added to Yehudah from¦73350 the¦73351 country¦73352 of Shomron \add !(Samaria)\add*, let them be annexed to¦73357 Yehudah, that they may be reckoned to be¦73361 under¦73362 one¦73363 ruler, that they may not¦73365 obey¦73366 any other authority¦73368 than¦73370 the¦73371 high priest's.
\v 39 As for Ptolemais and¦73374 its land, I've given¦73378 it¦73377 as a gift¦73379 to the¦73380 sanctuary¦73381 that's¦73382 at Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, for the¦73386 expenses of the¦73389 sanctuary¦73390.
\v 40 I¦73391 also give¦73392 every year¦73394 fifteen¦73395 thousand shekels of¦73402 silver from the¦73402 king's¦73403 revenues from¦73404 the¦73405 places¦73406 that¦73407 are appropriate.
\v 41 And¦73409 all¦73410 the¦73411 additional funds which¦73413 those who¦73416 manage the¦73418 king's affairs didn't pay as in¦73421 the¦73422 first¦73423 years¦73424, they'll give¦73428 from¦73425 now¦73427 on towards¦73429 the¦73430 works¦73431 of¦73432 the¦73432 temple¦73433.
\v 42 Besides this¦73436, the five¦73437 thousand¦73437 shekels of silver which¦73440 they received from¦73442 the¦73443 uses of¦73445 the¦73445 sanctuary¦73446 from¦73447 the¦73448 revenue year by year is also¦73452 released¦73454, because¦73455 it¦73458 belongs to the¦73459 priests¦73460 who¦73461 minister there.
\v 43 Anyone who flees to the¦73468 temple¦73469 that's¦73470 at Yerushalem, and¦73473 within all¦73475 of its borders, whether one owe¦73479 money to the king, or any other matter, let them go free, along with all that they have in my kingdom¦73492.
\v 44 Because the building and renewing of the structures of the sanctuary¦73503, the expense will also¦73504 be given¦73507 out¦73508 of the¦73511 king's¦73512 revenue.
\v 45 Because the building of the walls¦73517 of Yerushalem and¦73519 fortifying it all around¦73521, the¦73523 expense will also be given¦73525 out¦73526 of the king's¦73530 revenue, also for the building of the walls¦73535 in¦73537 Yehudah.”
\p
\v 46 Now when¦73541 Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* and¦73544 the¦73545 people heard¦73542 these words¦73548, they gave no¦73550 credence to¦73551 them, and¦73553 didn't¦73553 accept them, because they remembered the¦73559 great¦73560 evil¦73558 which¦73561 he'd done¦73562 in¦73563 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*, and¦73565 that¦73555 he'd¦73567 afflicted them very¦73568 severely.
\v 47 They were well pleased¦73570 with Alexandros, because¦73573 he¦73574 was¦73575 the first who spoke words¦73578 of peace to them, and¦73580 they were allies with him always.
\s1 Alexandros becomes king and honours Yonatan
\p
\v 48 King¦73590 Alexandros¦73588 \add !(Alexander)\add* gathered together great¦73592 forces and¦73593 encamped near Demetrios.
\v 49 The¦73600 two¦73601 kings¦73602 joined battle¦73599, and¦73603 Alexandros'¦73612 army fled¦73604; and¦73608 Demetrios followed after him, and¦73613 prevailed against¦73615 them.
\v 50 He strengthened¦73618 the¦73619 battle¦73620 greatly until¦73622 the¦73624 sun¦73625 went down; and¦73626 Demetrios fell that¦73633 day¦73632.
\p
\v 51 Alexandros¦73636 sent¦73635 ambassadors to¦73637 Mitsrayim's \add !(Egypt)\add* King¦73639 Ptolemaios \add !(Ptolemy)\add* with this¦73643 message¦73644:
\v 52 “Since¦73647 I've returned to my kingdom¦73651, and¦73653 am seated¦73654 on¦73655 the throne¦73656 of my fathers¦73657, and¦73659 have established my dominion, and¦73663 have overthrown Demetrios, and¦73667 have taken possession of our country¦73670—
\v 53 yes, I joined the battle with¦73674 him, and¦73677 he¦73679 and¦73680 his army were defeated by¦73684 us, and we sat on¦73688 the throne¦73689 of his kingdom¦73690—
\v 54 now¦73693 also let's make friends with¦73695 one another. Give me now your daughter¦73703 as my wife¦73706. I'll be joined with you¦73709, and¦73710 will give¦73711 both you¦73712 and¦73714 her gifts¦73713 worthy¦73716 of you¦73717.”
\p
\v 55 King¦73722 Ptolemaios¦73720 answered¦73719, saying, “Happy is the¦73721 day¦73725 you¦73732 returned to the land¦73730 of your ancestors and¦73733 sat on the throne¦73736 of their kingdom¦73737.
\v 56 Now¦73740 I'll do¦73741 to you¦73742 as you've written, but¦73745 meet me at Ptolemais, that¦73749 we may see one¦73751 another¦73751; and¦73752 I'll join with you¦73754, even as¦73755 you've said¦73756.”
\v 57 So¦73757 Ptolemaios¦73759 went¦73758 out¦73760 of Mitsrayim, himself and¦73763 Kleopatra¦73764 \add !(Cleopatra)\add* his daughter¦73766, and¦73768 came to¦73769 Ptolemais in the one hundred and sixty-second year.\f + \fr 10:57 \ft circa B.C. 151.\f*
\v 58 King Alexandros¦73781 met him, and¦73784 he¦73786 gave him his daughter¦73789 Kleopatra, and¦73791 celebrated her wedding¦73794 at Ptolemais with great¦73803 pomp, as¦73798 kings¦73800 do.
\p
\v 59 King¦73808 Alexandros¦73806 wrote¦73805 to¦73811 Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add*, that he should come¦73811 to meet him.
\v 60 He went with¦73817 pomp to Ptolemais, and¦73821 met the¦73823 two¦73824 kings¦73825. He gave¦73827 them and their friends¦73834\f + \fr 10:60 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18. Compare 1 Maccabees 10:65.\f* silver and gold¦73831, and many gifts¦73837, and¦73839 found¦73840 favour in¦73842 their sight.
\v 61 Some malcontents out¦73850 of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*, men¦73852 who were transgressors of the law, gathered together against him to¦73855 complain against him, but¦73857 the¦73861 king¦73862 didn't pay any attention to them.
\v 62 The¦73865 king¦73866 commanded that they take off Yonatan's clothes and¦73867 clothe¦73871 him in purple¦73876, and¦73877 they did¦73878 so.
\v 63 The¦73883 king¦73884 made him sit with¦73885 him, and¦73887 said¦73888 to¦73892 his princes, “Go¦73892 out¦73892 with¦73893 him into the middle¦73896 of the¦73897 city¦73898, and¦73899 proclaim that no man may complain against him of¦73901 any matter, and¦73909 let no man trouble him for any reason.”
\v 64 When¦73916 those who complained against him saw his honour¦73923 according to¦73926 the proclamation, and¦73927 saw him clothed¦73928 in purple¦73930, they all¦73933 fled¦73932 away.
\v 65 The¦73937 king¦73938 gave him honour¦73935, and¦73939 enrolled him among his chief friends¦73944,\f + \fr 10:65 \ft See 1 Maccabees 11:27; 2 Maccabees 8:9. Compare 1 Maccabees 2:18; 10:16, etc.\f* and¦73945 made him a captain and¦73949 governor of a province.
\v 66 Then¦73951 Yonatan returned to¦73952 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* with¦73956 peace¦73957 and¦73958 gladness¦73959.
\s1 Yonatan defeats Apolonios
\p
\v 67 In¦73961 the one hundred and sixty-fifth year¦73962,\f + \fr 10:67 \ft circa B.C. 148.\f* Demetrios, son¦73970 of Demetrios, came¦73968 out¦73972 of Kraitai \add !(Crete)\add* into the¦73975 land¦73976 of his ancestors.
\v 68 When¦73980 King¦73984 Alexandros¦73982 \add !(Alexander)\add* heard¦73981 of it, he grieved¦73986 greatly and¦73985 returned to¦73986 Antiokeia.
\v 69 Demetrios appointed Apolonios, who was over Coele-Syria, and he gathered together a great army, and encamped against Yavneh, and sent to Yonatan the high priest, saying,
\p
\v 70 “You alone lift up yourself against us, but I'm ridiculed and in reproach because of you. Why do you assume authority against us in the mountains?
\v 71 Now¦74039 therefore¦74040, if¦74041 you¦74046 trust in your forces, come¦74047 down¦74047 to¦74048 us into the¦74051 plain¦74052, and¦74053 let's match strength with each other there¦74056; for the power¦74061 of the¦74062 cities¦74063 is with me.
\v 72 Ask¦74064 and¦74065 learn who I am¦74068, and¦74069 the¦74070 rest who¦74072 help us. They say¦74076, ‘Your foot¦74081 can't stand before our face¦74083; for your ancestors have been put to flight twice¦74086 in¦74091 their own land¦74093.’
\v 73 Now¦74096 you won't be¦74098 able¦74098 to withstand the¦74100 cavalry and¦74102 such¦74104 an army as¦74104 this¦74104 in¦74105 the¦74106 plain, where is¦74110 there's no stone¦74111 or pebble¦74113, or place¦74115 to¦74117 flee¦74117.”
\p
\v 74 Now when¦74119 Yonatan heard¦74120 Apolonios' words¦74123, he was moved¦74125 in his mind¦74127, and¦74128 he chose ten¦74130 thousand men¦74132, and¦74133 went¦74134 out from¦74135 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*; and¦74137 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* his brother¦74142 met¦74138 him to¦74144 help¦74145 him.
\v 75 Then¦74147 he encamped against¦74149 Yafo \add !(Joppa)\add*. The people of the¦74155 city¦74156 shut him out¦74154, because¦74157 Apolonios had a¦74158 garrison in¦74160 Yafo.
\v 76 So¦74165 they fought against it. The¦74168 people of the¦74170 city¦74171 were afraid¦74166, and opened to him; and Yonatan became master of Yafo.
\p
\v 77 Apolonios heard¦74177 about that, and¦74179 he gathered an army of three thousand cavalry, and¦74183 a great army, and¦74186 went¦74194 to¦74187 Azotos as though he were on a journey, and¦74192 at the same time advanced onward into¦74194 the¦74196 plain¦74197, because¦74198 he¦74201 had a multitude¦74202 of cavalry which¦74190 he¦74207 trusted.
\v 78 He¦74212 pursued him to¦74209 Azotos, and¦74215 the¦74217 armies joined battle¦74220.\f + \fr 10:78 \ft Most of the authorities here repeat \fqa after him.\f*
\v 79 Apolonios had secretly left a thousand cavalry behind them.
\v 80 Yonatan learnt that¦74233 there¦74237 was an ambush behind him. They surrounded¦74239 his army, and¦74243 shot their arrows at the people¦74249, from¦74251 morning¦74251 until¦74252 evening¦74253;
\v 81 but the people¦74256 stood¦74257 fast, as¦74258 Yonatan commanded¦74259 them; and¦74261 the¦74263 enemy's horses grew tired.
\p
\v 82 Then¦74266 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* brought forward his army and¦74272 joined battle with¦74274 the phalanx (for¦74278 the cavalry were exhausted), and¦74281 they were defeated by¦74283 him and¦74285 fled¦74286.
\v 83 The¦74288 cavalry were scattered in¦74291 the¦74292 plain. They fled¦74295 to¦74295 Azotos and¦74298 entered¦74299 into Beyt-Dagon, their idol's¦74303 temple¦74303, to¦74306 save¦74306 themselves.
\v 84 Yonatan burnt Azotos and the cities¦74314 around it¦74317 and¦74318 took¦74319 their spoils. He¦74322 burnt the¦74324 temple¦74325 of Dagon¦74326 and¦74327 those who¦74328 fled into it¦74331 with fire¦74333.
\v 85 Those who'd fallen by the¦74336 sword¦74338 plus¦74334 those who¦74340 were burnt were about eight thousand men¦74343.
\p
\v 86 From¦74347 there¦74347, Yonatan left and¦74349 encamped against¦74351 Ashkelon. The¦74355 people of the¦74357 city¦74358 came out to¦74363 meet him with great¦74364 pomp.
\v 87 Yonatan, with¦74370 those who¦74371 were on his side, returned to¦74374 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, having¦74374 many spoils.
\v 88 When¦74377 King¦74383 Alexandros¦74381 heard¦74380 these things, he¦74386 honoured Yonatan even more.
\v 89 He¦74394 sent¦74393 him a gold¦74396 buckle, as the custom¦74398 is¦74399 to¦74406 give¦74406 to the¦74403 king's¦74404 kindred¦74402. He¦74407 gave him Ekron and¦74410 all¦74411 its land for a possession.
\c 11
\s1 Ptolemaios turns against Alexandros
\p
\v 1 Then¦74417 the¦74418 king¦74419 of Mitsrayim \add !(Egypt)\add* gathered together great forces, as the¦74425 sand¦74426 which¦74424 is by the¦74431 sea¦74432 shore, and¦74433 many ships, and¦74436 sought¦74437 to¦74437 make himself master of Alexandros's \add !(Alexander)\add* kingdom¦74440 by deceit¦74442, and¦74443 to¦74444 add¦74444 it¦74445 to his own kingdom¦74447.
\v 2 He went¦74450 out¦74450 into Aram \add !(Syria)\add* with words¦74453 of peace, and¦74455 the¦74458 people of the¦74460 cities¦74461 opened their gates to him and met him; for King¦74470 Alexandros's command was that¦74465 they should meet him, because¦74473 he¦74476 was¦74477 his father-in-law.
\v 3 Now as he entered¦74480 into the¦74482 cities¦74483 of Ptolemais, he set his forces for a garrison in¦74489 each¦74490 city¦74491.
\p
\v 4 But¦74493 when he came¦74494 near¦74494 to Azotos, they showed him Dagon's¦74500 temple¦74499 burnt with fire, and¦74502 Azotos and¦74504 its pasture lands destroyed, and¦74509 the¦74510 bodies¦74511 thrown out, and¦74513 those who'd¦74514 been burnt, whom he burnt in¦74518 the¦74519 war¦74520, for¦74522 they'd made¦74521 heaps of them in¦74525 his way¦74492.
\v 5 They told the¦74531 king¦74532 what Yonatan had done¦74534, that¦74537 they might throw blame on him; but¦74540 the¦74542 king¦74543 kept silent¦74541.
\v 6 Yonatan met¦74545 the¦74547 king¦74548 with¦74551 pomp at Yafo \add !(Joppa)\add*, and¦74553 they greeted one¦74555 another¦74555, and¦74556 they slept¦74557 there¦74558.
\v 7 Yonatan went with¦74562 the¦74563 king¦74564 as far as the¦74566 river¦74567 that's called¦74569 Eleutherus, then¦74571 returned to¦74572 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*.
\p
\v 8 But¦74576 King¦74577 Ptolemaios¦74578 \add !(Ptolemy)\add* took control of the¦74580 cities¦74581 along the¦74582 sea coast, to¦74589 Seleukeia which is by the¦74586 sea, and¦74588 he devised evil¦74593 plans about¦74590 Alexandros.
\v 9 He sent¦74595 ambassadors to¦74597 King¦74600 Demetrios, saying, “Come¦74602! Let's make a covenant¦74606 with one another, and¦74607 I'll give¦74608 you¦74609 my daughter¦74611 whom Alexandros¦74615 has, and¦74616 you'll reign over your father's¦74621 kingdom¦74619;
\v 10 for¦74624 I regret that¦74627 I gave¦74625 my daughter¦74628 to¦74630 him, for¦74631 he tried¦74630 to¦74632 kill¦74632 me.
\v 11 He¦74636 accused him, because¦74637 he¦74640 coveted his kingdom¦74642.
\v 12 Taking his daughter¦74648 from him, he gave¦74649 her to Demetrios, and¦74653 was estranged from Alexandros, and¦74657 their enmity was openly seen.
\p
\v 13 Ptolemaios¦74664 entered¦74663 into Antiokeia, and¦74667 put on himself Asia's crown. He put two¦74669 crowns on his head¦74673, the crown of Mitsrayim \add !(Egypt)\add* and¦74678 that of Asia.
\v 14 But¦74681 King¦74683 Alexandros¦74680 was¦74684 in¦74685 Kilikia¦74686 at that¦74688 time¦74689, because¦74691 the people of that¦74697 region were in revolt.
\v 15 When¦74698 Alexandros¦74700 heard¦74699 of it, he came¦74702 against¦74703 him in war¦74705. Ptolemaios¦74708 marched out¦74707 and¦74711 met him with a strong¦74716 force, and¦74717 put him to flight.
\v 16 Alexandros¦74722 fled¦74721 into Arav, that¦74724 he¦74728 might be sheltered there¦74729; but¦74731 King¦74732 Ptolemaios¦74733 was triumphant.
\v 17 Zavdiyel the Aravi took off Alexandros's head¦74741, and¦74743 sent¦74744 it to¦74744 Ptolemaios.
\v 18 King¦74749 Ptolemaios¦74750 died¦74751 the¦74755 third¦74756 day¦74754 after, and¦74757 those who¦74758 were¦74759 in¦74760 his strongholds were slain by¦74764 the¦74765 inhabitants of the¦74767 strongholds.
\v 19 Demetrios became king in the one hundred and sixty-seventh year.\f + \fr 11:19 \ft circa B.C. 146.\f*
\s1 Yonatan negotiates with Demetrios
\p
\v 20 In¦74778 those days¦74780 Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* gathered together the¦74779 Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add* to¦74782 take the¦74784 citadel that¦74781 was at Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*. He made¦74796 many engines of¦74788 war to¦74796 use against¦74797 it¦74798.
\v 21 Some lawless men¦74808 who hated¦74804 their own nation¦74806 went to¦74810 the¦74811 king¦74812 and¦74813 reported to¦74814 him that¦74816 Yonatan was besieging the¦74819 citadel.
\v 22 He heard, and¦74821 was angry¦74823, but¦74825 when he heard¦74826 it, he set out immediately¦74827, and came¦74829 to¦74829 Ptolemais, and¦74832 wrote¦74833 to¦74833 Yonatan, that¦74838 he¦74843 shouldn't¦74836 besiege it¦74844, and that¦74848 he should meet him and speak with him at Ptolemais with all speed.
\p
\v 23 But¦74851 when Yonatan heard¦74852 this¦74858, he gave¦74865 orders¦74854 to¦74854 continue the siege. He chose some of the elders¦74859 of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* and¦74861 of the¦74862 priests¦74863, and¦74864 put himself¦74866 in peril
\v 24 by taking¦74870 silver, gold¦74873, clothing¦74875, and¦74876 various other¦74877 presents, and went to¦74880 Ptolemais to¦74881 the¦74882 king¦74883. Then¦74886 he¦74890 found¦74887 favour in his sight.
\v 25 Some lawless men of those who were of¦74899 the¦74899 nation¦74900 made complaints against him,
\v 26 and¦74901 the¦74904 king¦74905 did to him even as¦74906 his predecessors had done to¦74907 him, and¦74912 exalted him in¦74915 the sight of¦74915 all¦74916 his\f + \fr 11:26 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* friends¦74918,
\v 27 and¦74920 confirmed to¦74921 him the¦74923 high priesthood, and¦74925 all the other honours that he had¦74928 before, and¦74931 gave him preeminence among his\f + \fr 11:27 \ft See 1 Maccabees 10:65.\f* chief friends¦74936.
\v 28 And¦74938 Yonatan requested of the¦74941 king¦74942 that he'd make¦74943 Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add* free from tribute, along with the¦74948 three¦74949\f + \fr 11:28 \ft Grk. \fqa toparchies\f* provinces and¦74951 the¦74952 country of Shomron \add !(Samaria)\add*, and¦74954 promised him three hundred talents¦74957.
\v 29 The¦74961 king¦74962 consented, and¦74963 wrote¦74964 letters to¦74964 Yonatan about¦74968 all¦74969 these things as follows:
\p
\v 30 “King¦74975 Demetrios to his brother¦74979 Yonatan, and¦74981 to the nation¦74982 of the Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add*, greetings.
\v 31 The¦74984 copy of the¦74986 letter which¦74988 we¦74993 wrote to Lasthenes our kinsman about¦74994 you¦74995, we've written also¦74997 to¦74998 you¦74999, that¦75000 you may see it.
\v 32 ‘King¦75002 Demetrios to Lasthenes his father¦75006, greetings.
\v 33 We've determined to do good to the¦75008 nation¦75009 of the Yehudim, who are our friends¦75012, and¦75014 observe what's just¦75019 towards us, because¦75022 of¦75022 their good will towards us.
\v 34 We've confirmed therefore¦75030 to them the borders of Yehudah, and also the¦75038 three¦75039 governments of Aphaerema, Lod, and Ramatayim (these were added¦75047 to¦75047 Yehudah from¦75050 the¦75051 country of Shomron), and¦75053 all¦75054 their territory¦75034 to them, for all¦75058 who¦75059 do sacrifice in Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, instead of the¦75064 king's dues which¦75066 the¦75068 king¦75069 received of them yearly before from the¦75076 produce of the¦75078 earth¦75079 and¦75080 the¦75082 fruits of trees.
\v 35 As for the other payments to us from¦75090 now¦75092 on, of¦75091 the tithes and¦75095 the¦75096 taxes that¦75098 pertain to us, and¦75101 the salt pits, and¦75106 the¦75107 crown¦75110 taxes due to us, all¦75111 these we'll give back to them.
\v 36 Not¦75118 one¦75119 of¦75122 these grants will be annulled from¦75121 this¦75126 time¦75128 forth and forever.
\v 37 Now¦75129 therefore¦75130 be careful to¦75133 make¦75133 a¦75135 copy of these things, and¦75136 let it be given to Yonatan, and¦75139 let it be set up on¦75141 the¦75144 holy¦75145 mountain¦75143 in¦75146 a suitable and conspicuous place¦75147.’ ”
\s1 Yonatan's troops rescue Demetrios
\p
\v 38 When¦75149 King¦75153 Demetrios saw that¦75154 the¦75156 land¦75157 was quiet before¦75158 him, and that no resistance was made to¦75165 him, he¦75169 sent away¦75181 all his troops, each¦75170 man¦75173 to his own¦75173 place¦75174, except the¦75176 foreign¦75177 troops, which¦75179 he'd raised from the¦75182 islands of the¦75184 Gentiles. So¦75186 all¦75189 the¦75190 troops of his fathers¦75193 hated him.
\v 39 Now Trufon¦75195 was¦75197 one of those who¦75198 previously had been on Alexandros's \add !(Alexander)\add* side, and¦75202 he saw that¦75204 all¦75205 the¦75206 forces murmured against Demetrios. So¦75211 he went to Imalcue the Aravi, who was raising up Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* the young child of¦75224 Alexandros,
\v 40 and¦75226 urgently insisted to him that he should deliver¦75230 him to him, that he might reign¦75234 in his father's¦75237 place. He told him all that Demetrios had done, and the¦75246 hatred with which his forces hated him; and he stayed¦75255 there¦75256 many days¦75257.
\p
\v 41 Now Yonatan sent¦75260 to¦75262 King¦75265 Demetrios, that¦75266 he should remove the¦75268 troops of the¦75270 citadel from¦75272 Yerushalem, and¦75274 the troops who were¦75279 in¦75276 the¦75277 strongholds; for¦75280 they fought against Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* continually.
\v 42 Demetrios sent¦75285 to Yonatan, saying, “I won't only¦75291 do¦75293 this for you¦75294 and¦75295 your nation¦75297, but¦75299 I'll greatly honour you¦75302 and¦75303 your nation¦75305, if¦75307 I find an opportunity.
\v 43 Now¦75310 therefore¦75311 you'll do¦75313 well if you send¦75314 me men¦75316 who'll¦75317 fight for me; for all¦75321 my forces have revolted.”
\v 44 So¦75325 Yonatan sent¦75326 him three thousand valiant men¦75328 to Antiokeia. They came to the¦75338 king¦75339, and¦75340 the¦75342 king¦75343 was glad at their coming.
\p
\v 45 The¦75350 people of the¦75352 city¦75353 gathered themselves together into the middle¦75355 of the¦75356 city¦75357, to the number of one hundred and twenty thousand men¦75359, and¦75362 they wanted to¦75364 kill the¦75365 king¦75366.
\v 46 The¦75369 king¦75370 fled¦75368 into the¦75372 palace courtyard, and¦75374 the¦75376 people of the¦75378 city¦75379 seized the¦75380 main streets of the¦75382 city¦75383 and¦75384 began to fight.
\v 47 The¦75389 king¦75390 called¦75388 the¦75391 Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add* to¦75393 help¦75394 him, and¦75395 they were gathered together to¦75397 him all¦75399 at once, and¦75401 they dispersed themselves in¦75403 the¦75404 city¦75405, and¦75408 killed¦75409 that¦75415 day¦75414 about one hundred thousand.
\v 48 They set the¦75421 city¦75422 on¦75427 fire, and seized many spoils that¦75428 day¦75430, and¦75431 saved the¦75433 king¦75434.
\v 49 The¦75437 people of the¦75439 city¦75440 saw that¦75441 the¦75443 Yehudim had taken control of the¦75445 city¦75446 as they pleased, and¦75449 they became faint in their hearts, and¦75454 they cried out to¦75456 the¦75457 king¦75458 with¦75459 supplication, saying,
\v 50 “Give¦75462 us your right¦75464 hand, and¦75465 let the¦75467 Yehudim cease from fighting against us and¦75471 the¦75472 city¦75473.”
\v 51 They threw¦75475 away their weapons¦75477 and¦75478 made¦75479 peace¦75480. The¦75483 Yehudim were glorified in¦75485 the sight of the¦75486 king¦75487, and¦75488 before¦75489 all¦75490 who were in¦75492 his kingdom¦75494. Then¦75496 they returned to Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, having¦75500 much¦75502 plunder¦75501.
\v 52 So¦75503 King¦75507 Demetrios sat on¦75508 the throne¦75509 of his kingdom¦75511, and¦75513 the¦75515 land¦75516 was quiet before¦75517 him.
\v 53 He lied in all¦75521 that he spoke, and¦75524 estranged himself from Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add*, and¦75528 didn't repay him according¦75531 to¦75531 the¦75532 benefits with which¦75534 he¦75536 had repaid him, and¦75537 treated him very¦75540 harshly.
\s1 Yonatan supports the young Antiokos
\p
\v 54 Now after¦75541 this¦75543, Trufon¦75545 returned, and¦75546 with¦75548 him the young child Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add*, who reigned¦75553 and¦75554 put on a crown.
\v 55 All¦75561 the¦75562 forces which¦75564 Demetrios had sent away with disgrace were gathered to him, and they fought against him, and he fled¦75572 and¦75573 was routed.
\v 56 Trufon¦75577 took the¦75578 elephants, and¦75580 took control of Antiokeia.
\v 57 The young Antiokos wrote¦75584 to¦75590 Yonatan, saying, “I confirm to¦75591 you¦75592 the¦75593 high priesthood, and¦75595 appoint¦75596 you¦75597 over the¦75599 four¦75600 districts, and¦75602 to¦75603 be¦75603 one of¦75607 the¦75607 king's¦75608\f + \fr 11:57 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* friends¦75606.”
\v 58 He sent¦75610 to him golden vessels and¦75613 furniture for the table, and¦75615 gave¦75616 him permission to¦75619 drink¦75619 in¦75620 golden vessels, and¦75622 to¦75623 be¦75623 clothed in¦75624 purple¦75625, and¦75626 to¦75627 have¦75627 a golden¦75629 buckle.
\v 59 He made his brother¦75633 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* governor from¦75637 the¦75638 Ladder of Tsor \add !(Tyre)\add* to¦75635 the¦75642 borders of Mitsrayim \add !(Egypt)\add*.
\p
\v 60 Yonatan went¦75646 out¦75646 and¦75648 took his journey beyond the¦75651 river¦75652 and¦75653 through¦75649 the¦75655 cities¦75656. All¦75661 the¦75662 forces of Aram \add !(Syria)\add* gathered themselves to¦75668 him to be his allies. He¦75673 came to Ashkelon, and the¦75674 people of the¦75676 city¦75677 met¦75672 him honourably.
\v 61 He departed from¦75681 there¦75681 to Azah \add !(Gaza)\add*, and¦75684 Azah's people shut him out. So¦75689 he besieged it and burnt its pasture lands with fire¦75698, and¦75699 plundered them.
\v 62 Azah's people pleaded with Yonatan, and¦75709 he¦75711 gave¦75710 them his right¦75712 hand, and¦75713 took¦75714 the¦75715 sons¦75716 of their princes for hostages, and¦75721 sent¦75722 them away¦75722 to Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*. Then he passed¦75727 through¦75727 the¦75728 country¦75729 as far as Damesek \add !(Damascus)\add*.
\s1 Yonatan defeats Demetrios' army
\p
\v 63 Then¦75732 Yonatan heard¦75733 that¦75735 Demetrios’ princes had come to Kedesh, which is in¦75743 Galil, with¦75746 a great army, intending to¦75749 remove him from his office.
\v 64 He went to¦75755 meet¦75755 them, but¦75758 he¦75760 left¦75762 Shim'on his brother¦75759 in¦75763 the¦75764 country¦75765.
\v 65 Shim'on encamped against Beyt-Tsur, and fought against it¦75773 many days¦75774, and¦75776 hemmed it¦75778 in.
\v 66 They asked him to¦75786 give¦75786 them his right¦75783 hand, and¦75785 he gave it¦75787 to¦75789 them. He¦75790 removed them from¦75791 there¦75791, took¦75784 possession of the¦75794 city¦75795, and¦75796 set a garrison over it¦75799.
\p
\v 67 Yonatan and his army encamped at the¦75809 water¦75810 of Gennaisaret, and¦75812 early in the morning they marched to the plain¦75817 of Hatsor.
\v 68 Listen, an army of foreigners met him in¦75825 the¦75826 plain. They laid an ambush for him in¦75833 the¦75834 mountains¦75835, but¦75837 they themselves met him face to¦75838 face.
\v 69 But those who lay in ambush rose out of their places and joined battle. All those who were on Yonatan's side fled.
\v 70 Not one of them was left, except Matityah \add !(Mattathias)\add* the son of Avshalom \add !(Absalom)\add*, and Yehudah \add !(Judas)\add* the son of Chalphi, captains of the forces.
\v 71 Yonatan tore¦75878 his clothes¦75881, put¦75884 dirt on¦75884 his head¦75888, and¦75890 prayed¦75891.
\v 72 He turned again to them in battle¦75896, and¦75897 routed them, and¦75900 they fled¦75901.
\v 73 When¦75902 the¦75904 men on his side who'd fled saw this¦75906, they returned to him and¦75913 pursued¦75914 with¦75915 him to Kedesh to their camp, and¦75923 they encamped there¦75925.
\v 74 About three thousand men¦75936 of the¦75929 foreigners fell on¦75931 that¦75934 day¦75933. Then¦75938 Yonatan returned to¦75939 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*.
\c 12
\s1 Yonatan renews alliances with Romai and Sparta
\p
\v 1 Yonatan saw that¦75946 the¦75947 time¦75948 was favourable for him, so he¦75949 chose men¦75953 and¦75954 sent¦75955 them to¦75955 Romai to¦75958 confirm and¦75959 renew the¦75961 friendship that they had with¦75962 them.
\v 2 He also¦75965 sent¦75971 similar letters to¦75966 the Spartans, and¦75968 to other¦75970 places¦75969.
\v 3 They went to Romai, entered¦75981 into the¦75983 senate house, and¦75985 said¦75986, “Yonatan the¦75988 high priest and¦75990 the¦75991 nation¦75992 of the¦75993 Yehudim have sent¦75995 us to¦75995 renew for them the¦75998 friendship and¦76001 the alliance, as in former time.”
\v 4 They gave¦76008 them letters to the men in every place¦76014, that¦76015 they should provide safe conduct for them on their way to the land¦76019 of Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add*.
\v 5 This¦76024 is the¦76025 copy of the¦76027 letters which¦76029 Yonatan wrote¦76030 to¦76030 the¦76032 Spartans:
\p
\v 6 “Yonatan the high priest¦76043, and¦76036 the¦76037 senate of the¦76039 nation¦76040, and¦76041 the¦76042 priests, and¦76044 the rest of the people¦76047 of the Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add*, to¦76053 their kindred the Spartans, greetings.
\v 7 Even before¦76055 this time letters were sent to¦76058 Honyo \add !(Onias)\add* the¦76060 high priest from¦76062 Arius,\f + \fr 12:7 \ft So the old Latin versions and Josephus: compare also ver. 20. All the other authorities read \fqa Darius \ft in this place.\f* who was reigning among¦76066 you¦76067, to signify that¦76068 you're¦76069 our kindred, as the¦76073 copy written below shows.
\v 8 Honyo welcomed honourably the¦76079 man¦76080 who¦76081 was sent and¦76084 received the¦76086 letters, wherein declaration was made of alliance and¦76093 friendship.
\v 9 Therefore¦76097 we also¦76095, even though we¦76096 need none of these things, having for our encouragement¦76101 the¦76105 holy¦76106 books which are in¦76108 our hands¦76110,
\v 10 have undertaken to¦76113 send¦76113 that¦76114 we might renew our brotherhood¦76117 and¦76118 friendship with you, to the¦76122 end that we shouldn't¦76123 become estranged from you¦76125 altogether; for¦76127 a long time¦76128 has passed¦76129 since you sent your letter to¦76133 us.
\v 11 We¦76135 therefore¦76136 at all¦76138 times¦76139 without ceasing, both in our feasts, and on the other convenient days¦76149, remember¦76165 you¦76151 in the sacrifices¦76155 which¦76153 we offer, and¦76156 in¦76157 our prayers¦76159, as it's¦76162 right¦76139 and¦76163 proper¦76164 to¦76165 be mindful of kindred.
\v 12 Moreover, we're glad for your glory¦76171.
\v 13 But¦76174 as for ourselves, many afflictions and¦76178 many wars¦76179 have encompassed us, and¦76181 the¦76184 kings¦76185 who are around¦76175 us have fought against us.
\v 14 We were unwilling to¦76193 be troublesome¦76193 to you¦76194, and¦76195 to the¦76196 rest of our allies and¦76199 friends¦76200, in¦76202 these wars;
\v 15 for¦76207 we have the¦76208 help which is from¦76209 heaven¦76210 to help¦76211 us, and¦76214 we've been delivered from¦76216 our enemies¦76218, and¦76220 our enemies¦76223 have been humbled.
\v 16 We chose therefore¦76226 Numenios the son of Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* and¦76229 Antipater the son of Yason, and¦76232 have sent¦76233 them to¦76233 the Romaios, to¦76234 renew the¦76237 friendship that we had with¦76238 them, and¦76241 the¦76243 former alliance.
\v 17 We commanded them therefore¦76246 to go also¦76248 to¦76249 you¦76250, and to salute you¦76254, and¦76255 to¦76256 deliver you¦76257 our letters about¦76262 the¦76263 renewing of friendship and¦76265 our brotherhood.
\v 18 And¦76269 now¦76270 you'll do well¦76271 if you give us a reply.”
\p
\v 19 And¦76277 this¦76278 is the¦76279 copy of the¦76281 letters which¦76283 they sent¦76284 to¦76284 Honyo \add !(Onias)\add*:
\p
\v 20 “Arius king¦76286 of the Spartans to Honyo the chief priest¦76289, greetings.
\v 21 It's been found¦76292 in¦76293 writing¦76294, about¦76295 the Spartans and the Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add*, that¦76301 they're¦76302 kindred, and¦76304 that¦76305 they're¦76306 of the descendants of Avraham.
\v 22 Now¦76311, since this¦76315 has come to our knowledge, you'll do well¦76316 to¦76317 write to us of your\f + \fr 12:22 \ft Grk. \fqa peace\f* prosperity¦76322.
\v 23 We¦76325 moreover write on our part to you¦76328, that¦76329 your livestock and¦76332 goods are¦76337 ours, and¦76338 ours are yours. We¦76340 do command therefore¦76344 that¦76345 they make report to you accordingly.”
\s1 Yonatan and Shim'on strengthen the country
\p
\v 24 Now Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* heard¦76351 that¦76353 Demetrios’ princes had returned to¦76365 fight¦76365 against him with a greater army than before¦76363,
\v 25 so¦76368 he marched away from¦76370 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, and¦76372 met them in the¦76376 country¦76378 of Hamat; for¦76380 he gave¦76381 them no¦76379 opportunity to¦76381 set foot in his country¦76387.
\v 26 He sent¦76390 spies¦76391 into his camp, and¦76396 they came again, and¦76398 reported to¦76399 him that¦76401 they were preparing to¦76405 attack them at night¦76408.
\v 27 But¦76410 as soon as the¦76412 sun¦76413 was down, Yonatan commanded his men to watch, and¦76420 to¦76421 be¦76421 armed, that¦76423 all¦76430 the¦76431 night¦76432 long they might be ready for battle¦76428. He stationed sentinels around the¦76437 camp.
\v 28 The¦76441 adversaries heard¦76440 that¦76443 Yonatan and his men were ready¦76444 for battle¦76451, and¦76452 they feared¦76453, and¦76454 trembled in their hearts¦76457, and¦76459 they kindled fires in¦76462 their camp then withdrew.
\v 29 But¦76467 Yonatan and¦76468 his men didn't know¦76473 it until¦76474 the morning; for¦76477 they saw¦76476 the¦76478 fires burning.
\v 30 Yonatan pursued after¦76484 them, but¦76486 didn't overtake them; for¦76491 they'd gone over the¦76492 river¦76494 Eleutherus.
\v 31 Then¦76495 Yonatan turned towards¦76498 the¦76499 Aravim, who¦76501 are called Zabadaeans, and¦76504 struck¦76505 them, and¦76507 took¦76508 their spoils.
\v 32 He came out from there, and¦76512 came to¦76514 Damesek \add !(Damascus)\add*, and¦76517 took his journey through all¦76520 the¦76521 country¦76522.
\p
\v 33 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* went¦76525 out¦76525, and¦76526 took his journey as far as Ashkelon, and¦76530 the¦76531 strongholds¦76533 that were near it. Then¦76534 he turned towards¦76536 Yafo \add !(Joppa)\add* and¦76538 took possession of it¦76540;
\v 34 for¦76542 he'd heard¦76541 that¦76543 they were planning to¦76547 hand¦76547 over the¦76548 stronghold¦76546 to¦76552 Demetrios’ men. He set a garrison there¦76553 to guard it¦76557.
\p
\v 35 Then¦76558 Yonatan returned and¦76561 called the¦76565 people's¦76566 elders¦76564 together. He¦76570 planned with¦76569 them to¦76572 build¦76572 strongholds in¦76574 Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add*,
\v 36 and¦76577 to make Yerushalem's \add !(Jerusalem)\add* walls¦76580 higher, and¦76582 to raise a great¦76585 mound between the¦76587 citadel and¦76589 the¦76590 city¦76591, to separate it¦76595 from the¦76596 city¦76597, that¦76598 so it might be¦76599 isolated, that¦76603 its garrison might neither buy nor sell.
\v 37 They were gathered together to¦76611 build¦76611 the¦76612 city¦76613. Part of¦76616 the¦76616 wall¦76617 of¦76618 the¦76618 brook¦76619 that's on the¦76620 east side fell down, and¦76623 he repaired the¦76625 section called¦76626 Kafenata.
\v 38 Shim'on also¦76628 built¦76630 Hadid in¦76633 the¦76634\f + \fr 12:38 \ft Grk. \fqa Sephela.\f* plain country, made it strong, and¦76636 set up gates and¦76639 bars.
\s1 Trufon captures Yonatan by deceit
\p
\v 39 And¦76641 Trufon¦76643 sought¦76642 to¦76644 reign¦76644 over Asia and¦76647 to crown himself, and¦76651 to stretch out his hand¦76653 against¦76654 Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* the¦76656 king¦76657.
\v 40 He was afraid¦76659 that Yonatan wouldn't allow him, and that he'd fight against him; and he sought¦76671 a way to¦76674 seize¦76674 him, that¦76675 he might destroy him. So he marched out and¦76680 came¦76682 to¦76682 Beyt-Shean.
\v 41 Yonatan came out¦76686 to meet¦76689 him with forty¦76692 thousand¦76693 men¦76694 chosen for battle, and¦76698 came to¦76699 Beyt-Shean.
\v 42 Trufon¦76704 saw that¦76705 he came with¦76708 a great army, and¦76711 he was afraid to stretch out his hand¦76713 against¦76714 him.
\v 43 He¦76719 received him honourably, and¦76721 commended him to all¦76724 his\f + \fr 12:43 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* friends¦76726, and¦76728 gave¦76729 him gifts¦76731, and¦76732 commanded¦76733 his forces to¦76737 be obedient¦76737 to him, as to himself¦76740.
\v 44 He said¦76742 to¦76742 Yonatan, “Why¦76745 have you put all¦76747 this¦76748 people to so¦76741 much trouble, seeing there's no war between us?
\v 45 Now¦76756 send¦76757 them away¦76799 to their homes¦76761, but¦76764 choose for yourself¦76765 a few men¦76766 who'll¦76768 be¦76769 with¦76770 you¦76771, and¦76772 come¦76773 with¦76774 me to Ptolemais, and¦76778 I'll give¦76779 it to¦76779 you¦76780, and¦76782 the rest of the strongholds and¦76786 the¦76787 rest of the¦76789 forces, and¦76791 all¦76792 the king's officers. Then¦76797 I'll turn¦76798 around and depart; for this is why I came.”
\p
\v 46 He put his trust in him, and did¦76807 even as¦76808 he said¦76809, and¦76810 sent¦76811 away¦76811 his forces, and¦76814 they departed into¦76815 the¦76812 land¦76817 of Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add*.
\v 47 But¦76820 he reserved to himself¦76822 three thousand men¦76823, of whom¦76829 he left¦76819 two thousand¦76831 in Galil, but¦76832 one thousand went with him.
\v 48 Now as soon as Yonatan entered¦76837 into Ptolemais, Ptolemais' people shut the¦76844 gates¦76845 and¦76846 seized¦76847 him. They killed¦76855 all¦76850 those who¦76851 came in¦76856 with him with the sword¦76857.
\p
\v 49 Trufon¦76860 sent¦76859 troops and¦76862 cavalry into Galil, and¦76867 into the¦76870 Great¦76871 Plain¦76869, to¦76873 destroy¦76873 all¦76874 Yonatan's men.
\v 50 They perceived that¦76880 he'd been seized and had perished, along with those who¦76886 were with¦76887 him. They encouraged one another and went¦76879 on their way close together, prepared¦76895 to fight¦76897.
\v 51 Those who¦76900 followed them saw that¦76902 they were¦76906 ready to fight for their lives, and turned¦76908 back again.
\v 52 They all¦76911 came¦76910 in peace¦76913 into the land¦76915 of Yehudah, and¦76917 they mourned for Yonatan and¦76921 those who were with¦76923 him, and¦76925 they were very¦76927 afraid¦76926. All Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* mourned with a great¦76933 mourning.
\v 53 And¦76934 all¦76936 the¦76937 Gentiles who¦76939 were around them sought¦76935 to¦76944 destroy them utterly; for¦76945 they said¦76944, “They have no¦76946 ruler¦76948 nor anyone to help them. Now¦76951 therefore¦76952 let's fight against them, and¦76955 take away their memory¦76960 from¦76957 among men.”
\c 13
\s1 Shim'on takes over the leadership
\p
\v 1 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* heard¦76963 that¦76965 Trufon¦76967 had gathered together a mighty army to¦76971 come¦76971 into the land¦76973 of Yehudah and¦76975 destroy it¦76978 utterly.
\v 2 He saw that¦76983 the¦76981 people¦76982 were¦76984 trembling¦76985 in great fear¦76987. So¦76988 he went up to¦76989 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* and¦76992 gathered the¦76994 people¦76995 together.
\v 3 He¦76998 encouraged them, and¦76999 said¦77000 to¦77003 them, “You yourselves know all the¦77007 things that I¦77009, my kindred, and¦77011 my father's¦77014 house¦77012 have done¦77016 for the¦77018 laws and¦77020 the¦77021 sanctuary¦77022, and¦77023 the¦77024 battles and¦77026 the¦77027 distresses which¦77029 we've seen.
\v 4 Because¦77032 of¦77032 this¦77034, all¦77037 my brothers¦77035 have perished for¦77038 Yisrael's sake, and¦77041 I'm¦77043 left alone¦77044.
\v 5 Now¦77046 be¦77049 it far from me, that I¦77051 should spare my own life in¦77054 any time¦77056 of affliction, for¦77059 I'm¦77064 not better than my kindred.
\v 6 However¦77065, I'll take vengeance for my nation¦77069, for the¦77073 sanctuary¦77074, and¦77075 for our wives and¦77079 children¦77081, because¦77091 all¦77085 the¦77086 Gentiles have gathered out of¦77091 hatred to destroy us.”
\p
\v 7 The¦77096 people's¦77097 spirit¦77095 revived as soon as they heard¦77100 these words¦77102.
\v 8 They answered¦77105 with a loud voice¦77106, saying, “You're¦77110 our leader in the¦77117 place of¦77117 Yehudah and Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* your brothers¦77118.
\v 9 Fight¦77122 our battles, and¦77124 we'll do all¦77125 that¦77121 you tell¦77128 us to¦77130 do¦77130.”
\p
\v 10 He gathered together all¦77133 the¦77134 men¦77135 of¦77140 war, and hurried to finish Yerushalem's \add !(Jerusalem)\add* walls¦77143. He fortified it all around¦77148.
\v 11 He sent¦77150 Yonatan the¦77152 son of¦77153 Avshalom \add !(Absalom)\add*, and¦77155 with¦77156 him a great army, to Yafo \add !(Joppa)\add*. He threw out those who¦77164 were¦77165 in¦77166 it¦77167, and¦77168 lived there¦77170.
\s1 Trufon demands a ransom for Yonatan
\p
\v 12 Trufon¦77175 left Ptolemais with¦77178 a mighty army to¦77181 enter¦77181 into the land¦77183 of Yehudah, and¦77185 Yonatan was with¦77187 him under guard.
\v 13 But¦77192 Shim'on encamped at Hadid, near the¦77198 plain.
\v 14 Trufon¦77202 knew that¦77203 Shim'on had risen¦77204 up in the¦77208 place of¦77208 his brother¦77209 Yonatan, and¦77211 meant to¦77215 join battle¦77216 with¦77219 him, so he¦77220 sent¦77218 ambassadors to¦77222 him, saying,
\v 15 “It's for money¦77224 which¦77225 Yonatan your brother¦77229 owed¦77226 to the king's treasury, because¦77234 of¦77234 the offices which¦77235 he¦77239 had, that we're detaining him.
\v 16 Now¦77241 send¦77242 one hundred¦77245 talents¦77244 of silver and¦77246 two¦77247 of his sons¦77249 for hostages, so that¦77252 when he's released he may not¦77253 revolt against us, and we'll¦77257 release him.”
\p
\v 17 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* knew¦77262 that¦77264 they spoke¦77266 to¦77267 him deceitfully¦77265, but he¦77268 sent¦77270 to¦77270 get¦77278 the¦77271 money¦77272 and¦77273 the¦77274 children, to avoid arousing great¦77279 hostility¦77277 among the¦77281 people¦77282,
\v 18 who might say¦77283, “Because¦77284 I didn't send¦77286 him the¦77288 money¦77289 and¦77290 the¦77291 children, he perished.”
\v 19 So¦77295 he sent¦77296 the¦77297 children and¦77299 the¦77300 hundred¦77301 talents¦77302, but¦77303 Trufon lied, and¦77305 didn't release¦77307 Yonatan.
\p
\v 20 After¦77311 this¦77312, Trufon¦77314 came to invade the land and¦77320 destroy it¦77322, and¦77323 he went around by the¦77326 way that leads to Adorayim. Shim'on and his army marched near him to every¦77338 place¦77339, wherever he went.
\v 21 Now the people of the citadel sent to Trufon ambassadors, urging him to¦77355 come¦77355 to them through¦77358 the¦77359 wilderness, and¦77361 to¦77362 send¦77362 them food¦77364.
\v 22 So¦77365 Trufon¦77367 prepared¦77366 all¦77368 his cavalry to¦77372 come¦77372, but on¦77373 that¦77376 night¦77375 a very¦77381 heavy snow fell, and¦77382 he didn't come¦77384 because¦77385 of¦77385 the¦77386 snow¦77387. He marched off and went¦77391 into the¦77393 land of Gilead.
\v 23 When¦77396 he came¦77397 near¦77397 to¦77400 Bascama, he killed¦77400 Yonatan, and¦77403 he was buried¦77404 there¦77405.
\v 24 Then¦77406 Trufon¦77408 turned¦77407 back, and¦77409 went¦77410 away¦77410 into his own land¦77413.
\s1 Shim'on buries Yonatan
\p
\v 25 Shim'on sent¦77416, and¦77418 took¦77419 the¦77420 bones of¦77423 Yonatan his brother¦77424, and¦77426 buried him at Modi'in, the city¦77431 of his fathers¦77433.
\v 26 All¦77438 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* made great¦77441 lamentation¦77440 over him, and¦77442 mourned for him many days¦77445.
\v 27 Shim'on built¦77448 a monument on¦77450 the¦77451 tomb¦77452 of¦77453 his father¦77454 and¦77456 his kindred, and¦77460 raised it¦77462 high so that¦77463 it could be seen, with polished stone¦77465 on the¦77468 front¦77473 and¦77470 back.
\v 28 He¦77477 also set up seven¦77478 pyramids, one near another, for his father¦77485, his mother, and his four¦77494 brothers¦77495.
\v 29 Because these, he¦77497 made¦77498 an elaborate setting, erecting great¦77502 pillars around them, and¦77503 on¦77505 the¦77506 pillars he made suits of armour for a perpetual memorial, and¦77512 beside the¦77514 suits of armour, he carved ships, so that¦77519 they could be seen by¦77521 all¦77522 who¦77523 sail¦77524 on the¦77525 sea¦77526.
\v 30 This¦77527 is the¦77528 tomb¦77529 which¦77530 he made¦77531 at Modi'in. It remains to¦77531 this¦77535 day¦77536.
\s1 Yisrael gains independence
\p
\v 31 Now Trufon¦77540 deceived¦77542 the¦77545 young King¦77546 Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* and¦77549 killed¦77550 him,
\v 32 and¦77552 reigned¦77553 in his place. He put on himself the¦77559 crown of Asia and¦77561 brought a great¦77564 calamity on¦77565 the¦77566 land¦77567.
\v 33 Shim'on built¦77569 up the strongholds of Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add*, and¦77575 walled them all around with high¦77578 towers, great walls, gates, and bars; and he stored food¦77588 in¦77589 the¦77590 strongholds.
\v 34 Shim'on chose men¦77595, and¦77596 sent¦77597 to¦77598 King¦77601 Demetrios with a request that he grant the¦77605 country¦77606 an immunity, because¦77607 all¦77608 that¦77609 Trufon did was¦77612 to¦77612 plunder.
\v 35 King¦77619 Demetrios sent¦77615 to him according¦77620 to¦77620 these words¦77622, and¦77624 answered¦77625 him, and¦77627 wrote¦77628 a letter to¦77628 him, as¦77631 follows:
\p
\v 36 “King¦77632 Demetrios to Shim'on the high priest and friend\f + \fr 13:36 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* of kings¦77638, and¦77639 to the elders¦77640 and¦77641 nation¦77642 of the Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add*, greetings.
\v 37 The¦77647 golden¦77648 crown¦77646 and¦77649 the¦77650 palm branch, which¦77652 you sent, we've received. We're ready¦77656 to make¦77659 a steadfast peace¦77661 with you, yes, and¦77663 to¦77664 write¦77664 to¦77666 our officers to¦77670 release¦77670 you¦77671 from tribute.
\v 38 Whatever things we confirmed to you¦77677, they're confirmed. The¦77680 strongholds, which¦77682 you've¦77685 built, let them be your own.
\v 39 As for any oversights and faults committed to this day¦77695, we forgive them, and¦77696 the¦77697 crown¦77698 tax which¦77699 you owed¦77700 us. If¦77702 there were any other tax collected in¦77706 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, let it be collected no longer.
\v 40 If¦77711 any among you're¦77714 qualified to¦77722 be enrolled in our court, let them be enrolled, and let there be peace¦77725 between us.”
\p
\v 41 In the one hundred seventieth year,\f + \fr 13:41 \ft circa B.C. 143.\f* the¦77731 yoke¦77732 of the¦77733 Gentiles was taken¦77730 away¦77735 from¦77735 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*.
\v 42 The¦77740 people¦77741 began to¦77743 write¦77743 in¦77744 their instruments and contracts, “In the first¦77750 year of Shim'on, the great¦77754 high priest and¦77755 captain and¦77757 leader of the Yehudim.”
\s1 Shim'on captures Gezer
\p
\v 43 In¦77760 those days¦77762 Shim'on encamped against¦77766\f + \fr 13:43 \ft See 1 Maccabees 13:53 (compare 1 Maccabees 13:48); 1 Maccabees 14:7, 34; 15:28; 16:1: also Josephus. All the authorities read \fqa Gaza \ft in this verse.\f* Gezer, and¦77768 surrounded it with troops. He made¦77773 a siege engine, and¦77772 brought it up to¦77773 the¦77777 city¦77778, and¦77779 struck¦77780 a tower¦77781, and¦77783 captured it.
\v 44 Those who¦77787 were in¦77788 the¦77789 engine leapt out into the¦77792 city¦77793; and¦77794 there was¦77795 a great¦77797 uproar in¦77798 the¦77799 city¦77800.
\v 45 The¦77803 people of the¦77805 city¦77806 tore their clothes¦77818, and¦77810 went up on the¦77814 walls¦77815 with their wives and children¦77812, and¦77820 cried with a loud voice¦77822, asking Shim'on to¦77828 give¦77828 them\f + \fr 13:45 \ft Grk. \fqa right hands.\f* his right¦77826 hand.
\v 46 They said¦77830, “Don't¦77831 deal with us according¦77834 to¦77834 our wickednesses, but¦77838 according¦77839 to¦77839 your mercy¦77841.”
\v 47 So Shim'on was reconciled to them, and didn't fight¦77849 against them; but he¦77850 expelled¦77852 them from¦77854 the¦77855 city¦77856 and¦77857 cleansed¦77858 the¦77859 houses where the¦77864 idols¦77865 were, and¦77866 then entered¦77868 into it¦77870 with singing and¦77872 giving praise¦77873.
\v 48 He removed all¦77878 uncleanness out¦77876 of it, and¦77880 placed in it men¦77883 who'd¦77884 keep the¦77885 law¦77886, and¦77888 made¦77887 it stronger than it was before, and¦77891 built¦77892 a dwelling place for himself¦77893 in¦77894 it¦77895.
\s1 The citadel in Yerushalem surrenders
\p
\v 49 But the people of the citadel in¦77902 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* were hindered from going out and¦77906 from going into the¦77909 country¦77910, and¦77911 from buying and¦77913 selling. So¦77915 they were very¦77917 hungry, and¦77918 a great number of them perished from¦77920 famine.
\v 50 Then¦77925 they cried out to¦77927 Shim'on, that he should give¦77932 them his right¦77929 hand; and¦77931 he gave it¦77933 to¦77935 them; but he¦77936 expelled¦77935 them from¦77937 there¦77937, and¦77938 he cleansed¦77939 the¦77940 citadel from¦77942 its pollutions.
\v 51 He entered¦77946 into it¦77948 on the¦77949 twenty-third day of¦77953 the¦77953 second¦77954 month, in the one¦77957 hundred and seventy-first year,\f + \fr 13:51 \ft circa B.C. 142.\f* with¦77962 praise¦77963 and palm branches, with harps, with cymbals, and with stringed instruments, with hymns¦77977, and¦77978 with songs¦77980, because¦77981 a great¦77984 enemy¦77983 had been destroyed out¦77985 of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*.
\v 52 Shim'on ordained that they should keep that day¦77994 every year¦77990 with¦77996 gladness¦77997. He made the¦78000 hill¦78001 of¦78002 the¦78002 temple¦78003 that was by the citadel stronger than before, and¦78008 he lived there with his men.
\v 53 Shim'on saw that¦78023 his son¦78021 Yohan \add !(John)\add* was a man¦78024, so¦78026 he¦78028 made him leader of all¦78032 his forces; and¦78033 he lived in¦78035 Gezer.
\c 14
\s1 Demetrios is captured
\p
\v 1 In¦78038 the one hundred and seventy-second year¦78039,\f + \fr 14:1 \ft circa B.C. 141.\f* King¦78048 Demetrios gathered his forces together, and¦78052 went into Maday \add !(Media)\add* to¦78053 get help¦78058, that¦78060 he might fight against Trufon.
\v 2 When¦78064 Arsakes, the¦78067 king¦78068 of Paras \add !(Persia)\add* and¦78071 Maday, heard¦78065 that¦78073 Demetrios had come¦78074 into his borders, he¦78079 sent¦78081 one¦78082 of his princes to take him alive¦78088.
\v 3 He went and struck¦78092 Demetrios' army, and¦78096 seized¦78097 him and¦78099 brought¦78100 him to Arsakes, who¦78093 put him under guard.
\s1 Peace and prosperity under Shim'on
\p
\v 4 The¦78111 land¦78112 had rest all¦78114 the¦78115 days¦78116 of Shim'on. He sought¦78119 the¦78121 good of his nation¦78122. His authority¦78128 and¦78130 his honour¦78132 was pleasing¦78125 to them all¦78134 his days¦78136.
\v 5 Amid all¦78139 his honours, he¦78142 took¦78143 Yafo \add !(Joppa)\add* for a harbour¦78147, and¦78148 made¦78149 it an entrance for the¦78151 islands of the¦78153 sea¦78154.
\v 6 He enlarged the borders of his nation¦78160 and¦78162 took possession of the¦78164 country¦78165.
\v 7 He gathered together a great number of captives¦78168, and took control of Gezer, Beyt-Tsur, and the¦78176 citadel, and¦78178 he removed its uncleannesses from¦78182 it¦78183. There was no¦78185 one who¦78187 resisted him.
\v 8 They tilled their land¦78194 in peace¦78197, and¦78198 the¦78199 land¦78200 gave¦78201 her increase, and¦78205 the trees of the plains gave their fruit¦78211.
\v 9 The old men sat in¦78214 the¦78215 streets; they all¦78218 conversed together about¦78219 good things. The¦78223 young¦78224 men¦78224 put on glorious¦78226 and¦78227 warlike clothing.
\v 10 He provided food¦78233 for the¦78230 cities¦78231 and¦78234 furnished them with means of defence, until¦78240 the¦78243 glory¦78246 of his name¦78244 was known to the¦78245 end¦78249 of the¦78250 earth¦78251.
\v 11 He made¦78252 peace¦78254 in the¦78256 land¦78257, and¦78258 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* rejoiced with great¦78262 joy.
\v 12 Each¦78265 man sat under¦78266 his vine¦78268 and¦78270 his fig¦78272 tree¦78272, and there was no¦78275 one to¦78276 make them afraid.
\v 13 No one was left in the land¦78287 who fought¦78283 against¦78285 them. The kings¦78290 were defeated in¦78292 those days¦78294.
\v 14 He strengthened all¦78298 those of¦78301 his people who were humble¦78300. He¦78303 searched out the¦78304 law¦78305, and¦78307 every¦78309 lawless and¦78311 wicked¦78312 person he took away.
\v 15 He glorified¦78315 the¦78313 sanctuary¦78314, and¦78316 added to the¦78318 vessels¦78319 of the¦78320 temple.
\s1 Romai and Sparta renew their friendship
\p
\v 16 It was heard¦78323 at Romai that¦78326 Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* was dead, and¦78329 even in Sparta, and¦78332 they were extremely grieved¦78333.
\v 17 But¦78336 as soon as they heard¦78337 that¦78338 his brother¦78341 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* was¦78343 made high priest in his place, and¦78347 ruled the¦78349 country¦78350 and¦78351 the¦78352 cities¦78353 in¦78355 it¦78356,
\v 18 they wrote¦78357 to him on brass tablets to renew with him the friendship and¦78367 the¦78368 alliance which¦78370 they'd confirmed with¦78372 his brothers¦78377 Yehudah \add !(Judas)\add* and¦78374 Yonatan.
\v 19 These were read before¦78381 the¦78382 congregation¦78383 at Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*.
\p
\v 20 This¦78387 is the¦78388 copy of the¦78390 letters which¦78392 the Spartans sent¦78393:
\p “The¦78394 rulers¦78397 and¦78398 the¦78399 city¦78400 of the Spartans, to Shim'on the high priest¦78402, to the¦78405 elders¦78406, the¦78408 priests¦78409, and¦78410 the rest of the people¦78413 of the¦78414 Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add*, our kindred, greetings.
\v 21 The¦78418 ambassadors who¦78420 were sent to¦78422 our people¦78424 reported to¦78426 us about¦78428 your glory¦78430 and¦78432 honour¦78433. We were glad for their coming,
\v 22 and¦78440 we registered the¦78442 things that were spoken by¦78443 them in¦78446 the¦78447 public records\f + \fr 14:22 \ft Grk. \fqa counsels of the people.\f* as follows: ‘Numenios son of Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add*, and Antipater son of Yason, the Yehudim’ ambassadors, came to us to renew the¦78463 friendship they had with¦78464 us.
\v 23 It pleased¦78468 the¦78469 people¦78470 to entertain the¦78472 men¦78473 honourably, and¦78475 to put the copy of their words¦78481 in¦78483 the public records,\f + \fr 14:23 \ft Grk. \fqa books that are appointed for the people.\f* to the end that the people of¦78489 the¦78489 Spartans might have¦78490 a record of them. Moreover they wrote a copy of these things to Shim'on the¦78502 high priest.’ ”
\p
\v 24 After¦78504 this¦78505, Shim'on sent¦78506 Numenios to¦78512 Romai with a great¦78515 shield of gold of weighing one thousand¦78518 minas,\f + \fr 14:24 \ft 1,000 minas is about 499 kg or 1,098 pounds.\f* in order to confirm the alliance with them.
\s1 The people honour Shim'on as their leader
\p
\v 25 But¦78527 when the¦78529 people heard¦78528 these things, they said¦78534, “How¦78526 can we thank Shim'on and¦78539 his sons¦78541?
\v 26 Because he and his brothers and his father's house have made themselves strong, and have fought and chased away Yisrael's \add !(Israel)\add* enemies, and confirmed liberty to Yisrael.”\f + \fr 14:26 \ft Grk. \fqa him.\f*
\v 27 So they wrote on tablets of brass, and set them on pillars on Mt. Tsiyon \add !(Zion)\add*. This is the copy of the writing:
\p “On the eighteenth day of Elul, in the one hundred and seventy-second year,\f + \fr 14:27 \ft circa B.C. 141.\f* which is the third year of Shim'on the high priest,
\v 28 in Asaramel, in a great¦78604 congregation of priests¦78605 and¦78606 people¦78607 and¦78608 princes of the nation¦78610, and¦78611 of the¦78612 elders¦78613 of the¦78614 country¦78615, it was proclaimed to¦78616 us:\f + \fr 14:28 \ft Grk. \fqa he made known.\f*
\v 29 ‘Since¦78618 wars¦78621 often¦78619 occurred in¦78622 the¦78623 country¦78624, Shim'on the¦78627 son¦78628 of Matityah \add !(Mattathias)\add*, the¦78630 son¦78631 of the¦78632 sons¦78633 of Yoyariv, and¦78635 his brothers¦78637, put themselves in jeopardy and¦78643 withstood the¦78645 enemies of¦78647 their nation¦78648, that¦78650 their sanctuary¦78653 and¦78655 the¦78656 law¦78657 might be established, and¦78658 glorified¦78661 their nation¦78663 with great¦78660 glory¦78659.
\v 30 Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add* rallied the¦78668 nation¦78669, became their high priest, and¦78671 was¦78672 gathered to his people¦78679.
\v 31 Their enemies¦78684 planned to invade their country¦78689, that¦78693 they might destroy their country¦78694 utterly, and¦78696 stretch out their hands¦78698 against¦78699 their sanctuary¦78701.
\v 32 Then¦78703 Shim'on rose up and¦78706 fought¦78707 for his nation¦78710. He¦78711 spent much¦78715 of his own money¦78714 to arm the valiant men¦78721 of¦78724 his nation¦78725 and¦78727 give¦78728 them wages.
\v 33 He fortified the¦78733 cities¦78734 of Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add* and¦78737 Beyt-Tsur that lies on¦78741 the borders of Yehudah, where the weapons¦78749 of the¦78750 enemies were had been stored, and¦78753 there¦78755 he placed¦78754 a garrison of Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add*.
\v 34 He fortified Yafo \add !(Joppa)\add* which is on¦78763 the¦78764 sea¦78765, and¦78766 Gezer which is on¦78770 the¦78771 borders of Azotos, where the¦78777 enemies used to¦78782 live, and¦78785 placed¦78793 Yehudim there, and set in there all things necessary¦78787 for their restoration.
\v 35 The¦78798 people¦78799 saw Shim'on's faith,\f + \fr 14:35 \ft Some authorities read \fqa acts.\f* and¦78804 the¦78805 glory¦78806 which¦78807 he resolved to bring to his nation, and they made him their leader and high priest, because¦78820 he'd¦78822 done¦78823 all¦78824 these things, and¦78826 for the¦78827 justice and¦78829 the¦78830 faith¦78831 which¦78832 he kept to his nation, and because he sought¦78838 by all¦78839 means to exalt his people¦78843.
\v 36 In¦78846 his days¦78848, things prospered in¦78851 his hands¦78853, so that the Gentiles were taken away out¦78859 of their country¦78861, and¦78863 they also who were in¦78865 the¦78866 city¦78867 of David, those who¦78869 were in¦78870 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, who'd¦78872 made¦78873 themselves a citadel, out¦78876 of which¦78877 they used to¦78878 go¦78878, and¦78879 polluted everything around the¦78882 sanctuary¦78883, and¦78884 did¦78885 great¦78887 damage to its purity¦78890.
\v 37 He placed Yehudim in¦78893 it¦78894 and¦78897 fortified it¦78899 for the safety¦78901 of the¦78902 country¦78903 and¦78904 the¦78905 city¦78906, and¦78907 made high Yerushalem's walls¦78910.
\v 38 King¦78914 Demetrios confirmed to¦78916 him the¦78918 high priesthood according¦78920 to¦78920 these things,
\v 39 and¦78922 made¦78923 him one of his friends¦78926,\f + \fr 14:39 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* and¦78928 honoured him with great¦78932 honour;
\v 40 for¦78934 he'd heard¦78933 that¦78935 the¦78937 Yehudim had been called by¦78939 the Romaios friends¦78941, allies, and kindred, and that¦78947 they'd met¦78948 the¦78949 ambassadors of Shim'on honourably;
\v 41 and¦78953 that¦78954 the¦78956 Yehudim and¦78958 the¦78959 priests were well pleased¦78955 that Shim'on should be¦78962 their leader and¦78965 high priest¦78960 forever, until¦78970 there should arise¦78972 a faithful¦78974 prophet¦78973;
\v 42 and¦78975 that he should be¦78977 governor over them, and¦78981 should take charge of the¦78986 sanctuary¦78987, to¦78990 set them over their works¦78992, and¦78994 over the¦78996 country¦78997, and¦78998 over the¦79000 weapons¦79001, and¦79002 over the¦79004 strongholds¦79005; and that he should take charge of the sanctuary,
\v 43 and¦79006 that¦79007 he¦79009 should be obeyed by¦79016 all¦79017, and¦79018 that¦79019 all¦79025 contracts in¦79027 the¦79028 country¦79029 should be written in his name¦79023, and¦79030 that¦79031 he should be clothed¦79032 in purple¦79033, and¦79034 wear gold;
\v 44 and¦79036 that it shouldn't be lawful for any of¦79040 the¦79040 people¦79041 or of the¦79043 priests¦79044 to¦79045 nullify any of these things, or to¦79049 oppose the¦79050 words that he¦79052 should speak, or to gather an assembly in¦79057 the¦79058 country¦79059 without¦79060 him, or to be clothed in purple¦79064, or wear a buckle of gold¦79068;
\v 45 but¦79070 anyone¦79077 who should do¦79074 otherwise, or¦79075 nullify any of these things, he'll¦79078 be liable¦79079 to¦79080 punishment.’ ”
\v 46 All¦79083 the¦79084 people¦79085 consented to¦79089 ordain for Shim'on that he should do¦79089 according¦79090 to¦79090 these words¦79092.
\v 47 So¦79094 Shim'on accepted this, and¦79097 consented to¦79098 be high priest¦79108, and¦79100 to¦79101 be¦79101 captain¦79102 and¦79103 governor¦79104\f + \fr 14:47 \ft Grk. \fqa ethnarch.\f* of the¦79105 Yehudim and¦79107 of the priests, and¦79109 to be protector of¦79110 all¦79112.
\p
\v 48 They commanded to put this¦79114 writing¦79115 on¦79119 tablets of brass, and¦79122 to¦79123 set them up within the precinct of the sanctuary¦79128 in¦79129 a conspicuous place¦79130,
\v 49 and¦79133 moreover to put copies of them in¦79137 the¦79138 treasury¦79139, so that¦79140 Shim'on and¦79143 his sons¦79145 might have them.
\c 15
\s1 Antiokos seeks Shim'on's support
\p
\v 1 Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* son¦79151 of¦79153 Demetrios the¦79153 king¦79154 sent¦79148 a letter from¦79156 the¦79157 islands of the¦79159 sea¦79160 to Shim'on the priest¦79162 and¦79163\f + \fr 15:1 \ft Grk. \fqa ethnarch.\f* governor of the¦79165 Yehudim, and¦79167 to all¦79168 the¦79169 nation¦79170.
\v 2 Its contents follow:
\p “King¦79177 Antiokos to¦79172 Shim'on the¦79174 chief priest¦79180 and¦79182\f + \fr 15:2 \ft Grk. \fqa ethnarch.\f* governor, and¦79184 to the nation¦79185 of the Yehudim, greetings.
\v 3 Whereas certain troublemakers have made themselves masters of the¦79192 kingdom¦79193 of our fathers¦79195, but my purpose is to claim the¦79200 kingdom¦79201, that¦79202 I may restore it as it was¦79206 before¦79207; and¦79209 moreover I've raised a multitude¦79210 of foreign soldiers, and¦79212 have prepared warships;
\v 4 moreover I plan¦79216 to¦79219 land in the¦79220 country¦79221, that¦79222 I may punish those who've destroyed our country¦79227, and¦79229 those who've¦79230 made many cities¦79232 in¦79234 the¦79235 kingdom¦79236 desolate;
\v 5 now¦79237 therefore¦79238 I confirm to¦79239 you¦79240 all¦79241 the¦79242 tax remissions which¦79244 the¦79247 kings¦79250 who were before¦79248 me remitted to you, and¦79251 whatever gifts¦79254 besides they remitted to¦79255 you¦79256,
\v 6 and¦79257 I permit you¦79259 to¦79260 coin¦79263 money for your country¦79265 with your own¦79262 stamp,
\v 7 but¦79268 that Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* and¦79269 the¦79270 sanctuary¦79271 should be¦79272 free¦79273. All¦79275 the¦79276 weapons¦79277 that you've prepared, and¦79280 the¦79281 strongholds that you've built, which¦79285 you¦79288 have in your possession, let them remain yours.
\v 8 Every¦79290 debt¦79291 owed to the king, and¦79293 the things that'll be owed to the king from¦79297 now¦79299 on and¦79300 forever, let them be remitted to you¦79306.
\v 9 Moreover, when¦79308 we've established our kingdom¦79312, we'll¦79313 glorify you¦79315 and¦79316 your nation¦79318 and¦79320 the¦79321 temple¦79322 with great¦79324 glory, so¦79325 that¦79328 your glory¦79329 will be made manifest in¦79331 all¦79332 the¦79333 earth¦79334.
\p
\v 10 In the one hundred and seventy-fourth year,\f + \fr 15:10 \ft circa B.C. 139\f* Antiokos went¦79341 into the¦79344 land¦79345 of his fathers¦79346; and¦79348 all¦79352 the¦79353 forces came together to him, so¦79355 that there¦79347 were¦79357 few men with¦79360 Trufon.
\v 11 King¦79367 Antiokos pursued¦79363 him, and he came¦79369, as he fled, to¦79374 Dor, which is by the¦79375 sea¦79376;
\v 12 for¦79378 he knew that¦79379 troubles had come on¦79381 him all at once, and¦79385 that¦79388 his forces had deserted him.
\v 13 Antiokos encamped against¦79393 Dor, and¦79395 with¦79396 him one hundred and twenty thousand men¦79400 of war and¦79402 eight thousand cavalry.
\v 14 He surrounded the¦79407 city¦79408, and¦79409 the ships joined in the attack from¦79412 the sea¦79413. He harassed the¦79417 city¦79418 by land¦79421 and¦79422 sea¦79424, and¦79425 permitted no¦79426 one to go¦79429 out or in.
\s1 Romai confirms its support for the Yehudim
\p
\v 15 Numenios and¦79432 his company came¦79433 from Romai, having letters to¦79441 the¦79443 kings¦79444 and¦79445 to the¦79446 countries¦79447, in¦79448 which¦79449 were written these things:
\p
\v 16 “Lukios, consul of the Romaios, to King¦79456 Ptolemaios \add !(Ptolemy)\add*, greetings.
\v 17 The Yehudim’ \add !(Jews)\add* ambassadors came¦79462 to¦79463 us as our friends¦79465 and¦79467 allies, to renew the¦79470 old friendship and¦79474 alliance, being sent¦79476 from¦79477 Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* the¦79479 high priest, and¦79481 from the people of the Yehudim.
\v 18 Moreover they brought a shield of gold¦79489 weighing one thousand¦79492 minas.\f + \fr 15:18 \ft 1,000 minas is about 499 kg. or about 1,098 pounds.\f*
\v 19 It pleased¦79493 us therefore¦79494 to¦79496 write¦79496 to the¦79497 kings¦79498 and¦79499 to the¦79500 countries¦79501, that¦79502 they shouldn't¦79503 seek¦79504 their harm¦79506 or fight against them, their cities¦79513, and¦79515 their country¦79517, or be allies with those who¦79523 fight against them.
\v 20 Moreover, it seemed good to¦79526 us to¦79529 receive¦79529 the¦79530 shield from¦79532 them.
\v 21 If¦79534 therefore¦79536 any troublemakers have fled from¦79539 their country¦79541 to¦79543 you¦79544, deliver them to Shim'on the¦79548 high priest, that¦79550 he may take vengeance on¦79552 them according¦79554 to¦79554 their law¦79556.”
\p
\v 22 He¦79560 wrote¦79561 the¦79563 same things to King¦79564 Demetrios, to Atalos, to Ariarathes, to Arsakes,
\v 23 to all¦79572 the¦79573 countries¦79574, to\f + \fr 15:23 \ft Some authorities read \fqa Sampsaces: \ft the Latin versions have \fqa Lampsacus.\f* Sampsames, to the Spartans, to Delos, to Mundos, to Sikuon, to Karia, to Samos, to Pamfulia, to Lukia, to Halikarnasos, to Rodos, to Faselis, to Kos, to Side, to Arvad, Gortuna, Knidos, Kupros \add !(Cyprus)\add*, and Kurainai \add !(Cyrene)\add*.
\v 24 They also¦79631 wrote¦79634 this¦79630 copy to¦79634 Shim'on the¦79636 high priest.
\s1 Antiokos turns against Shim'on
\p
\v 25 But¦79639 King¦79641 Antiokos \add !(Antiochus)\add* encamped against¦79643 Dor the¦79646 second¦79647 day, bringing his forces up to it¦79650 continually¦79649, and¦79653 making¦79655 engines of¦79660 war; and¦79663 he shut up Trufon from going in or out.
\v 26 Shim'on sent¦79666 him two thousand chosen men¦79670 to fight on his side, with silver, gold¦79677, and¦79678 instruments of war in abundance.
\v 27 He¦79684 wouldn't receive¦79685 them, but¦79686 nullified all¦79688 the covenants which he'd¦79691 made with him before, and¦79693 was estranged from him.
\v 28 He sent¦79697 to¦79698 him Athenobios, one¦79701 of his friends¦79703,\f + \fr 15:28 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* to¦79707 confer with him, saying, “You¦79708 hold possession of Yafo \add !(Joppa)\add*, Gezer, and the¦79715 citadel that's¦79717 in¦79718 Yerushalem, cities¦79720 of my kingdom¦79722.
\v 29 You've devastated their territory¦79725, and¦79728 done¦79729 great¦79731 harm in the¦79733 land¦79734, and¦79735 control of many places¦79737 in¦79739 my kingdom¦79741.
\v 30 Now¦79743 therefore¦79744 hand over the¦79746 cities¦79747 which¦79748 you've taken, and¦79750 the¦79751 tributes of the¦79753 places¦79754 which¦79755 you've taken control of outside¦79757 of the borders of Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add*;
\v 31 or else give¦79765 me for them five¦79768 hundred¦79768 talents¦79769 of silver; and¦79771 for the¦79772 harm that¦79774 you've done, and¦79776 the¦79777 tributes of the¦79779 cities¦79780, another¦79781 five¦79783 hundred¦79783 talents. Otherwise we'll come¦79787 and subdue you¦79789.”
\p
\v 32 Athenobios, the¦79794 king's¦79795 friend¦79793,\f + \fr 15:32 \ft See 1 Maccabees 2:18.\f* came¦79791 to¦79799 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*. When he saw the¦79800 glory¦79801 of Shim'on, the cupboard of gold and silver vessels, and his great attendance, he was amazed¦79813. He reported to him the¦79819 king's¦79820 words¦79818.
\v 33 Shim'on answered¦79822, and¦79821 said¦79824 to him, “We haven't taken other men's land¦79827 nor do we have possession of that which belongs to others, but¦79833 of the¦79834 inheritance¦79835 of our fathers¦79837. However, it'd been in¦79843 possession of our enemies¦79841 wrongfully for a while.
\v 34 But¦79849 we, having¦79851 opportunity, firmly hold the¦79853 inheritance¦79854 of our fathers¦79856.
\v 35 As for Yafo and Gezer, which¦79863 you demand, they did¦79866 great¦79871 harm among¦79867 the¦79868 people¦79869 throughout our country¦79874. We'll¦79875 give¦79877 one hundred¦79879 talents¦79878 for them.”
\p Athenobios didn't answer even one word,
\v 36 but¦79887 returned in a rage to¦79890 the¦79891 king¦79892, and¦79893 reported to¦79894 him these words¦79897, and¦79899 Shim'on's glory¦79901, and¦79903 all¦79904 that he'd seen; and¦79907 the¦79909 king¦79910 was extremely angry¦79908.
\v 37 Meanwhile, Trufon¦79913 embarked on board a ship, and¦79914 fled¦79918 to Orthosia.
\s1 Kendebaios attacks Yehudah
\p
\v 38 The¦79923 king¦79924 appointed¦79922 Kendebaios chief captain of the sea coast, and¦79930 gave¦79935 him troops of infantry and¦79933 cavalry.
\v 39 He¦79939 commanded him to¦79941 encamp against Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add*, and¦79945 he¦79947 commanded him to¦79948 build¦79948 up Kidron¦79950, and¦79951 to fortify the¦79953 gates¦79954, and¦79955 that¦79956 he should fight against the¦79958 people¦79959; but the king¦79962 pursued¦79963 Trufon.
\v 40 So¦79966 Kendebaios¦79968 came to Yavneh and¦79971 began to provoke the people¦79976, and¦79977 to invade Yehudah, and¦79982 to take the¦79984 people¦79985 captive and¦79986 kill them.
\v 41 He built¦79989 Kidron¦79991 and stationed cavalry and infantry there¦79994, to¦79999 the¦80001 end that¦79998 going out they might make raids on the¦80003 highways of Yehudah, as¦80005 the¦80008 king¦80009 had commanded him.
\c 16
\s1 Shim'on's sons defeat Kendebaios
\p
\v 1 Yohan \add !(John)\add* went up from¦80013 Gezer and¦80015 told Shim'on his father¦80019 what Kendebaios¦80023 was doing.
\v 2 Shim'on called¦80025 his two¦80028 oldest sons¦80029, Yehudah and¦80034 Yohan, and¦80036 said¦80037 to¦80037 them, “I¦80039 and¦80040 my brothers¦80042 and¦80044 my father's¦80048 house¦80046 have fought the battles of¦80047 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* from¦80054 our youth¦80055, even to this¦80057 day¦80059; and¦80060 things have prospered in¦80062 our hands¦80064, that we've¦80065 often delivered Yisrael.
\v 3 But now¦80070 I'm old, and you¦80074 moreover, by his mercy¦80078, are of a sufficient¦80079 age. Take the¦80082 place of me and my¦80086 brother¦80089, and¦80091 go¦80092 out¦80092 and fight for¦80094 our nation¦80096; and¦80099 let the¦80101 help¦80103 which is from heaven¦80102 be¦80104 with¦80105 you¦80106.
\p
\v 4 He chose out¦80109 of the¦80110 country¦80111 twenty¦80112 thousand men¦80114 of war and¦80116 cavalry, and¦80118 they went against¦80120 Kendebaios, and¦80123 slept¦80124 at Modi'in.
\v 5 Rising up in the morning, they went into the¦80132 plain¦80133, and a great army of infantry and cavalry came to¦80145 meet them. There was¦80145 a brook between them.
\v 6 He¦80153 encamped near them, he¦80154 and¦80155 his people¦80157. He¦80158 saw that the¦80161 people¦80162 were afraid to pass over the¦80165 brook, and¦80167 he passed over first¦80169. When¦80170 the¦80173 men¦80174 saw him, they passed over after¦80177 him.
\v 7 He divided the¦80181 people¦80182, and¦80183 placed the¦80184 cavalry in¦80186 the¦80188 middle¦80187 of the¦80190 infantry; but¦80191 the¦80193 enemies’ cavalry were very¦80196 many.
\v 8 They sounded the¦80199 trumpets; and¦80202 Kendebaios¦80204 and¦80205 his army were put to flight, and¦80209 many of them fell wounded to¦80210 death, but those who were left fled¦80218 to¦80218 the¦80220 stronghold¦80221.
\v 9 At that¦80225 time Yehudah, Yohan's brother¦80226, was wounded; but¦80229 Yohan pursued after them until¦80232 he came¦80233 to¦80233 Kidron¦80235, which¦80236 Kendebaios had built¦80237.
\v 10 They fled¦80239 to¦80239 the¦80242 towers that¦80244 are in¦80245 Azotos' fields; and¦80249 he¦80251 burnt it¦80257 with fire¦80253. About two thousand men¦80259 of them fell. Then¦80261 he returned into Yehudah in peace¦80267.
\s1 Shim'on and two of his sons are murdered
\p
\v 11 Ptolemaios¦80269 \add !(Ptolemy)\add* the¦80270 son of¦80271 Abubus had been¦80273 appointed governor over the¦80277 plain¦80278 of Yeriho \add !(Jericho)\add*, and¦80280 he had¦80281 much¦80285 silver and¦80283 gold¦80284;
\v 12 for¦80287 he was¦80286 the¦80289 high priest's son-in-law.
\v 13 His heart¦80294 was lifted up¦80310, and he planned to make himself master of the¦80299 country¦80300, and¦80301 he made deceitful¦80303 plans against Shim'on \add !(Simon)\add* and¦80306 his sons¦80308, to do away with them.
\v 14 Now Shim'on was¦80314 visiting the¦80316 cities¦80317 that¦80318 were in¦80319 the¦80320 country¦80321, and attending to their needs. He went¦80328 down¦80328 to Yeriho—himself with Matityah \add !(Mattathias)\add* and Yehudah his sons¦80337—in the one hundred and seventy-seventh year,\f + \fr 16:14 \ft circa B.C. 136.\f* in¦80345 the eleventh month¦80346, which is the¦80349 month¦80350 Shevat.
\v 15 The¦80355 son of¦80356 Abubus received¦80353 them deceitfully¦80365 into the little¦80360 stronghold that's¦80361 called¦80362 Dok¦80363, which¦80366 he'd built¦80367, and¦80368 made¦80369 them a great¦80372 banquet, and¦80373 hid men¦80376 there¦80375.
\v 16 When¦80378 Shim'on and¦80381 his sons¦80383 had drunk freely, Ptolemaios¦80386 and his men rose up, took their weapons¦80394, rushed in against Shim'on in the banqueting place, and¦80403 killed¦80404 him, his two¦80408 sons¦80409, and¦80411 some of his servants.
\v 17 He committed a great¦80419 iniquity, and¦80420 repaid evil for¦80423 good.
\p
\v 18 Ptolemaios¦80428 wrote¦80426 these things and¦80429 sent to¦80430 the¦80431 king¦80432, that¦80433 he should send him forces to aid him, and should deliver¦80440 him their country¦80443 and¦80445 the¦80446 cities¦80447.
\v 19 He sent¦80449 others¦80450 to Gezer to do away with Yohan. To the captains of thousands, he sent letters to come to him, that¦80464 he might give¦80465 them silver, gold¦80469, and¦80470 gifts¦80471.
\v 20 He sent¦80474 others to¦80475 take possession of¦80481 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* and the¦80481 temple¦80482 hill¦80480.
\v 21 One¦80485 ran before to¦80486 Gezer, and told Yohan that¦80490 his father¦80493 and kindred had perished, and he's sent¦80501 to¦80504 kill¦80504 you also.
\v 22 When¦80505 he heard¦80506, he was greatly shocked. He seized¦80510 the¦80511 men¦80512 who¦80513 came¦80514 to¦80515 destroy¦80515 him and¦80517 killed¦80518 them; for¦80521 he perceived that¦80522 they were seeking¦80523 to¦80525 destroy¦80525 him.
\p
\v 23 And¦80526 the¦80527 rest of the¦80529 acts of Yohan \add !(John)\add* and¦80532 of his wars¦80534 and¦80536 of his valiant actions, and¦80542 of the walls which¦80547 he built¦80548, and¦80549 of his achievements,
\v 24 look¦80553, they're written¦80555 in the records\f + \fr 16:24 \ft Grk. \fqa book of days.\f* of his high priesthood, from¦80561 the time¦80558 that¦80562 he was¦80563 made high priest after¦80565 his father¦80567.
